window.COURSE = {"generated":"2026-10-19T11:42:55.004Z","version":"1.0.0","chapters":[{"id":"ch1","num":1,"color":"#bc4a24","colorDark":"#e0714a","icon":"01","sections":["1.1","1.2","1.3","1.4","1.5"],"zh":{"title":"数据","short":"数据","blurb":"从数据到视觉编码：DIKW、Stevens 测量尺度、Mackinlay 视觉通道，以及 D3 的数据加载、变换与选择器。","lead":"先回答「数据是什么、属于哪种尺度」，再决定「用哪个视觉通道」。本章是后面所有图表的语法基础。","outcome":"能把一张 CSV 正确加载为带类型的对象，并为属性选对比例尺与颜色映射。"},"en":{"title":"Data","short":"Data","blurb":"From data to visual encoding: DIKW, Stevens' measurement scales, Mackinlay's channels, plus D3 loading, transformation, and selections.","lead":"First answer what the data is and which scale it belongs to; then choose the visual channel. This chapter is the grammar behind every later chart.","outcome":"Load a CSV into typed objects correctly, and choose the right scale and color mapping for each attribute."},"minutes":45,"chars":6045},{"id":"ch2","num":2,"color":"#2f6f62","colorDark":"#5aa596","icon":"02","sections":["2.1","2.2","2.3","2.4"],"zh":{"title":"数据可视化流程","short":"可视化流程","blurb":"把「一张表」变成「一张图」：Card 数据流、Mackinlay 自动决策、van Wijk 反馈环，以及 rollup、树布局、事件与动画。","lead":"可视化不是「画图」，而是一条从原始数据到视图、再回到用户的闭环。本章沿着这条链走一遍。","outcome":"能说清每一步在做什么，并能用 d3.rollup、tree、事件委托和 transition 把链路实现出来。"},"en":{"title":"The Visualization Pipeline","short":"Pipeline","blurb":"Turn a table into a view: Card's data flow, Mackinlay's automatic decisions, van Wijk's feedback loop, plus rollup, tree layout, events, and animation.","lead":"Visualization is not drawing; it is a loop from raw data to views and back to the user. This chapter walks the whole chain.","outcome":"Explain what each stage does, and implement the chain with d3.rollup, tree, event delegation, and transitions."},"minutes":40,"chars":6868},{"id":"ch3","num":3,"color":"#a97b2f","colorDark":"#d3a24d","icon":"03","sections":["3.1","3.2","3.3","3.4","3.5","3.6","3.7","3.8"],"zh":{"title":"色彩专题","short":"色彩","blurb":"颜色是数据通道：四种颜色空间、三类 colormap、CIE Lab 色域、五种配色规则、经典科研配色与色觉缺陷模拟。","lead":"同一组数据，换一套颜色就可能改变结论。本章把「好看」拆成可检查的规则。","outcome":"能为数据类型选对 colormap，并用 CVD 模拟和灰度检查验证配色。"},"en":{"title":"Color","short":"Color","blurb":"Color is a data channel: four color spaces, three colormap types, CIE Lab gamut, five palette rules, classic scientific palettes, and CVD simulation.","lead":"The same data with a different palette can change the conclusion. This chapter turns taste into checkable rules.","outcome":"Choose the right colormap for the data type and validate it with CVD simulation and a grayscale check."},"minutes":66,"chars":4262},{"id":"ch4","num":4,"color":"#33566f","colorDark":"#6f9ab8","icon":"04","sections":["4.1","4.2","4.3","4.4","4.5"],"zh":{"title":"低维数据可视化","short":"低维数据","blurb":"坐标、比例尺、曲线、45° 倾角与等值线：低维数据最常见的五种画法，以及它们各自容易踩的坑。","lead":"一两个属性也能画出很多花样，但每一种都对应一个明确的感知问题。","outcome":"能在宽/长格式间转换，选对比例尺与曲线，并用 Marching Squares 提取等值线。"},"en":{"title":"Low-Dimensional Data","short":"Low-Dim","blurb":"Coordinates, scales, curves, the 45° angle, and contours: five common ways to draw low-dimensional data, and the pitfalls of each.","lead":"One or two attributes can be drawn many ways, but each way answers a specific perceptual question.","outcome":"Reshape wide/long tables, choose scales and curves, and extract contours with Marching Squares."},"minutes":43,"chars":3101},{"id":"ch5","num":5,"color":"#6b4a63","colorDark":"#b081a6","icon":"05","sections":["5.1","5.2","5.3","5.4","5.5"],"zh":{"title":"时序数据可视化","short":"时序数据","blurb":"趋势、周期与叙事：五个时间属性，以及折线图、日历热图、阿基米德螺旋、Storyline 四种画法。","lead":"时间既是连续的，也是循环的。选错时间域，周期就会被画成噪声。","outcome":"能根据「想看趋势、周期还是叙事」选择正确的时间可视化形式。"},"en":{"title":"Time Series","short":"Time","blurb":"Trend, cycle, and narrative: five temporal properties, plus line charts, calendar heatmaps, Archimedean spirals, and Storyline.","lead":"Time is both continuous and cyclic. Choose the wrong time domain and cycles turn into noise.","outcome":"Pick the right temporal form depending on whether you want trend, cycle, or narrative."},"minutes":42,"chars":2913}],"sections":{"1.1":{"id":"1.1","num":"1.1","chapter":"ch1","demo":"datagen","minutes":9,"related":["1.3","1.4"],"zh":{"title":"数据生成","rawTitle":"数据生成","short":"数据生成","subtitle":"把 CSV 变成可计算的 JS 对象：字段映射、类型转换与异步加载。","bigIdea":"数据进入可视化的第一步不是画图，而是把「字符串表」变成「带类型的对象」。","points":["中文列名负责可读，英文变量负责可维护；中间用 COLUMN_MAP 做桥。","一元 + 与 trim() 完成最常见的类型清洗；日期要用 d3.timeParse 兜底。","d3.csv 的 row 回调逐行执行，加载与转换一次完成，省去二次遍历。"],"quiz":{"q":"要在读取 CSV 的同时完成类型转换，最合适的写法是？","options":["先 await d3.csv(url)，再对结果 .map(transform)","d3.csv(url, transformRow)，把转换函数作为第二个参数","用 fetch 拿到文本，再用正则替换字段"],"answer":1,"why":"row 回调在每一行解析后立即执行，加载与转换一次完成；先读后 map 也可行，但多一次遍历与一份中间数组。"},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">你的原案例</span></h3>\n<p>本章采用中国石油大学（华东）2025 级新生数据。数据由 DeepSeek 大模型合成，含 80 条记录：</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"text\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">Text</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code>序号、姓名、性别、生日、年龄、班级、籍贯、民族</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-1-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">理论</span><span class=\"blk__text\">AI 合成数据的可信度边界</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>维度</th>\n<th>含义</th>\n<th>DeepSeek 生成数据</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>准确性</td>\n<td>反映真实世界的程度</td>\n<td>⚠️ 姓名/籍贯虚构</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>完整性</td>\n<td>必填字段是否齐全</td>\n<td>✅ 字段齐全</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>一致性</td>\n<td>同一概念在不同地方表达一致</td>\n<td>✅ 字段一致</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>时效性</td>\n<td>数据反映当前状态</td>\n<td>✅ 入学年份匹配</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>AI 合成数据的&quot;采样偏差&quot;</strong>：模型倾向&quot;看起来合理&quot;的分布（民族偏汉族、籍贯偏大城市）。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-1-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① 字段名映射</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：字段映射 —— 把中文 CSV 列名转英文 JS 变量\nconst COLUMN_MAP = {\n  &quot;序号&quot;: &quot;id&quot;,\n  &quot;姓名&quot;: &quot;name&quot;,\n  &quot;性别&quot;: &quot;gender&quot;,\n  &quot;生日&quot;: &quot;birthday&quot;,\n  &quot;年龄&quot;: &quot;age&quot;,\n  &quot;班级&quot;: &quot;class&quot;,\n};</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>为什么不用中文 key？</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>JS 引擎对中文标识符的容错性差（老浏览器报错）</li>\n<li>后端、JSON、URL 编码都可能引入乱码</li>\n<li>IDE 自动补全、搜索、重构工具对中文支持不一致</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>最佳实践</strong>：CSV 用人可读的中文名，JS 内部统一英文变量。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-1-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② 类型转换函数</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：类型转换 —— 用户原文「推荐方式」\nfunction transformRow(d) {\n  return {\n    id:       +d[&quot;序号&quot;],              // 一元 + 把字符串转 Number\n    name:     d[&quot;姓名&quot;].trim(),       // trim() 去掉首尾空白\n    birthday: new Date(d[&quot;生日&quot;]),   // 字符串 → Date 对象\n    age:      +d[&quot;年龄&quot;],\n    class:    d[&quot;班级&quot;].trim(),\n  };\n}</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>+d[&quot;年龄&quot;]</code> 是一元加运算符，是 JS 里把字符串转数字的最快写法</li>\n<li><code>new Date(str)</code> 解析 ISO 格式日期，对 <code>&quot;2007/8/15&quot;</code> 兼容性差，要用 <code>d3.timeParse(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;)</code> 兜底</li>\n<li><strong>坑</strong>：没有 <code>trim()</code> 的话，&quot;软件工程1班 &quot; 里的空格会让后续过滤/聚合出错</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-1-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">③ d3.csv 第二参直接传 row 回调</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ③：一行完成加载 + 转换\nconst data = await d3.csv(&quot;data/newstudent.csv&quot;, transformRow);\n\n// 验证类型确实转换了：\nconsole.log(typeof data[0].age);              // &quot;number&quot;\nconsole.log(data[0].birthday instanceof Date); // true</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>为什么这一行很重要</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>d3.csv</code> 是异步函数，必须 <code>await</code></li>\n<li>第二参的 row 回调会在<strong>每一行解析后立即调用</strong>——比&quot;先 <code>await d3.csv()</code> 再 <code>.map()</code>&quot;省内存</li>\n<li><strong>异步加载的意义</strong>：不阻塞页面渲染，用户能继续交互</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-1-h1","text":"你的原案例","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-1-h2","text":"AI 合成数据的可信度边界","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-1-h3","text":"① 字段名映射","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-1-h4","text":"② 类型转换函数","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-1-h5","text":"③ d3.csv 第二参直接传 row 回调","kind":"code"}],"text":"你的原案例 本章采用中国石油大学（华东）2025 级新生数据。数据由 DeepSeek 大模型合成，含 80 条记录： Text复制 序号、姓名、性别、生日、年龄、班级、籍贯、民族 理论AI 合成数据的可信度边界 维度 含义 DeepSeek 生成数据 准确性 反映真实世界的程度 ⚠️ 姓名/籍贯虚构 完整性 必填字段是否齐全 ✅ 字段齐全 一致性 同一概念在不同地方表达一致 ✅ 字段一致 时效性 数据反映当前状态 ✅ 入学年份匹配 AI 合成数据的\"采样偏差\"：模型倾向\"看起来合理\"的分布（民族偏汉族、籍贯偏大城市）。 代码① 字段名映射 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ①：字段映射 —— 把中文 CSV 列名转英文 JS 变量 const COLUMN_MAP = { \"序号\": \"id\", \"姓名\": \"name\", \"性别\": \"gender\", \"生日\": \"birthday\", \"年龄\": \"age\", \"班级\": \"class\", }; 为什么不用中文 key？ JS 引擎对中文标识符的容错性差（老浏览器报错） 后端、JSON、URL 编码都可能引入乱码 IDE 自动补全、搜索、重构工具对中文支持不一致 最佳实践：CSV 用人可读的中文名，JS 内部统一英文变量。 代码② 类型转换函数 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ②：类型转换 —— 用户原文「推荐方式」 function transformRow(d) { return { id: +d[\"序号\"], // 一元 + 把字符串转 Number name: d[\"姓名\"].trim(), // trim() 去掉首尾空白 birthday: new Date(d[\"生日\"]), // 字符串 → Date 对象 age: +d[\"年龄\"], class: d[\"班级\"].trim(), }; } 关键点解释： +d[\"年龄\"] 是一元加运算符，是 JS 里把字符串转数字的最快写法 new Date(str) 解析 ISO 格式日期，对 \"2007/8/15\" 兼容性差，要用 d3.timeParse(\"%Y-%m-%d\") 兜底 坑：没有 trim() 的话，\"软件工程1班 \" 里的空格会让后续过滤/聚合出错 代码③ d3.csv 第二参直接传 row 回调 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ③：一行完成加载 + 转换 const data = await d3.csv(\"data/newstudent.csv\", transformRow); // 验证类型确实转换了： console.log(typeof data[0].age); // \"number\" console.log(data[0].birthday instanceof Date); // true 为什么这一行很重要： d3.csv 是异步函数，必须 await 第二参的 row 回调会在每一行解析后立即调用——比\"先 await d3.csv() 再 .map()\"省内存 异步加载的意义：不阻塞页面渲染，用户能继续交互","chars":1146},"en":{"title":"Data Generation","rawTitle":"Data Generation","short":"Data Generation","subtitle":"Turn a CSV into typed JS objects: field mapping, type conversion, and async loading.","bigIdea":"The first step is not drawing; it is turning a table of strings into typed objects.","points":["Chinese columns stay readable; English variables stay maintainable. COLUMN_MAP bridges them.","Unary + and trim() cover the common cleanup; use d3.timeParse for dates.","The row callback of d3.csv runs per row, combining loading and conversion in one pass."],"quiz":{"q":"Which is the best way to convert types while reading a CSV?","options":["await d3.csv(url), then .map(transform) on the result","d3.csv(url, transformRow), passing the converter as the second argument","fetch the text, then replace fields with regular expressions"],"answer":1,"why":"The row callback runs immediately after each row is parsed, so loading and conversion happen in one pass. Read-then-map also works but adds a traversal and an intermediate array."},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Your Original Case</span></h3>\n<p>This chapter uses the new student data (新生数据) of the China University of Petroleum (East China) Class of 2025. The data was synthesized by the DeepSeek large model, containing 80 records:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"text\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">Text</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code>序号、姓名、性别、生日、年龄、班级、籍贯、民族</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-1-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">Theory</span><span class=\"blk__text\">The Credibility Boundary of AI-Synthesized Data</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Dimension</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th>Data generated by DeepSeek</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Accuracy</td>\n<td>Degree of reflection of the real world</td>\n<td>⚠️ names/places of origin fabricated</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Completeness</td>\n<td>Whether required fields are complete</td>\n<td>✅ all fields present</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Consistency</td>\n<td>Same concept expressed consistently in different places</td>\n<td>✅ fields consistent</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Timeliness</td>\n<td>Data reflects current state</td>\n<td>✅ enrollment year matches</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>The &quot;sampling bias&quot; of AI-synthesized data</strong>: models tend toward &quot;plausible-looking&quot; distributions (ethnicity skewed toward Han, places of origin skewed toward large cities).</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-1-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① Field Name Mapping</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：字段映射 —— 把中文 CSV 列名转英文 JS 变量\nconst COLUMN_MAP = {\n  &quot;序号&quot;: &quot;id&quot;,\n  &quot;姓名&quot;: &quot;name&quot;,\n  &quot;性别&quot;: &quot;gender&quot;,\n  &quot;生日&quot;: &quot;birthday&quot;,\n  &quot;年龄&quot;: &quot;age&quot;,\n  &quot;班级&quot;: &quot;class&quot;,\n};</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Why not use Chinese keys?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>JS engines have poor tolerance for Chinese identifiers (older browsers throw errors)</li>\n<li>Backends, JSON, and URL encoding may all introduce garbled characters</li>\n<li>IDE autocomplete, search, and refactoring tools have inconsistent support for Chinese</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Best practice</strong>: use human-readable Chinese names in CSV, and unified English variables inside JS.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-1-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② Type Conversion Function</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：类型转换 —— 用户原文「推荐方式」\nfunction transformRow(d) {\n  return {\n    id:       +d[&quot;序号&quot;],              // 一元 + 把字符串转 Number\n    name:     d[&quot;姓名&quot;].trim(),       // trim() 去掉首尾空白\n    birthday: new Date(d[&quot;生日&quot;]),   // 字符串 → Date 对象\n    age:      +d[&quot;年龄&quot;],\n    class:    d[&quot;班级&quot;].trim(),\n  };\n}</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>+d[&quot;年龄&quot;]</code> is the unary plus operator, the fastest way in JS to convert a string to a number</li>\n<li><code>new Date(str)</code> parses ISO-format dates, but has poor compatibility with <code>&quot;2007/8/15&quot;</code>; use <code>d3.timeParse(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;)</code> as a fallback</li>\n<li><strong>Pitfall</strong>: without <code>trim()</code>, the trailing space in &quot;软件工程1班 &quot; will cause errors in later filtering/aggregation</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-1-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">③ Passing the row Callback Directly as the Second Argument of d3.csv</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ③：一行完成加载 + 转换\nconst data = await d3.csv(&quot;data/newstudent.csv&quot;, transformRow);\n\n// 验证类型确实转换了：\nconsole.log(typeof data[0].age);              // &quot;number&quot;\nconsole.log(data[0].birthday instanceof Date); // true</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Why this line matters</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>d3.csv</code> is an asynchronous function and must be <code>await</code>ed</li>\n<li>The row callback in the second argument is called <strong>immediately after each row is parsed</strong> — saving memory compared to &quot;first <code>await d3.csv()</code> then <code>.map()</code>&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>The meaning of asynchronous loading</strong>: it does not block page rendering, so users can keep interacting</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-1-h1","text":"Your Original Case","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-1-h2","text":"The Credibility Boundary of AI-Synthesized Data","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-1-h3","text":"① Field Name Mapping","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-1-h4","text":"② Type Conversion Function","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-1-h5","text":"③ Passing the row Callback Directly as the Second Argument of d3.csv","kind":"code"}],"text":"Your Original Case This chapter uses the new student data (新生数据) of the China University of Petroleum (East China) Class of 2025. The data was synthesized by the DeepSeek large model, containing 80 records: TextCopy 序号、姓名、性别、生日、年龄、班级、籍贯、民族 TheoryThe Credibility Boundary of AI-Synthesized Data Dimension Meaning Data generated by DeepSeek Accuracy Degree of reflection of the real world ⚠️ names/places of origin fabricated Completeness Whether required fields are complete ✅ all fields present Consistency Same concept expressed consistently in different places ✅ fields consistent Timeliness Data reflects current state ✅ enrollment year matches The \"sampling bias\" of AI-synthesized data: models tend toward \"plausible-looking\" distributions (ethnicity skewed toward Han, places of origin skewed toward large cities). Code① Field Name Mapping JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ①：字段映射 —— 把中文 CSV 列名转英文 JS 变量 const COLUMN_MAP = { \"序号\": \"id\", \"姓名\": \"name\", \"性别\": \"gender\", \"生日\": \"birthday\", \"年龄\": \"age\", \"班级\": \"class\", }; Why not use Chinese keys? JS engines have poor tolerance for Chinese identifiers (older browsers throw errors) Backends, JSON, and URL encoding may all introduce garbled characters IDE autocomplete, search, and refactoring tools have inconsistent support for Chinese Best practice: use human-readable Chinese names in CSV, and unified English variables inside JS. Code② Type Conversion Function JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ②：类型转换 —— 用户原文「推荐方式」 function transformRow(d) { return { id: +d[\"序号\"], // 一元 + 把字符串转 Number name: d[\"姓名\"].trim(), // trim() 去掉首尾空白 birthday: new Date(d[\"生日\"]), // 字符串 → Date 对象 age: +d[\"年龄\"], class: d[\"班级\"].trim(), }; } Explanation of key points: +d[\"年龄\"] is the unary plus operator, the fastest way in JS to convert a string to a number new Date(str) parses ISO-format dates, but has poor compatibility with \"2007/8/15\"; use d3.timeParse(\"%Y-%m-%d\") as a fallback Pitfall: without trim(), the trailing space in \"软件工程1班 \" will cause errors in later filtering/aggregation Code③ Passing the row Callback Directly as the Second Argument of d3.csv JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ③：一行完成加载 + 转换 const data = await d3.csv(\"data/newstudent.csv\", transformRow); // 验证类型确实转换了： console.log(typeof data[0].age); // \"number\" console.log(data[0].birthday instanceof Date); // true Why this line matters: d3.csv is an asynchronous function and must be awaited The row callback in the second argument is called immediately after each row is parsed — saving memory compared to \"first await d3.csv() then .map()\" The meaning of asynchronous loading: it does not block page rendering, so users can keep interacting","chars":2238}},"1.2":{"id":"1.2","num":"1.2","chapter":"ch1","demo":"dikw","minutes":7,"related":["1.3","2.1"],"zh":{"title":"数据定义","rawTitle":"数据定义","short":"数据定义","subtitle":"DIKW 金字塔：数据、信息、知识、智慧，以及可视化真正能到达哪一层。","bigIdea":"可视化主要把 Data 升到 Information；Knowledge 需要模型，Wisdom 超出图表的能力。","points":["DIKW 四层回答的问题不同：是什么、谁/何时/何地、如何、为什么。","图表把离散观测组织成可读结构，这是 Data → Information 的核心动作。","把可视化说成「洞察」时要谨慎：模式发现往往还需要统计模型。"],"quiz":{"q":"按 DIKW 模型，可视化最直接完成的是哪一次跃迁？","options":["Data → Information","Information → Knowledge","Knowledge → Wisdom"],"answer":0,"why":"图表把原始观测组织成可读的结构，主要完成 Data → Information；Knowledge 通常需要统计或领域模型，Wisdom 涉及决策与价值判断。"},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--case\">案例</span><span class=\"blk__text\">DIKW 金字塔</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>层</th>\n<th>原文</th>\n<th>回答的问题</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>数据 Data</td>\n<td>原始、离散的观察结果</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>信息 Information</td>\n<td>经过处理、组织、赋予上下文的数据</td>\n<td>谁/什么/何时/何地</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>知识 Knowledge</td>\n<td>对信息的进一步提炼和理解</td>\n<td>如何</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>智慧 Wisdom</td>\n<td>运用知识做出明智判断和战略决策</td>\n<td>为什么/应该怎么做</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-1-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">理论</span><span class=\"blk__text\">可视化在 DIKW 中的位置</span></h3>\n<p><strong>关键洞见</strong>：可视化主要把 <strong>Data 升到 Information</strong>，少数场景能升到 <strong>Knowledge</strong>，但难以跨越到 Wisdom。</p>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ Data → Information：把表格&quot;翻译&quot;成可读图形（折线图、柱状图、热图）</li>\n<li>⚠ Information → Knowledge：模式发现需要统计模型辅助（机器学习）</li>\n<li>❌ Knowledge → Wisdom：决策与战略超出可视化能力</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rowley (2007) 批评</strong>：DIKW 是过度简化的层次模型。但作为教学脚手架仍然最有价值。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-2-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① SVG 金字塔路径</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：trapezoid 路径 —— 从上到下 4 个点的连线\nconst topW = 60, botW = 120;\nconst yTop = 20, yBot = 100;\nconst path = `\n  M ${cx - topW/2} ${yTop}\n  L ${cx + topW/2} ${yTop}\n  L ${cx + botW/2} ${yBot}\n  L ${cx - botW/2} ${yBot}\n  Z\n`;</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SVG path 的 <code>M</code>(moveto)、<code>L</code>(lineto)、<code>Z</code>(close) 是 3 个最常用指令</li>\n<li>模板字符串 <code>${...}</code> 直接嵌入 JS 变量，比字符串拼接可读</li>\n<li><strong>实践</strong>：复杂形状用 <code>d3.symbol()</code>（内置 ★●▲），自己 path 容易出错</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-2-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② 交互高亮（事件）</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：选择集绑定事件 —— 注意 function 而非箭头函数\nconst g = svg.append(&quot;g&quot;)\n  .style(&quot;cursor&quot;, &quot;pointer&quot;)\n  .on(&quot;mouseover&quot;, function () {       // ⚠️ 必须 function，不能箭头函数\n    d3.select(this).select(&quot;path&quot;)      //    因为要用 this 访问当前元素\n       .transition().duration(150)\n       .attr(&quot;fill&quot;, d3.color(layer.color).brighter(0.5));\n  })\n  .on(&quot;click&quot;, () =&gt; showDetail(layer));  // 这里箭头函数 OK（不用 this）</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>必须用 <code>function()</code> 而非箭头函数</strong>——因为 D3 回调要用 <code>this</code> 访问当前元素，箭头函数捕获外层 <code>this</code> 会失效</li>\n<li>这是 D3 最常见的坑</li>\n<li><code>transition().duration()</code> 是 D3 内置动画 API，比 jQuery 还简洁</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-2-h1","text":"DIKW 金字塔","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-2-h2","text":"可视化在 DIKW 中的位置","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-2-h3","text":"① SVG 金字塔路径","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-2-h4","text":"② 交互高亮（事件）","kind":"code"}],"text":"案例DIKW 金字塔 层 原文 回答的问题 数据 Data 原始、离散的观察结果 — 信息 Information 经过处理、组织、赋予上下文的数据 谁/什么/何时/何地 知识 Knowledge 对信息的进一步提炼和理解 如何 智慧 Wisdom 运用知识做出明智判断和战略决策 为什么/应该怎么做 理论可视化在 DIKW 中的位置 关键洞见：可视化主要把 Data 升到 Information，少数场景能升到 Knowledge，但难以跨越到 Wisdom。 ✅ Data → Information：把表格\"翻译\"成可读图形（折线图、柱状图、热图） ⚠ Information → Knowledge：模式发现需要统计模型辅助（机器学习） ❌ Knowledge → Wisdom：决策与战略超出可视化能力 Rowley (2007) 批评：DIKW 是过度简化的层次模型。但作为教学脚手架仍然最有价值。 代码① SVG 金字塔路径 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ①：trapezoid 路径 —— 从上到下 4 个点的连线 const topW = 60, botW = 120; const yTop = 20, yBot = 100; const path = ` M ${cx - topW/2} ${yTop} L ${cx + topW/2} ${yTop} L ${cx + botW/2} ${yBot} L ${cx - botW/2} ${yBot} Z `; 关键点解释： SVG path 的 M(moveto)、L(lineto)、Z(close) 是 3 个最常用指令 模板字符串 ${...} 直接嵌入 JS 变量，比字符串拼接可读 实践：复杂形状用 d3.symbol()（内置 ★●▲），自己 path 容易出错 代码② 交互高亮（事件） JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ②：选择集绑定事件 —— 注意 function 而非箭头函数 const g = svg.append(\"g\") .style(\"cursor\", \"pointer\") .on(\"mouseover\", function () { // ⚠️ 必须 function，不能箭头函数 d3.select(this).select(\"path\") // 因为要用 this 访问当前元素 .transition().duration(150) .attr(\"fill\", d3.color(layer.color).brighter(0.5)); }) .on(\"click\", () => showDetail(layer)); // 这里箭头函数 OK（不用 this） 关键点解释： 必须用 function() 而非箭头函数——因为 D3 回调要用 this 访问当前元素，箭头函数捕获外层 this 会失效 这是 D3 最常见的坑 transition().duration() 是 D3 内置动画 API，比 jQuery 还简洁","chars":1112},"en":{"title":"Data Definition","rawTitle":"Data Definition","short":"Data Definition","subtitle":"The DIKW pyramid: data, information, knowledge, wisdom — and how far visualization actually reaches.","bigIdea":"Visualization mainly lifts Data to Information; Knowledge needs models, and Wisdom is beyond charts.","points":["The four DIKW layers answer different questions: what, who/when/where, how, and why.","Charts organize discrete observations into readable structure: the core Data → Information move.","Be careful when calling a chart an insight: pattern discovery often still needs a statistical model."],"quiz":{"q":"In DIKW terms, which transition does visualization most directly accomplish?","options":["Data → Information","Information → Knowledge","Knowledge → Wisdom"],"answer":0,"why":"Charts organize raw observations into readable structure, mainly Data → Information. Knowledge usually needs statistical or domain models; Wisdom involves judgment and values."},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--case\">Case</span><span class=\"blk__text\">DIKW Pyramid</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>Original text</th>\n<th>Question answered</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Data</td>\n<td>Raw, discrete observations</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Information</td>\n<td>Data that has been processed, organized, and given context</td>\n<td>Who / What / When / Where</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Knowledge</td>\n<td>Further refinement and understanding of information</td>\n<td>How</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Wisdom</td>\n<td>Applying knowledge to make wise judgments and strategic decisions</td>\n<td>Why / What should be done</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-1-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">Theory</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Where Visualization Sits in the DIKW Pyramid</span></h3>\n<p><strong>Key insight</strong>: visualization mainly lifts <strong>Data up to Information</strong>, and in a few scenarios up to <strong>Knowledge</strong>, but it is hard to cross over to Wisdom.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ Data → Information: &quot;translating&quot; tables into readable graphics (line charts, bar charts, heatmaps)</li>\n<li>⚠️ Information → Knowledge: pattern discovery requires statistical models as aid (machine learning)</li>\n<li>❌ Knowledge → Wisdom: decisions and strategy exceed the capability of visualization</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rowley (2007) criticism</strong>: DIKW is an over-simplified hierarchical model. But as a teaching scaffold it remains the most valuable.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-2-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① SVG Pyramid Path</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：trapezoid 路径 —— 从上到下 4 个点的连线\nconst topW = 60, botW = 120;\nconst yTop = 20, yBot = 100;\nconst path = `\n  M ${cx - topW/2} ${yTop}\n  L ${cx + topW/2} ${yTop}\n  L ${cx + botW/2} ${yBot}\n  L ${cx - botW/2} ${yBot}\n  Z\n`;</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The SVG path commands <code>M</code> (moveto), <code>L</code> (lineto), <code>Z</code> (close) are the 3 most commonly used</li>\n<li>Template literals <code>${...}</code> embed JS variables directly, more readable than string concatenation</li>\n<li><strong>Practice</strong>: for complex shapes use <code>d3.symbol()</code> (built-in ★●▲); writing your own path is error-prone</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-2-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② Interactive Highlight (Events)</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：选择集绑定事件 —— 注意 function 而非箭头函数\nconst g = svg.append(&quot;g&quot;)\n  .style(&quot;cursor&quot;, &quot;pointer&quot;)\n  .on(&quot;mouseover&quot;, function () {       // ⚠️ 必须 function，不能箭头函数\n    d3.select(this).select(&quot;path&quot;)      //    因为要用 this 访问当前元素\n       .transition().duration(150)\n       .attr(&quot;fill&quot;, d3.color(layer.color).brighter(0.5));\n  })\n  .on(&quot;click&quot;, () =&gt; showDetail(layer));  // 这里箭头函数 OK（不用 this）</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You must use <code>function()</code> instead of an arrow function</strong> — because D3 callbacks use <code>this</code> to access the current element, and an arrow function captures the outer <code>this</code>, which fails</li>\n<li>This is the most common pitfall in D3</li>\n<li><code>transition().duration()</code> is D3&#39;s built-in animation API, even cleaner than jQuery</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-2-h1","text":"DIKW Pyramid","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-2-h2","text":"Where Visualization Sits in the DIKW Pyramid","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-2-h3","text":"① SVG Pyramid Path","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-2-h4","text":"② Interactive Highlight (Events)","kind":"code"}],"text":"CaseDIKW Pyramid Layer Original text Question answered Data Raw, discrete observations — Information Data that has been processed, organized, and given context Who / What / When / Where Knowledge Further refinement and understanding of information How Wisdom Applying knowledge to make wise judgments and strategic decisions Why / What should be done TheoryWhere Visualization Sits in the DIKW Pyramid Key insight: visualization mainly lifts Data up to Information, and in a few scenarios up to Knowledge, but it is hard to cross over to Wisdom. ✅ Data → Information: \"translating\" tables into readable graphics (line charts, bar charts, heatmaps) ⚠️ Information → Knowledge: pattern discovery requires statistical models as aid (machine learning) ❌ Knowledge → Wisdom: decisions and strategy exceed the capability of visualization Rowley (2007) criticism: DIKW is an over-simplified hierarchical model. But as a teaching scaffold it remains the most valuable. Code① SVG Pyramid Path JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ①：trapezoid 路径 —— 从上到下 4 个点的连线 const topW = 60, botW = 120; const yTop = 20, yBot = 100; const path = ` M ${cx - topW/2} ${yTop} L ${cx + topW/2} ${yTop} L ${cx + botW/2} ${yBot} L ${cx - botW/2} ${yBot} Z `; Explanation of key points: The SVG path commands M (moveto), L (lineto), Z (close) are the 3 most commonly used Template literals ${...} embed JS variables directly, more readable than string concatenation Practice: for complex shapes use d3.symbol() (built-in ★●▲); writing your own path is error-prone Code② Interactive Highlight (Events) JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ②：选择集绑定事件 —— 注意 function 而非箭头函数 const g = svg.append(\"g\") .style(\"cursor\", \"pointer\") .on(\"mouseover\", function () { // ⚠️ 必须 function，不能箭头函数 d3.select(this).select(\"path\") // 因为要用 this 访问当前元素 .transition().duration(150) .attr(\"fill\", d3.color(layer.color).brighter(0.5)); }) .on(\"click\", () => showDetail(layer)); // 这里箭头函数 OK（不用 this） Explanation of key points: You must use function() instead of an arrow function — because D3 callbacks use this to access the current element, and an arrow function captures the outer this, which fails This is the most common pitfall in D3 transition().duration() is D3&#39;s built-in animation API, even cleaner than jQuery","chars":1904}},"1.3":{"id":"1.3","num":"1.3","chapter":"ch1","demo":"scales","minutes":10,"related":["1.1","3.2","2.3"],"zh":{"title":"数据属性","rawTitle":"数据属性","short":"数据属性","subtitle":"Stevens 四种测量尺度 × Mackinlay 视觉通道：什么数据配什么通道。","bigIdea":"位置是最强的定量通道，色相是最强的定性通道；错配会丢信息。","points":["名义、序数、区间、比率，允许的运算不同；区间没有真零点。","定量数据优先位置与长度，序数优先亮度/饱和度，名义优先色相与形状。","比例尺选型是通道匹配的代码实现：连续用 Linear，分类用 Band。"],"quiz":{"q":"「温度 20°C」按 Stevens 尺度属于哪一类？","options":["名义 nominal","序数 ordinal","区间 interval"],"answer":2,"why":"摄氏度可以加减（20°C 比 10°C 高 10°C），但没有真零点（0°C 不等于没有温度），因此是区间尺度；开尔文才是比率尺度。"},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--case\">案例</span><span class=\"blk__text\">3 大类</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>类别</th>\n<th>例子</th>\n<th>说明</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>类别型</td>\n<td>姓名、性别</td>\n<td>无顺序关系</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>序数型</td>\n<td>班级、学位</td>\n<td>有顺序，无间距</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>数值型</td>\n<td>年龄、考试成绩</td>\n<td>定量</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-1-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">理论</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Stevens 测量尺度（1946）—— 4 类</span></h3>\n<p>比你的原文更精细的 4 类：</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>类别</th>\n<th>允许的运算</th>\n<th>典型示例</th>\n<th>对应你原文</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>名义 Nominal</strong></td>\n<td>等价 / 不等价</td>\n<td>姓名、性别</td>\n<td>类别型</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>序数 Ordinal</strong></td>\n<td>+ &gt; &lt;</td>\n<td>等级、班级序号</td>\n<td>序数型</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>区间 Interval</strong></td>\n<td>+ 加减</td>\n<td>温度（°C）</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>比率 Ratio</strong></td>\n<td>+ 加减乘除</td>\n<td>年龄、价格</td>\n<td>数值型</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>关键区别</strong>：区间尺度没有&quot;真零点&quot;（0°C 不是&quot;没有温度&quot;）；比率尺度有真零点（0 元 = 没有钱）。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-3-h3\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">理论</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Mackinlay 视觉通道排序（1986）</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>档次</th>\n<th>通道</th>\n<th>适合的属性</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>定量型</strong></td>\n<td>位置、长度、角度</td>\n<td>比率 / 区间</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>顺序型</strong></td>\n<td>亮度、密度、饱和度</td>\n<td>序数</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>定性型</strong></td>\n<td>色相、形状</td>\n<td>名义</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>核心发现</strong>：位置是最强的定量通道；色相是最强的定性通道。<strong>错配 → 信息丢失</strong>。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-3-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① 比例尺选型</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：scale 选型 —— 属性 ↔ 通道的映射\n// 比率型数据 → scaleLinear（连续定量）\nconst x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, 100]).range([0, 800]);\n\n// 名义/序数型数据 → scaleBand（离散分类）\nconst x = d3.scaleBand()\n  .domain([&quot;软件1班&quot;, &quot;软件2班&quot;, &quot;数据1班&quot;])\n  .range([0, 800]);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>domain()</code> 是数据域（输入），<code>range()</code> 是值域（输出像素）</li>\n<li><strong>选错比例尺是初学者最常犯的错</strong>：类别数据用 scaleLinear 会算出没有意义的中间值（如 0.5 班）</li>\n<li><strong>记忆口诀</strong>：连续定量用 Linear，离散分类用 Band，序数可用 Point</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-3-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② colormap 选型</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：颜色映射 —— 顺序 vs 定性 vs 发散\n// 顺序型（顺序有意义）→ Viridis / Blues —— CVD 友好\nconst color = d3.scaleSequential(d3.interpolateViridis);\n\n// 定性型（无顺序）→ schemeTableau10\nconst color = d3.scaleOrdinal().range(d3.schemeTableau10);\n\n// 发散型（有中点）→ RdBu\nconst color = d3.scaleDiverging(d3.interpolateRdBu);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Viridis 是顺序 colormap 标杆，色觉缺陷（CVD）友好且感知均匀</li>\n<li><strong>常见错误</strong>：用彩虹色 <code>interpolateRainbow</code> 编码数值——既不 CVD 友好，又有假边界</li>\n<li><strong>什么时候用发散型</strong>：有&quot;中间值&quot;的数据（正负、温度 vs 平均值）</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-3-h1","text":"3 大类","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-3-h2","text":"Stevens 测量尺度（1946）—— 4 类","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-3-h3","text":"Mackinlay 视觉通道排序（1986）","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-3-h4","text":"① 比例尺选型","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-3-h5","text":"② colormap 选型","kind":"code"}],"text":"案例3 大类 类别 例子 说明 类别型 姓名、性别 无顺序关系 序数型 班级、学位 有顺序，无间距 数值型 年龄、考试成绩 定量 理论Stevens 测量尺度（1946）—— 4 类 比你的原文更精细的 4 类： 类别 允许的运算 典型示例 对应你原文 名义 Nominal 等价 / 不等价 姓名、性别 类别型 序数 Ordinal + > < 等级、班级序号 序数型 区间 Interval + 加减 温度（°C） — 比率 Ratio + 加减乘除 年龄、价格 数值型 关键区别：区间尺度没有\"真零点\"（0°C 不是\"没有温度\"）；比率尺度有真零点（0 元 = 没有钱）。 理论Mackinlay 视觉通道排序（1986） 档次 通道 适合的属性 定量型 位置、长度、角度 比率 / 区间 顺序型 亮度、密度、饱和度 序数 定性型 色相、形状 名义 核心发现：位置是最强的定量通道；色相是最强的定性通道。错配 → 信息丢失。 代码① 比例尺选型 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ①：scale 选型 —— 属性 ↔ 通道的映射 // 比率型数据 → scaleLinear（连续定量） const x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, 100]).range([0, 800]); // 名义/序数型数据 → scaleBand（离散分类） const x = d3.scaleBand() .domain([\"软件1班\", \"软件2班\", \"数据1班\"]) .range([0, 800]); 关键点解释： domain() 是数据域（输入），range() 是值域（输出像素） 选错比例尺是初学者最常犯的错：类别数据用 scaleLinear 会算出没有意义的中间值（如 0.5 班） 记忆口诀：连续定量用 Linear，离散分类用 Band，序数可用 Point 代码② colormap 选型 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ②：颜色映射 —— 顺序 vs 定性 vs 发散 // 顺序型（顺序有意义）→ Viridis / Blues —— CVD 友好 const color = d3.scaleSequential(d3.interpolateViridis); // 定性型（无顺序）→ schemeTableau10 const color = d3.scaleOrdinal().range(d3.schemeTableau10); // 发散型（有中点）→ RdBu const color = d3.scaleDiverging(d3.interpolateRdBu); 关键点解释： Viridis 是顺序 colormap 标杆，色觉缺陷（CVD）友好且感知均匀 常见错误：用彩虹色 interpolateRainbow 编码数值——既不 CVD 友好，又有假边界 什么时候用发散型：有\"中间值\"的数据（正负、温度 vs 平均值）","chars":1083},"en":{"title":"Data Attributes","rawTitle":"Data Attributes","short":"Data Attributes","subtitle":"Stevens' four measurement scales × Mackinlay's channels: which channel fits which data.","bigIdea":"Position is the strongest quantitative channel; hue is the strongest categorical one. Mismatches lose information.","points":["Nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio allow different operations; interval has no true zero.","Quantitative data prefers position and length; ordinal prefers lightness/saturation; nominal prefers hue and shape.","Scale choice is the code-level implementation: Linear for continuous, Band for categories."],"quiz":{"q":"According to Stevens, '20°C' is which kind of scale?","options":["nominal","ordinal","interval"],"answer":2,"why":"Celsius supports addition/subtraction (20°C is 10°C above 10°C) but has no true zero (0°C does not mean no temperature), so it is interval. Kelvin is a ratio scale."},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--case\">Case</span><span class=\"blk__text\">3 Major Categories</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Categorical</td>\n<td>Name, gender</td>\n<td>No ordinal relationship</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ordinal</td>\n<td>Class, degree</td>\n<td>Has order, no spacing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Numerical</td>\n<td>Age, exam score</td>\n<td>Quantitative</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-1-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">Theory</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Stevens&#39; Measurement Scales (1946) — 4 Categories</span></h3>\n<p>Four categories finer than your original text:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Allowed operations</th>\n<th>Typical example</th>\n<th>Corresponding to your original</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Nominal</strong></td>\n<td>equivalence / non-equivalence</td>\n<td>Name, gender</td>\n<td>Categorical</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ordinal</strong></td>\n<td>+ &gt; &lt;</td>\n<td>rank, class number</td>\n<td>Ordinal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Interval</strong></td>\n<td>+ addition/subtraction</td>\n<td>temperature (°C)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ratio</strong></td>\n<td>+ addition/subtraction/multiplication/division</td>\n<td>age, price</td>\n<td>Numerical</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>Key distinction</strong>: the interval scale has no &quot;true zero point&quot; (0°C is not &quot;no temperature&quot;); the ratio scale has a true zero point (0 yuan = no money).</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-3-h3\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">Theory</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Mackinlay&#39;s Visual Channel Ranking (1986)</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Tier</th>\n<th>Channel</th>\n<th>Suitable attribute</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Quantitative</strong></td>\n<td>position, length, angle</td>\n<td>Ratio / Interval</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ordered</strong></td>\n<td>brightness, density, saturation</td>\n<td>Ordinal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Categorical (qualitative)</strong></td>\n<td>hue, shape</td>\n<td>Nominal</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>Core finding</strong>: position is the strongest quantitative channel; hue is the strongest categorical channel. <strong>Mismatch → information loss</strong>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-3-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① Scale Selection</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：scale 选型 —— 属性 ↔ 通道的映射\n// 比率型数据 → scaleLinear（连续定量）\nconst x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, 100]).range([0, 800]);\n\n// 名义/序数型数据 → scaleBand（离散分类）\nconst x = d3.scaleBand()\n  .domain([&quot;软件1班&quot;, &quot;软件2班&quot;, &quot;数据1班&quot;])\n  .range([0, 800]);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>domain()</code> is the data domain (input), <code>range()</code> is the value range (output pixels)</li>\n<li><strong>Choosing the wrong scale is the most common mistake beginners make</strong>: using scaleLinear for categorical data yields meaningless intermediate values (e.g., 0.5 class)</li>\n<li><strong>Memory aid</strong>: use Linear for continuous quantitative, Band for discrete categorical, Point for ordinal</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-3-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② Colormap Selection</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：颜色映射 —— 顺序 vs 定性 vs 发散\n// 顺序型（顺序有意义）→ Viridis / Blues —— CVD 友好\nconst color = d3.scaleSequential(d3.interpolateViridis);\n\n// 定性型（无顺序）→ schemeTableau10\nconst color = d3.scaleOrdinal().range(d3.schemeTableau10);\n\n// 发散型（有中点）→ RdBu\nconst color = d3.scaleDiverging(d3.interpolateRdBu);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Viridis is the benchmark sequential colormap, color-vision-deficiency (CVD) friendly and perceptually uniform</li>\n<li><strong>Common mistake</strong>: encoding values with the rainbow <code>interpolateRainbow</code> — neither CVD friendly nor free of false boundaries</li>\n<li><strong>When to use diverging</strong>: data with a &quot;midpoint&quot; (positive/negative, temperature vs. average)</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-3-h1","text":"3 Major Categories","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-3-h2","text":"Stevens&#39; Measurement Scales (1946) — 4 Categories","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-3-h3","text":"Mackinlay&#39;s Visual Channel Ranking (1986)","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-3-h4","text":"① Scale Selection","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-3-h5","text":"② Colormap Selection","kind":"code"}],"text":"Case3 Major Categories Category Example Description Categorical Name, gender No ordinal relationship Ordinal Class, degree Has order, no spacing Numerical Age, exam score Quantitative TheoryStevens&#39; Measurement Scales (1946) — 4 Categories Four categories finer than your original text: Category Allowed operations Typical example Corresponding to your original Nominal equivalence / non-equivalence Name, gender Categorical Ordinal + > < rank, class number Ordinal Interval + addition/subtraction temperature (°C) — Ratio + addition/subtraction/multiplication/division age, price Numerical Key distinction: the interval scale has no \"true zero point\" (0°C is not \"no temperature\"); the ratio scale has a true zero point (0 yuan = no money). TheoryMackinlay&#39;s Visual Channel Ranking (1986) Tier Channel Suitable attribute Quantitative position, length, angle Ratio / Interval Ordered brightness, density, saturation Ordinal Categorical (qualitative) hue, shape Nominal Core finding: position is the strongest quantitative channel; hue is the strongest categorical channel. Mismatch → information loss. Code① Scale Selection JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ①：scale 选型 —— 属性 ↔ 通道的映射 // 比率型数据 → scaleLinear（连续定量） const x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, 100]).range([0, 800]); // 名义/序数型数据 → scaleBand（离散分类） const x = d3.scaleBand() .domain([\"软件1班\", \"软件2班\", \"数据1班\"]) .range([0, 800]); Explanation of key points: domain() is the data domain (input), range() is the value range (output pixels) Choosing the wrong scale is the most common mistake beginners make: using scaleLinear for categorical data yields meaningless intermediate values (e.g., 0.5 class) Memory aid: use Linear for continuous quantitative, Band for discrete categorical, Point for ordinal Code② Colormap Selection JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ②：颜色映射 —— 顺序 vs 定性 vs 发散 // 顺序型（顺序有意义）→ Viridis / Blues —— CVD 友好 const color = d3.scaleSequential(d3.interpolateViridis); // 定性型（无顺序）→ schemeTableau10 const color = d3.scaleOrdinal().range(d3.schemeTableau10); // 发散型（有中点）→ RdBu const color = d3.scaleDiverging(d3.interpolateRdBu); Explanation of key points: Viridis is the benchmark sequential colormap, color-vision-deficiency (CVD) friendly and perceptually uniform Common mistake: encoding values with the rainbow interpolateRainbow — neither CVD friendly nor free of false boundaries When to use diverging: data with a \"midpoint\" (positive/negative, temperature vs. average)","chars":2108}},"1.4":{"id":"1.4","num":"1.4","chapter":"ch1","demo":"arrayops","minutes":9,"related":["1.5","2.2"],"zh":{"title":"数据变换","rawTitle":"数据变换","short":"数据变换","subtitle":"8 个函数式数组操作：map、filter、reduce、cross、group 与 rollup。","bigIdea":"函数式数据流 = 不可变 + 纯函数 + 可链式；每一层都能单独测试。","points":["map / filter / reduce 是最小的三件套，链式调用不修改原数组。","cross 生成笛卡尔积，group / rollup 完成层次聚合。","group 保留组内所有元素，rollup 把每组归约成一个值。"],"quiz":{"q":"d3.group 与 d3.rollup 最关键的区别是？","options":["group 返回数组，rollup 返回对象","group 保留组内元素，rollup 归约为一个值","rollup 只能按一个键分组"],"answer":1,"why":"两者都返回 Map；group 的值是组内元素数组，rollup 的值是 reducer 的结果（如计数、求和）。"},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--case\">案例</span><span class=\"blk__text\">8 个函数</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>函数</th>\n<th>用途</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td><code>map(iterable, mapper)</code></td>\n<td>类似 Array.map</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><code>reduce(iterable, reducer, init)</code></td>\n<td>类似 Array.reduce</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><code>cross(...iterables, reducer)</code></td>\n<td>笛卡尔积</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><code>merge(iterables)</code></td>\n<td>合并为扁平数组</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><code>pairs(iterable, reducer)</code></td>\n<td>相邻元素对</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td><code>transpose(matrix)</code></td>\n<td>矩阵转置</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td><code>zip(...arrays)</code></td>\n<td>按位合并</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td><code>filter(iterable, test)</code></td>\n<td>类似 Array.filter</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-1-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">理论</span><span class=\"blk__text\">函数式数据流</span></h3>\n<p>这 8 个函数的共同特点：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>不可变（immutable）</strong>：输入不变，返回新数组</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>纯函数</strong>：相同输入 → 相同输出</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>可链式</strong>：返回值是数组，可以接下一层变换</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>为什么函数式？</strong> 可推理（每层独立可测）、可并行（map/reduce 天然并行）、可缓存（纯函数可记忆化）。</p>\n<p><strong>OLAP 数据立方体雏形</strong>：<code>transpose</code> 做宽/长格式转换，<code>group + rollup</code> 做切片/切块/钻取。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-4-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① map / reduce 链式组合</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：函数式数据流 —— map 后接 filter 再 reduce\nconst avgAge =\n  students\n    .filter(s =&gt; s.gender === &quot;男&quot;)     // ① 过滤男生\n    .map(s =&gt; s.age)                    // ② 提取年龄\n    .reduce((sum, a) =&gt; sum + a, 0)     // ③ 合计\n  / students.filter(s =&gt; s.gender === &quot;男&quot;).length; // ④ 求平均</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>链式调用的每一步返回新数组，不会修改原数组</li>\n<li><strong>与命令式对比</strong>：命令式需要 4 个临时变量 + 一个 for 循环，函数式一行搞定</li>\n<li><strong>性能权衡</strong>：每次 map/filter 都会创建新数组，对超大数组有性能损耗（百万级以上才显著）</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-4-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② cross（笛卡尔积）</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：cross —— 笛卡尔积\nconst genders = [&quot;男&quot;, &quot;女&quot;];\nconst majors  = [&quot;软件工程&quot;, &quot;数据科学&quot;];\nconst combos  = d3.cross(genders, majors);\n// → [[&quot;男&quot;,&quot;软件工程&quot;], [&quot;男&quot;,&quot;数据科学&quot;], [&quot;女&quot;,&quot;软件工程&quot;], [&quot;女&quot;,&quot;数据科学&quot;]]</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>笛卡尔积常用在&quot;两两组合&quot;分析（如性别 × 专业的人数统计）</li>\n<li>第二参 reducer 可选，用来&quot;合并&quot;两个元素</li>\n<li><strong>扩展</strong>：n 个数组的笛卡尔积大小是各数组长度的乘积</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-4-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">③ group / rollup（聚合）</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ③：group 与 rollup —— 层次聚合\n// group 返回 Map（保留所有元素）\nconst byClass = d3.group(students, s =&gt; s.class);\n\n// rollup 返回 Map（每个 key 只保留聚合值）\nconst countByClass = d3.rollup(\n  students,\n  v =&gt; v.length,         // reducer\n  s =&gt; s.class           // key 提取函数\n);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>group</code> vs <code>rollup</code> 是&quot;分组保留&quot;vs&quot;分组聚合&quot;的区别</li>\n<li><code>rollup</code> 第二参是 reducer 函数（这里取长度）</li>\n<li>后续章节 doc-02 会详细用 rollup 做树形数据</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-4-h1","text":"8 个函数","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-4-h2","text":"函数式数据流","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-4-h3","text":"① map / reduce 链式组合","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-4-h4","text":"② cross（笛卡尔积）","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-4-h5","text":"③ group / rollup（聚合）","kind":"code"}],"text":"案例8 个函数 # 函数 用途 1 map(iterable, mapper) 类似 Array.map 2 reduce(iterable, reducer, init) 类似 Array.reduce 3 cross(...iterables, reducer) 笛卡尔积 4 merge(iterables) 合并为扁平数组 5 pairs(iterable, reducer) 相邻元素对 6 transpose(matrix) 矩阵转置 7 zip(...arrays) 按位合并 8 filter(iterable, test) 类似 Array.filter 理论函数式数据流 这 8 个函数的共同特点： ✅ 不可变（immutable）：输入不变，返回新数组 ✅ 纯函数：相同输入 → 相同输出 ✅ 可链式：返回值是数组，可以接下一层变换 为什么函数式？ 可推理（每层独立可测）、可并行（map/reduce 天然并行）、可缓存（纯函数可记忆化）。 OLAP 数据立方体雏形：transpose 做宽/长格式转换，group + rollup 做切片/切块/钻取。 代码① map / reduce 链式组合 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ①：函数式数据流 —— map 后接 filter 再 reduce const avgAge = students .filter(s => s.gender === \"男\") // ① 过滤男生 .map(s => s.age) // ② 提取年龄 .reduce((sum, a) => sum + a, 0) // ③ 合计 / students.filter(s => s.gender === \"男\").length; // ④ 求平均 关键点解释： 链式调用的每一步返回新数组，不会修改原数组 与命令式对比：命令式需要 4 个临时变量 + 一个 for 循环，函数式一行搞定 性能权衡：每次 map/filter 都会创建新数组，对超大数组有性能损耗（百万级以上才显著） 代码② cross（笛卡尔积） JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ②：cross —— 笛卡尔积 const genders = [\"男\", \"女\"]; const majors = [\"软件工程\", \"数据科学\"]; const combos = d3.cross(genders, majors); // → [[\"男\",\"软件工程\"], [\"男\",\"数据科学\"], [\"女\",\"软件工程\"], [\"女\",\"数据科学\"]] 关键点解释： 笛卡尔积常用在\"两两组合\"分析（如性别 × 专业的人数统计） 第二参 reducer 可选，用来\"合并\"两个元素 扩展：n 个数组的笛卡尔积大小是各数组长度的乘积 代码③ group / rollup（聚合） JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ③：group 与 rollup —— 层次聚合 // group 返回 Map（保留所有元素） const byClass = d3.group(students, s => s.class); // rollup 返回 Map（每个 key 只保留聚合值） const countByClass = d3.rollup( students, v => v.length, // reducer s => s.class // key 提取函数 ); 关键点解释： group vs rollup 是\"分组保留\"vs\"分组聚合\"的区别 rollup 第二参是 reducer 函数（这里取长度） 后续章节 doc-02 会详细用 rollup 做树形数据","chars":1336},"en":{"title":"Data Transformation","rawTitle":"Data Transformation","short":"Data Transformation","subtitle":"Eight functional array operations: map, filter, reduce, cross, group, rollup.","bigIdea":"Functional data flow = immutable + pure + chainable; every stage can be tested in isolation.","points":["map / filter / reduce are the minimal trio; chaining never mutates the input.","cross produces a Cartesian product; group / rollup perform hierarchical aggregation.","group keeps all elements in a bucket; rollup reduces each bucket to one value."],"quiz":{"q":"What is the key difference between d3.group and d3.rollup?","options":["group returns an array, rollup returns an object","group keeps the elements, rollup reduces them to one value","rollup can only group by one key"],"answer":1,"why":"Both return a Map; group maps keys to arrays of elements, while rollup maps keys to the reducer result (count, sum, ...)."},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--case\">Case</span><span class=\"blk__text\">8 Functions</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Function</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td><code>map(iterable, mapper)</code></td>\n<td>similar to Array.map</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><code>reduce(iterable, reducer, init)</code></td>\n<td>similar to Array.reduce</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><code>cross(...iterables, reducer)</code></td>\n<td>Cartesian product</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><code>merge(iterables)</code></td>\n<td>merge into a flat array</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><code>pairs(iterable, reducer)</code></td>\n<td>adjacent element pairs</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td><code>transpose(matrix)</code></td>\n<td>matrix transpose</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td><code>zip(...arrays)</code></td>\n<td>combine element-wise</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td><code>filter(iterable, test)</code></td>\n<td>similar to Array.filter</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-1-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">Theory</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Functional Data Flow</span></h3>\n<p>Common characteristics of these 8 functions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>Immutable</strong>: input unchanged, returns a new array</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>Pure function</strong>: same input → same output</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>Chainable</strong>: the return value is an array, which can feed the next transformation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Why functional?</strong> Reasonable (each layer independently testable), parallelizable (map/reduce are naturally parallel), cacheable (pure functions can be memoized).</p>\n<p><strong>The embryonic form of an OLAP data cube</strong>: <code>transpose</code> converts wide/long formats, <code>group + rollup</code> performs slice/dice/drill-down.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-4-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① map / reduce Chained Composition</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：函数式数据流 —— map 后接 filter 再 reduce\nconst avgAge =\n  students\n    .filter(s =&gt; s.gender === &quot;男&quot;)     // ① 过滤男生\n    .map(s =&gt; s.age)                    // ② 提取年龄\n    .reduce((sum, a) =&gt; sum + a, 0)     // ③ 合计\n  / students.filter(s =&gt; s.gender === &quot;男&quot;).length; // ④ 求平均</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each step of the chained call returns a new array and does not modify the original</li>\n<li><strong>Compared with imperative</strong>: imperative needs 4 temporary variables + a for loop; functional does it in one line</li>\n<li><strong>Performance trade-off</strong>: each map/filter creates a new array, causing performance overhead for very large arrays (significant only at the millions level)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-4-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② cross (Cartesian Product)</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：cross —— 笛卡尔积\nconst genders = [&quot;男&quot;, &quot;女&quot;];\nconst majors  = [&quot;软件工程&quot;, &quot;数据科学&quot;];\nconst combos  = d3.cross(genders, majors);\n// → [[&quot;男&quot;,&quot;软件工程&quot;], [&quot;男&quot;,&quot;数据科学&quot;], [&quot;女&quot;,&quot;软件工程&quot;], [&quot;女&quot;,&quot;数据科学&quot;]]</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cartesian products are commonly used in &quot;pairwise combination&quot; analysis (e.g., counting people by gender × major)</li>\n<li>The second-argument reducer is optional, used to &quot;merge&quot; the two elements</li>\n<li><strong>Extension</strong>: the size of the Cartesian product of n arrays is the product of each array&#39;s length</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-4-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">③ group / rollup (Aggregation)</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ③：group 与 rollup —— 层次聚合\n// group 返回 Map（保留所有元素）\nconst byClass = d3.group(students, s =&gt; s.class);\n\n// rollup 返回 Map（每个 key 只保留聚合值）\nconst countByClass = d3.rollup(\n  students,\n  v =&gt; v.length,         // reducer\n  s =&gt; s.class           // key 提取函数\n);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>group</code> vs <code>rollup</code> is the difference between &quot;group and keep&quot; vs &quot;group and aggregate&quot;</li>\n<li>The second argument of <code>rollup</code> is the reducer function (here it takes the length)</li>\n<li>A later chapter, <code>doc-02</code>, will use <code>rollup</code> in detail for tree-shaped data</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-4-h1","text":"8 Functions","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-4-h2","text":"Functional Data Flow","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-4-h3","text":"① map / reduce Chained Composition","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-4-h4","text":"② cross (Cartesian Product)","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-4-h5","text":"③ group / rollup (Aggregation)","kind":"code"}],"text":"Case8 Functions # Function Purpose 1 map(iterable, mapper) similar to Array.map 2 reduce(iterable, reducer, init) similar to Array.reduce 3 cross(...iterables, reducer) Cartesian product 4 merge(iterables) merge into a flat array 5 pairs(iterable, reducer) adjacent element pairs 6 transpose(matrix) matrix transpose 7 zip(...arrays) combine element-wise 8 filter(iterable, test) similar to Array.filter TheoryFunctional Data Flow Common characteristics of these 8 functions: ✅ Immutable: input unchanged, returns a new array ✅ Pure function: same input → same output ✅ Chainable: the return value is an array, which can feed the next transformation Why functional? Reasonable (each layer independently testable), parallelizable (map/reduce are naturally parallel), cacheable (pure functions can be memoized). The embryonic form of an OLAP data cube: transpose converts wide/long formats, group + rollup performs slice/dice/drill-down. Code① map / reduce Chained Composition JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ①：函数式数据流 —— map 后接 filter 再 reduce const avgAge = students .filter(s => s.gender === \"男\") // ① 过滤男生 .map(s => s.age) // ② 提取年龄 .reduce((sum, a) => sum + a, 0) // ③ 合计 / students.filter(s => s.gender === \"男\").length; // ④ 求平均 Explanation of key points: Each step of the chained call returns a new array and does not modify the original Compared with imperative: imperative needs 4 temporary variables + a for loop; functional does it in one line Performance trade-off: each map/filter creates a new array, causing performance overhead for very large arrays (significant only at the millions level) Code② cross (Cartesian Product) JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ②：cross —— 笛卡尔积 const genders = [\"男\", \"女\"]; const majors = [\"软件工程\", \"数据科学\"]; const combos = d3.cross(genders, majors); // → [[\"男\",\"软件工程\"], [\"男\",\"数据科学\"], [\"女\",\"软件工程\"], [\"女\",\"数据科学\"]] Explanation of key points: Cartesian products are commonly used in \"pairwise combination\" analysis (e.g., counting people by gender × major) The second-argument reducer is optional, used to \"merge\" the two elements Extension: the size of the Cartesian product of n arrays is the product of each array&#39;s length Code③ group / rollup (Aggregation) JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ③：group 与 rollup —— 层次聚合 // group 返回 Map（保留所有元素） const byClass = d3.group(students, s => s.class); // rollup 返回 Map（每个 key 只保留聚合值） const countByClass = d3.rollup( students, v => v.length, // reducer s => s.class // key 提取函数 ); Explanation of key points: group vs rollup is the difference between \"group and keep\" vs \"group and aggregate\" The second argument of rollup is the reducer function (here it takes the length) A later chapter, doc-02, will use rollup in detail for tree-shaped data","chars":2288}},"1.5":{"id":"1.5","num":"1.5","chapter":"ch1","demo":"datajoin","minutes":10,"related":["2.3","2.4"],"zh":{"title":"D3 数据选择器","rawTitle":"D3 数据选择器","short":"D3 选择器","subtitle":"Data-Join 三态：enter、update、exit，以及 key 函数如何保住元素身份。","bigIdea":"数据变化时，D3 不是「重画」，而是把新数据与旧元素做一次差分。","points":["新数据多出来的进入 enter，对得上的进入 update，多余的进入 exit。","key 函数让元素在数据重排时保持身份，过渡动画才不会错乱。","select 操作单个元素，selectAll 用于批量绑定；先用空选择占位。"],"quiz":{"q":"数据从 5 条变成 3 条，D3 会把多出的 2 个元素放进哪个状态？","options":["enter","update","exit"],"answer":2,"why":"新数据少于旧元素时，多余的旧元素进入 exit，通常执行 remove()；反过来数据变多时，新元素进入 enter。"},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-5-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--case\">案例</span><span class=\"blk__text\">6 个方法</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>方法</th>\n<th>返回</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><code>d3.select</code></td>\n<td>单个元素</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>d3.selectAll</code></td>\n<td>多个元素的 selection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>selection.select</code></td>\n<td>每个选中元素的后代中第一个</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>selection.selectAll</code></td>\n<td>后代中所有</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>selection.selectChild</code></td>\n<td>直接子元素第一个</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>selection.selectChildren</code></td>\n<td>所有直接子元素</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-1-5-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">理论</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Data-Join 三态模型</span></h3>\n<p>D3 的核心是 <strong>Data-Join</strong>：把数据数组&quot;绑定&quot;到 DOM 元素上。当数据变化时：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>新数据 &gt; 旧数据：多出来的进入 <strong>enter</strong>（要 append）</li>\n<li>新数据 = 旧数据：原有元素进入 <strong>update</strong>（要改属性）</li>\n<li>新数据 &lt; 旧数据：多余的元素进入 <strong>exit</strong>（要 remove）</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-5-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① .join(enter, update, exit) 三态</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：D3 v5+ 的 join() API —— 优雅处理三态\nconst circles = svg.selectAll(&quot;circle&quot;)\n  .data(currentData)\n  .join(\n    enter  =&gt; enter.append(&quot;circle&quot;).attr(&quot;fill&quot;, &quot;green&quot;),  // enter\n    update =&gt; update.attr(&quot;fill&quot;, &quot;cyan&quot;),                    // update\n    exit   =&gt; exit.remove()                                   // exit\n  );</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>join 的三个回调分别在 enter / update / exit 阶段被调用</li>\n<li>比 v3 的 <code>enter().append()</code> + <code>exit().remove()</code> 写法更简洁，逻辑更不易出错</li>\n<li><strong>类比</strong>：React 的 diff + patch —— 同样思想，但 React 帮你做了，D3 让你自己写变换函数</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-5-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② key 函数保身份</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：key 函数 —— 元素身份的稳定器\n// ❌ 不带 key：数据顺序变化 → 所有元素都&quot;update&quot;，过渡动画错乱\nsvg.selectAll(&quot;circle&quot;).data(newData);\n\n// ✅ 带 key：用唯一字段绑定身份\nsvg.selectAll(&quot;circle&quot;).data(newData, d =&gt; d.id);\n\n// 同样的逻辑用 React 描述：key={item.id}</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>key 函数是 D3 动画的灵魂</strong></li>\n<li>没有 key 时，D3 按 index 绑定身份：数据重排会导致&quot;所有元素都换位置&quot;</li>\n<li>带 key 后，每个 circle 知道自己的 id 是什么，重排时只是 cx 变化，过渡动画自然</li>\n<li><strong>类比</strong>：与 React 的 <code>key={item.id}</code> 完全相同的思想</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-5-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">③ select vs selectAll</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ③：选择器的核心区别\n// select：返回 1 个元素（第一个匹配）；数据绑定只对这一个元素\nconst title = d3.select(&quot;#title&quot;);\n\n// selectAll：返回多个元素；数据绑定按顺序一一对应\nconst bars = d3.selectAll(&quot;.bar&quot;).data(values);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>select</code> 用于&quot;操作单个元素&quot;，<code>selectAll</code> 用于&quot;批量绑定数据&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>常见错误</strong>：用 <code>selectAll(&quot;.bar&quot;)</code> 给数组绑定数据时，元素数量与数据数量必须匹配，否则&quot;留空&quot;或&quot;溢出&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>最佳实践</strong>：先用 <code>selectAll</code> 创建占位元素（可能为空），再 <code>.data().join(...)</code></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-5-h1","text":"6 个方法","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-5-h2","text":"Data-Join 三态模型","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-5-h3","text":"① .join(enter, update, exit) 三态","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-5-h4","text":"② key 函数保身份","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-5-h5","text":"③ select vs selectAll","kind":"code"}],"text":"案例6 个方法 方法 返回 d3.select 单个元素 d3.selectAll 多个元素的 selection selection.select 每个选中元素的后代中第一个 selection.selectAll 后代中所有 selection.selectChild 直接子元素第一个 selection.selectChildren 所有直接子元素 理论Data-Join 三态模型 D3 的核心是 Data-Join：把数据数组\"绑定\"到 DOM 元素上。当数据变化时： 新数据 > 旧数据：多出来的进入 enter（要 append） 新数据 = 旧数据：原有元素进入 update（要改属性） 新数据 < 旧数据：多余的元素进入 exit（要 remove） 代码① .join(enter, update, exit) 三态 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ①：D3 v5+ 的 join() API —— 优雅处理三态 const circles = svg.selectAll(\"circle\") .data(currentData) .join( enter => enter.append(\"circle\").attr(\"fill\", \"green\"), // enter update => update.attr(\"fill\", \"cyan\"), // update exit => exit.remove() // exit ); 关键点解释： join 的三个回调分别在 enter / update / exit 阶段被调用 比 v3 的 enter().append() + exit().remove() 写法更简洁，逻辑更不易出错 类比：React 的 diff + patch —— 同样思想，但 React 帮你做了，D3 让你自己写变换函数 代码② key 函数保身份 JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ②：key 函数 —— 元素身份的稳定器 // ❌ 不带 key：数据顺序变化 → 所有元素都\"update\"，过渡动画错乱 svg.selectAll(\"circle\").data(newData); // ✅ 带 key：用唯一字段绑定身份 svg.selectAll(\"circle\").data(newData, d => d.id); // 同样的逻辑用 React 描述：key={item.id} 关键点解释： key 函数是 D3 动画的灵魂 没有 key 时，D3 按 index 绑定身份：数据重排会导致\"所有元素都换位置\" 带 key 后，每个 circle 知道自己的 id 是什么，重排时只是 cx 变化，过渡动画自然 类比：与 React 的 key={item.id} 完全相同的思想 代码③ select vs selectAll JavaScript复制 // ⭐ 关键点 ③：选择器的核心区别 // select：返回 1 个元素（第一个匹配）；数据绑定只对这一个元素 const title = d3.select(\"#title\"); // selectAll：返回多个元素；数据绑定按顺序一一对应 const bars = d3.selectAll(\".bar\").data(values); 关键点解释： select 用于\"操作单个元素\"，selectAll 用于\"批量绑定数据\" 常见错误：用 selectAll(\".bar\") 给数组绑定数据时，元素数量与数据数量必须匹配，否则\"留空\"或\"溢出\" 最佳实践：先用 selectAll 创建占位元素（可能为空），再 .data().join(...)","chars":1368},"en":{"title":"D3 Data Selectors","rawTitle":"D3 Data Selectors","short":"D3 Selections","subtitle":"The three states of data-join: enter, update, exit, and how a key function preserves identity.","bigIdea":"When data changes, D3 diffs new data against existing elements instead of redrawing everything.","points":["Extra data enters; matched data updates; leftover elements exit.","A key function preserves identity across reordering, keeping transitions coherent.","select targets one element; selectAll binds in bulk. Start with an empty selection."],"quiz":{"q":"Data shrinks from 5 items to 3. Where do the 2 extra elements go?","options":["enter","update","exit"],"answer":2,"why":"When there is less data than existing elements, the extra elements enter the exit selection and are usually removed. When data grows, new elements enter."},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-1-5-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--case\">Case</span><span class=\"blk__text\">6 Methods</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Returns</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><code>d3.select</code></td>\n<td>single element</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>d3.selectAll</code></td>\n<td>a selection of multiple elements</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>selection.select</code></td>\n<td>the first among the descendants of each selected element</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>selection.selectAll</code></td>\n<td>all among the descendants</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>selection.selectChild</code></td>\n<td>the first direct child element</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>selection.selectChildren</code></td>\n<td>all direct child elements</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-1-5-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--theory\">Theory</span><span class=\"blk__text\">The Data-Join Three-State Model</span></h3>\n<p>The core of D3 is <strong>Data-Join</strong>: &quot;binding&quot; a data array to DOM elements. When the data changes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>New data &gt; old data: the extras enter <strong>enter</strong> (need to append)</li>\n<li>New data = old data: the original elements enter <strong>update</strong> (need attribute changes)</li>\n<li>New data &lt; old data: the surplus elements enter <strong>exit</strong> (need to remove)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-5-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① The .join(enter, update, exit) Three States</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ①：D3 v5+ 的 join() API —— 优雅处理三态\nconst circles = svg.selectAll(&quot;circle&quot;)\n  .data(currentData)\n  .join(\n    enter  =&gt; enter.append(&quot;circle&quot;).attr(&quot;fill&quot;, &quot;green&quot;),  // enter\n    update =&gt; update.attr(&quot;fill&quot;, &quot;cyan&quot;),                    // update\n    exit   =&gt; exit.remove()                                   // exit\n  );</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The three callbacks of join are invoked at the enter / update / exit stages respectively</li>\n<li>More concise than the v3 <code>enter().append()</code> + <code>exit().remove()</code> style, and less error-prone logically</li>\n<li><strong>Analogy</strong>: React&#39;s diff + patch — same idea, but React does it for you, while D3 makes you write the transform functions yourself</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-5-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② The Key Function Preserves Identity</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ②：key 函数 —— 元素身份的稳定器\n// ❌ 不带 key：数据顺序变化 → 所有元素都&quot;update&quot;，过渡动画错乱\nsvg.selectAll(&quot;circle&quot;).data(newData);\n\n// ✅ 带 key：用唯一字段绑定身份\nsvg.selectAll(&quot;circle&quot;).data(newData, d =&gt; d.id);\n\n// 同样的逻辑用 React 描述：key={item.id}</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The key function is the soul of D3 animations</strong></li>\n<li>Without a key, D3 binds identity by index: reordering data causes &quot;all elements to change position&quot;</li>\n<li>With a key, each circle knows its own id; on reorder only cx changes, and the transition animation is natural</li>\n<li><strong>Analogy</strong>: exactly the same idea as React&#39;s <code>key={item.id}</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-1-5-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">③ select vs selectAll</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"javascript\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-javascript\">// ⭐ 关键点 ③：选择器的核心区别\n// select：返回 1 个元素（第一个匹配）；数据绑定只对这一个元素\nconst title = d3.select(&quot;#title&quot;);\n\n// selectAll：返回多个元素；数据绑定按顺序一一对应\nconst bars = d3.selectAll(&quot;.bar&quot;).data(values);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Explanation of key points</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>select</code> is for &quot;operating on a single element&quot;, <code>selectAll</code> is for &quot;binding data in bulk&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>Common mistake</strong>: when using <code>selectAll(&quot;.bar&quot;)</code> to bind data to an array, the number of elements and the number of data items must match, otherwise there is &quot;empty space&quot; or &quot;overflow&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>Best practice</strong>: first use <code>selectAll</code> to create placeholder elements (possibly empty), then <code>.data().join(...)</code></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-1-5-h1","text":"6 Methods","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-1-5-h2","text":"The Data-Join Three-State Model","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-1-5-h3","text":"① The .join(enter, update, exit) Three States","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-5-h4","text":"② The Key Function Preserves Identity","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-1-5-h5","text":"③ select vs selectAll","kind":"code"}],"text":"Case6 Methods Method Returns d3.select single element d3.selectAll a selection of multiple elements selection.select the first among the descendants of each selected element selection.selectAll all among the descendants selection.selectChild the first direct child element selection.selectChildren all direct child elements TheoryThe Data-Join Three-State Model The core of D3 is Data-Join: \"binding\" a data array to DOM elements. When the data changes: New data > old data: the extras enter enter (need to append) New data = old data: the original elements enter update (need attribute changes) New data < old data: the surplus elements enter exit (need to remove) Code① The .join(enter, update, exit) Three States JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ①：D3 v5+ 的 join() API —— 优雅处理三态 const circles = svg.selectAll(\"circle\") .data(currentData) .join( enter => enter.append(\"circle\").attr(\"fill\", \"green\"), // enter update => update.attr(\"fill\", \"cyan\"), // update exit => exit.remove() // exit ); Explanation of key points: The three callbacks of join are invoked at the enter / update / exit stages respectively More concise than the v3 enter().append() + exit().remove() style, and less error-prone logically Analogy: React&#39;s diff + patch — same idea, but React does it for you, while D3 makes you write the transform functions yourself Code② The Key Function Preserves Identity JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ②：key 函数 —— 元素身份的稳定器 // ❌ 不带 key：数据顺序变化 → 所有元素都\"update\"，过渡动画错乱 svg.selectAll(\"circle\").data(newData); // ✅ 带 key：用唯一字段绑定身份 svg.selectAll(\"circle\").data(newData, d => d.id); // 同样的逻辑用 React 描述：key={item.id} Explanation of key points: The key function is the soul of D3 animations Without a key, D3 binds identity by index: reordering data causes \"all elements to change position\" With a key, each circle knows its own id; on reorder only cx changes, and the transition animation is natural Analogy: exactly the same idea as React&#39;s key={item.id} Code③ select vs selectAll JavaScriptCopy // ⭐ 关键点 ③：选择器的核心区别 // select：返回 1 个元素（第一个匹配）；数据绑定只对这一个元素 const title = d3.select(\"#title\"); // selectAll：返回多个元素；数据绑定按顺序一一对应 const bars = d3.selectAll(\".bar\").data(values); Explanation of key points: select is for \"operating on a single element\", selectAll is for \"binding data in bulk\" Common mistake: when using selectAll(\".bar\") to bind data to an array, the number of elements and the number of data items must match, otherwise there is \"empty space\" or \"overflow\" Best practice: first use selectAll to create placeholder elements (possibly empty), then .data().join(...)","chars":2191}},"2.1":{"id":"2.1","num":"2.1","chapter":"ch2","demo":"pipeline","minutes":9,"related":["1.2","1.3","2.2"],"zh":{"title":"数据可视化流程","rawTitle":"数据可视化流程（Card · Mackinlay · van Wijk）","short":"可视化流程","subtitle":"Card 数据流、Mackinlay 自动决策、van Wijk 反馈环：三个模型，一条链路。","bigIdea":"三个模型不是互相竞争，而是同一件事的三个侧面：管道、决策、反馈。","points":["Card：Raw Data → Data Tables → Visual Structure → Views。","Mackinlay：按数据类型自动选量化误差最小的通道。","van Wijk：View ⇆ Filter ⇆ Param 的反馈环才是交互式可视化的核心。"],"quiz":{"q":"van Wijk 模型相对 Card 模型，最强调的是什么？","options":["数据清洗","视觉通道排序","用户交互形成的反馈环"],"answer":2,"why":"van Wijk 把 View、Filter、Param 之间的往复反馈放在中心；Card 更关注从数据到视图的管道，Mackinlay 关注通道选择。"},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-2-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">你的原案例</span></h3>\n<p>3 个可视化流程模型：</p>\n<ol>\n<li>参考 Card 1999 模型绘制流程图（Box Flowcharts）</li>\n<li>Mackinlay 自动化准则</li>\n<li>van Wijk 模型（含交互反馈）</li>\n</ol>\n<p>原图是一张概念图。本节课用 D3 重画这张概念图，每个节点点击后展开在三个模型中的对应细节。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__text\">嵌入的理论</span></h3>\n<p><strong>Card 数据流模型（Card, Mackinlay &amp; Shneiderman, 1999）</strong></p>\n<p>数据可视化的&quot;管道&quot;：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>原始数据</strong> (Raw Data) → <strong>数据表</strong> (Data Tables) → <strong>视觉结构</strong> (Visual Structure) → <strong>视图</strong> (Views)</li>\n<li>嵌套变换：D → T → V → C/L/S（Camera/Light/Screen）</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Mackinlay 自动化准则（Mackinlay 1986）</strong></p>\n<p>对每种数据类型，自动选&quot;量化准确性最高&quot;的视觉通道：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>数值型 → 位置（量化误差最小）</li>\n<li>有序型 → 长度、密度</li>\n<li>类别型 → 色调、形状</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>van Wijk 反馈模型（van Wijk 2005）</strong></p>\n<p>强调<strong>交互反馈循环</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"text\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">Text</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code>View ⇆ Filter ⇆ Param ⇆ Other Views</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-2-1-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① SVG 流程图节点</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>标记要点</strong>：SVG <code>&lt;marker&gt;</code> + <code>marker-end</code> 定义箭头；D3 classed() 做状态切换。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 1. 用 &lt;defs&gt; + &lt;marker&gt; 定义箭头\nsvg.append(&quot;defs&quot;).append(&quot;marker&quot;)\n   .attr(&quot;id&quot;, &quot;arrowhead&quot;)\n   .attr(&quot;refX&quot;, 8)            // 箭头位置校准\n   .attr(&quot;orient&quot;, &quot;auto&quot;)      // 跟随线方向旋转\n   .append(&quot;path&quot;).attr(&quot;d&quot;, &quot;M0,-5L10,0L0,5&quot;);\n\n// 2. 用 marker-end 引用箭头\nsvg.append(&quot;line&quot;)\n   .attr(&quot;marker-end&quot;, &quot;url(#arrowhead)&quot;)  // 把箭头&quot;装&quot;到线段末端\n   .attr(&quot;x1&quot;, x1).attr(&quot;y1&quot;, y)\n   .attr(&quot;x2&quot;, x2).attr(&quot;y2&quot;, y);\n\n// 3. classed 状态管理（关键）\nsvg.selectAll(&quot;.node&quot;).classed(&quot;selected&quot;, n =&gt; n.id === d.id);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>marker-end=&quot;url(#arrowhead)&quot;</code> 是 SVG 引用的方式 —— 用 URL 引用 <code>&lt;defs&gt;</code> 里定义的形状。</li>\n<li><code>classed(&quot;selected&quot;, predicate)</code> 接收布尔函数，一次性切换所有节点状态，<strong>比手动 forEach 简洁</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-1-h4\" class=\"blk blk--note\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--note\">小结</span><span class=\"blk__text\">教学要点</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>三个模型描述同一件事的不同侧面</strong><ul>\n<li>Card 给&quot;管道&quot;、Mackinlay 给&quot;自动决策&quot;、van Wijk 给&quot;反馈环&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>是叠加关系，不是冲突关系</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-2-1-h1","text":"你的原案例","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-2-1-h2","text":"嵌入的理论","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-2-1-h3","text":"① SVG 流程图节点","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-1-h4","text":"教学要点","kind":"note"}],"text":"你的原案例 3 个可视化流程模型： 参考 Card 1999 模型绘制流程图（Box Flowcharts） Mackinlay 自动化准则 van Wijk 模型（含交互反馈） 原图是一张概念图。本节课用 D3 重画这张概念图，每个节点点击后展开在三个模型中的对应细节。 嵌入的理论 Card 数据流模型（Card, Mackinlay & Shneiderman, 1999） 数据可视化的\"管道\"： 原始数据 (Raw Data) → 数据表 (Data Tables) → 视觉结构 (Visual Structure) → 视图 (Views) 嵌套变换：D → T → V → C/L/S（Camera/Light/Screen） Mackinlay 自动化准则（Mackinlay 1986） 对每种数据类型，自动选\"量化准确性最高\"的视觉通道： 数值型 → 位置（量化误差最小） 有序型 → 长度、密度 类别型 → 色调、形状 van Wijk 反馈模型（van Wijk 2005） 强调交互反馈循环： Text复制 View ⇆ Filter ⇆ Param ⇆ Other Views 代码① SVG 流程图节点 ⭐ 标记要点：SVG <marker> + marker-end 定义箭头；D3 classed() 做状态切换。 JavaScript复制 // 1. 用 <defs> + <marker> 定义箭头 svg.append(\"defs\").append(\"marker\") .attr(\"id\", \"arrowhead\") .attr(\"refX\", 8) // 箭头位置校准 .attr(\"orient\", \"auto\") // 跟随线方向旋转 .append(\"path\").attr(\"d\", \"M0,-5L10,0L0,5\"); // 2. 用 marker-end 引用箭头 svg.append(\"line\") .attr(\"marker-end\", \"url(#arrowhead)\") // 把箭头\"装\"到线段末端 .attr(\"x1\", x1).attr(\"y1\", y) .attr(\"x2\", x2).attr(\"y2\", y); // 3. classed 状态管理（关键） svg.selectAll(\".node\").classed(\"selected\", n => n.id === d.id); 关键点解释： marker-end=\"url(#arrowhead)\" 是 SVG 引用的方式 —— 用 URL 引用 <defs> 里定义的形状。 classed(\"selected\", predicate) 接收布尔函数，一次性切换所有节点状态，比手动 forEach 简洁。 小结教学要点 三个模型描述同一件事的不同侧面 Card 给\"管道\"、Mackinlay 给\"自动决策\"、van Wijk 给\"反馈环\" 是叠加关系，不是冲突关系","chars":1100},"en":{"title":"Data Visualization Pipeline","rawTitle":"Data Visualization Pipeline (Card · Mackinlay · van Wijk)","short":"Pipeline","subtitle":"Card's data flow, Mackinlay's automatic decisions, van Wijk's feedback loop: three models, one chain.","bigIdea":"The three models are not competitors; they are three sides of the same thing: pipeline, decision, feedback.","points":["Card: Raw Data → Data Tables → Visual Structure → Views.","Mackinlay: pick the channel with the smallest quantization error for each data type.","van Wijk: the View ⇆ Filter ⇆ Param feedback loop is the heart of interactive visualization."],"quiz":{"q":"Compared with Card's model, what does van Wijk's model emphasize most?","options":["data cleaning","visual channel ranking","the feedback loop created by user interaction"],"answer":2,"why":"van Wijk centers the back-and-forth among View, Filter, and Param. Card focuses on the data-to-view pipeline; Mackinlay focuses on channel choice."},"html":"<h3 id=\"s-2-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Your original case</span></h3>\n<p>Three visualization pipeline models:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Draw a flowchart based on the Card 1999 model (Box Flowcharts)</li>\n<li>Mackinlay&#39;s automation principles</li>\n<li>The van Wijk model (with interactive feedback)</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The original image is a concept diagram. In this lesson we redraw it with D3; clicking each node expands the corresponding details within the three models.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Embedded theory</span></h3>\n<p><strong>Card data flow model (Card, Mackinlay &amp; Shneiderman, 1999)</strong></p>\n<p>The &quot;pipeline&quot; of data visualization:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Raw Data (原始数据)</strong> → <strong>Data Tables (数据表)</strong> → <strong>Visual Structure (视觉结构)</strong> → <strong>Views (视图)</strong></li>\n<li>Nested transforms: D → T → V → C/L/S (Camera/Light/Screen)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Mackinlay automation principles (Mackinlay 1986)</strong></p>\n<p>For each data type, automatically choose the visual channel with the &quot;highest quantitative accuracy&quot;:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Numerical → position (smallest quantitative error)</li>\n<li>Ordinal → length, density</li>\n<li>Categorical → hue, shape</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>van Wijk feedback model (van Wijk 2005)</strong></p>\n<p>Emphasizes the <strong>interactive feedback loop</strong>:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"text\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">Text</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code>View ⇆ Filter ⇆ Param ⇆ Other Views</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-2-1-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ① SVG flowchart nodes</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>Key point to mark</strong>: SVG <code>&lt;marker&gt;</code> + <code>marker-end</code> define the arrowhead; D3 <code>classed()</code> handles state switching.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 1. 用 &lt;defs&gt; + &lt;marker&gt; 定义箭头\nsvg.append(&quot;defs&quot;).append(&quot;marker&quot;)\n   .attr(&quot;id&quot;, &quot;arrowhead&quot;)\n   .attr(&quot;refX&quot;, 8)            // 箭头位置校准\n   .attr(&quot;orient&quot;, &quot;auto&quot;)      // 跟随线方向旋转\n   .append(&quot;path&quot;).attr(&quot;d&quot;, &quot;M0,-5L10,0L0,5&quot;);\n\n// 2. 用 marker-end 引用箭头\nsvg.append(&quot;line&quot;)\n   .attr(&quot;marker-end&quot;, &quot;url(#arrowhead)&quot;)  // 把箭头&quot;装&quot;到线段末端\n   .attr(&quot;x1&quot;, x1).attr(&quot;y1&quot;, y)\n   .attr(&quot;x2&quot;, x2).attr(&quot;y2&quot;, y);\n\n// 3. classed 状态管理（关键）\nsvg.selectAll(&quot;.node&quot;).classed(&quot;selected&quot;, n =&gt; n.id === d.id);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Key point explanation</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>marker-end=&quot;url(#arrowhead)&quot;</code> is SVG&#39;s reference mechanism — referencing a shape defined in <code>&lt;defs&gt;</code> via URL.</li>\n<li><code>classed(&quot;selected&quot;, predicate)</code> takes a boolean function and switches the state of all nodes at once, which is <strong>cleaner than a manual forEach</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-1-h4\" class=\"blk blk--note\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--note\">Takeaway</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Teaching points</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The three models describe different facets of the same thing</strong><ul>\n<li>Card gives the &quot;pipeline&quot;, Mackinlay gives &quot;automated decisions&quot;, van Wijk gives the &quot;feedback loop&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>They are complementary, not conflicting</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-2-1-h1","text":"Your original case","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-2-1-h2","text":"Embedded theory","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-2-1-h3","text":"Key code ① SVG flowchart nodes","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-1-h4","text":"Teaching points","kind":"note"}],"text":"Your original case Three visualization pipeline models: Draw a flowchart based on the Card 1999 model (Box Flowcharts) Mackinlay&#39;s automation principles The van Wijk model (with interactive feedback) The original image is a concept diagram. In this lesson we redraw it with D3; clicking each node expands the corresponding details within the three models. Embedded theory Card data flow model (Card, Mackinlay & Shneiderman, 1999) The \"pipeline\" of data visualization: Raw Data (原始数据) → Data Tables (数据表) → Visual Structure (视觉结构) → Views (视图) Nested transforms: D → T → V → C/L/S (Camera/Light/Screen) Mackinlay automation principles (Mackinlay 1986) For each data type, automatically choose the visual channel with the \"highest quantitative accuracy\": Numerical → position (smallest quantitative error) Ordinal → length, density Categorical → hue, shape van Wijk feedback model (van Wijk 2005) Emphasizes the interactive feedback loop: TextCopy View ⇆ Filter ⇆ Param ⇆ Other Views CodeKey code ① SVG flowchart nodes ⭐ Key point to mark: SVG <marker> + marker-end define the arrowhead; D3 classed() handles state switching. JavaScriptCopy // 1. 用 <defs> + <marker> 定义箭头 svg.append(\"defs\").append(\"marker\") .attr(\"id\", \"arrowhead\") .attr(\"refX\", 8) // 箭头位置校准 .attr(\"orient\", \"auto\") // 跟随线方向旋转 .append(\"path\").attr(\"d\", \"M0,-5L10,0L0,5\"); // 2. 用 marker-end 引用箭头 svg.append(\"line\") .attr(\"marker-end\", \"url(#arrowhead)\") // 把箭头\"装\"到线段末端 .attr(\"x1\", x1).attr(\"y1\", y) .attr(\"x2\", x2).attr(\"y2\", y); // 3. classed 状态管理（关键） svg.selectAll(\".node\").classed(\"selected\", n => n.id === d.id); Key point explanation: marker-end=\"url(#arrowhead)\" is SVG&#39;s reference mechanism — referencing a shape defined in <defs> via URL. classed(\"selected\", predicate) takes a boolean function and switches the state of all nodes at once, which is cleaner than a manual forEach. TakeawayTeaching points The three models describe different facets of the same thing Card gives the \"pipeline\", Mackinlay gives \"automated decisions\", van Wijk gives the \"feedback loop\" They are complementary, not conflicting","chars":1801}},"2.2":{"id":"2.2","num":"2.2","chapter":"ch2","demo":"rollup","minutes":10,"related":["1.4","2.3"],"zh":{"title":"数据变换：原数据 → 数据表","rawTitle":"数据变换：原数据 → 数据表（d3.rollup 聚合）","short":"数据变换","subtitle":"从原始数据到数据表：清洗、聚合、连接、派生四类操作，以及双层 rollup。","bigIdea":"数据变换是流水线的「第一公里」；rollup 是「按 key 分桶、再 reduce 一次」。","points":["D 层四类操作：清洗过滤、聚合汇总、连接关联、派生衍生。","d3.rollup 返回嵌套 Map，而不是数组或对象。","视觉系统的下钻交互，通常就是 rollup + hierarchy 的组合。"],"quiz":{"q":"正则 /^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/ 里的 .+? 为什么必须非贪婪？","options":["否则会把整串都吃掉，末尾的「数字+班」没有字符可匹配","否则无法匹配中文","否则性能会变差"],"answer":0,"why":"贪婪的 .+ 会先吃掉整个字符串，导致末尾的 \\d+班 无法匹配或回溯出错；非贪婪让中间部分尽可能短，把结尾留给「数字+班」。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>在流程中的位置</strong>：Card 1999 数据流模型第一段箭头「原始数据 → 数据表」。这是 <strong>数据变换（Data Transformation）</strong>。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-2-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">你的原案例</span></h3>\n<p>用新生数据按&quot;专业 / 班级&quot;做 <strong>rollup 分桶聚合</strong>。\n你演示的核心是 d3.rollup 的链式调用 —— 一个函数完成多维度分组。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__text\">嵌入的理论</span></h3>\n<p><strong>理论补丁：数据变换的四大操作（Card 1999 D 层）</strong></p>\n<p>从「原始数据」到「数据表」，D 层做四类操作：</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>操作</th>\n<th>做什么</th>\n<th>D3 实现</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>清洗 / 过滤</td>\n<td>去缺失、去异常、筛选满足条件的行</td>\n<td><code>.filter()</code>、<code>d3.csv(row)</code> 回调</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>聚合 / 汇总</td>\n<td>按 key 分组，把同组归约为一个值</td>\n<td><code>d3.rollup()</code>、<code>d3.group()</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>连接 / 关联</td>\n<td>按键把两张表拼起来</td>\n<td><code>d3.map</code> + 手动索引</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>派生 / 衍生</td>\n<td>由已有列算出新列（如&quot;班级&quot;→&quot;专业&quot;）</td>\n<td>row 回调里算一个新字段</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>本节演示的 rollup 聚合属于&quot;聚合&quot;这一行</strong>。读懂这张表，你才知道数据变换是整个流水线的&quot;第一公里&quot;。</p>\n<p><strong>d3.rollup 是&quot;按 key 分桶、再 reduce 一次&quot;的函数式组合</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const result = d3.rollup(\n  data,                    // 输入数组\n  v =&gt; v.length,           // reducer\n  d =&gt; d.major,            // key1（外层）\n  d =&gt; d.class             // key2（内层）\n);</code></pre>\n</div><p>它返回 <strong><code>Map</code></strong>（不是数组、不是对象）：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>遍历用 <code>for ([k, v] of m)</code> 或 <code>m.entries()</code></li>\n<li>嵌套 rollup 出嵌套 Map</li>\n<li>与 <code>d3.group</code> 的差别：rollup 把组内数据归约成<strong>一个值</strong>，group 保留<strong>原数组</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>OLAP 切片/切块/钻取</strong>（Codd 1993）</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>OLAP 操作</th>\n<th>实际对应</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>切片 (Slice)</td>\n<td><code>.filter()</code> 后 rollup</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>切块 (Dice)</td>\n<td>多 key rollup</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>钻取 (Drill)</td>\n<td>嵌套 rollup + 递归展开</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>教学要点</strong>：可视化系统的&quot;下钻交互&quot;通常背后就是 rollup + hierarchy 的组合。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-2-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① 双层 rollup</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>标记要点</strong>：d3.rollup 的 keys 参数是 rest 参数（...keys）。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const nested = d3.rollup(\n  students,\n  v =&gt; v.length,           // 每组聚合为单一值（这里是 count）\n  d =&gt; d.major,            // 外层 key\n  d =&gt; d.class             // 内层 key（rest 参数，可继续加）\n);\n\nfor (const [major, inner] of nested) {\n  for (const [cls, count] of inner) {\n    console.log(major, cls, count);\n  }\n}</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-2-2-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② 用正则提取专业</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>标记要点</strong>：正则 <code>/^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/</code> —— <code>.+?</code> 是<strong>非贪婪</strong>匹配。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const data = await d3.csv(&quot;./data/newstudent.csv&quot;, d =&gt; {\n  const cls = d[&quot;班级&quot;].trim();\n  const m = cls.match(/^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/);  // 中间非贪婪 + 末尾&quot;数字+班&quot;\n  return {\n    id:    +d[&quot;序号&quot;],\n    name:  d[&quot;姓名&quot;].trim(),\n    class: cls,\n    major: m ? m[1] : cls,  // &quot;软件工程1班&quot; → &quot;软件工程&quot;\n  };\n});</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>.+?</code> 是<strong>非贪婪</strong>匹配 —— 让中间尽可能短、末尾留给 <code>\\d+班</code></li>\n<li>没这个非贪婪：<code>.+</code> 会把整串都匹配走，<code>m[1]</code> 就是 undefined</li>\n<li><strong>这类正则坑学生常踩，必须掌握</strong></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-2-2-h1","text":"你的原案例","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-2-2-h2","text":"嵌入的理论","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-2-2-h3","text":"① 双层 rollup","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-2-h4","text":"② 用正则提取专业","kind":"code"}],"text":"在流程中的位置：Card 1999 数据流模型第一段箭头「原始数据 → 数据表」。这是 数据变换（Data Transformation）。 你的原案例 用新生数据按\"专业 / 班级\"做 rollup 分桶聚合。 你演示的核心是 d3.rollup 的链式调用 —— 一个函数完成多维度分组。 嵌入的理论 理论补丁：数据变换的四大操作（Card 1999 D 层） 从「原始数据」到「数据表」，D 层做四类操作： 操作 做什么 D3 实现 清洗 / 过滤 去缺失、去异常、筛选满足条件的行 .filter()、d3.csv(row) 回调 聚合 / 汇总 按 key 分组，把同组归约为一个值 d3.rollup()、d3.group() 连接 / 关联 按键把两张表拼起来 d3.map + 手动索引 派生 / 衍生 由已有列算出新列（如\"班级\"→\"专业\"） row 回调里算一个新字段 本节演示的 rollup 聚合属于\"聚合\"这一行。读懂这张表，你才知道数据变换是整个流水线的\"第一公里\"。 d3.rollup 是\"按 key 分桶、再 reduce 一次\"的函数式组合： JavaScript复制 const result = d3.rollup( data, // 输入数组 v => v.length, // reducer d => d.major, // key1（外层） d => d.class // key2（内层） ); 它返回 Map（不是数组、不是对象）： 遍历用 for ([k, v] of m) 或 m.entries() 嵌套 rollup 出嵌套 Map 与 d3.group 的差别：rollup 把组内数据归约成一个值，group 保留原数组 OLAP 切片/切块/钻取（Codd 1993） OLAP 操作 实际对应 切片 (Slice) .filter() 后 rollup 切块 (Dice) 多 key rollup 钻取 (Drill) 嵌套 rollup + 递归展开 教学要点：可视化系统的\"下钻交互\"通常背后就是 rollup + hierarchy 的组合。 代码① 双层 rollup ⭐ 标记要点：d3.rollup 的 keys 参数是 rest 参数（...keys）。 JavaScript复制 const nested = d3.rollup( students, v => v.length, // 每组聚合为单一值（这里是 count） d => d.major, // 外层 key d => d.class // 内层 key（rest 参数，可继续加） ); for (const [major, inner] of nested) { for (const [cls, count] of inner) { console.log(major, cls, count); } } 代码② 用正则提取专业 ⭐ 标记要点：正则 /^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/ —— .+? 是非贪婪匹配。 JavaScript复制 const data = await d3.csv(\"./data/newstudent.csv\", d => { const cls = d[\"班级\"].trim(); const m = cls.match(/^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/); // 中间非贪婪 + 末尾\"数字+班\" return { id: +d[\"序号\"], name: d[\"姓名\"].trim(), class: cls, major: m ? m[1] : cls, // \"软件工程1班\" → \"软件工程\" }; }); 关键点解释： .+? 是非贪婪匹配 —— 让中间尽可能短、末尾留给 \\d+班 没这个非贪婪：.+ 会把整串都匹配走，m[1] 就是 undefined 这类正则坑学生常踩，必须掌握","chars":1392},"en":{"title":"Data Transformation: Raw → Data Table","rawTitle":"Data Transformation: Raw → Data Table (d3.rollup aggregation)","short":"Data Transform","subtitle":"From raw data to a data table: clean, aggregate, join, derive, plus nested rollup.","bigIdea":"Data transformation is the first mile of the pipeline; rollup buckets by key and reduces once.","points":["Four D-layer operations: clean/filter, aggregate, join, derive.","d3.rollup returns nested Maps, not arrays or plain objects.","Drill-down interactions are usually rollup plus hierarchy."],"quiz":{"q":"In /^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/, why must .+? be non-greedy?","options":["Otherwise it consumes the whole string and the trailing digits + class cannot match","Otherwise Chinese characters cannot match","Otherwise performance degrades"],"answer":0,"why":"A greedy .+ eats the entire string first, so the trailing \\d+班 has nothing left or backtracks incorrectly. Non-greedy keeps the middle short and reserves the ending."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Where this sits in the pipeline</strong>: Card 1999 data-flow model, first arrow &quot;raw data → data table&quot;. This is <strong>Data Transformation</strong>.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-2-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Your original case</span></h3>\n<p>Use freshman data to perform <strong>rollup bucketing aggregation</strong> by &quot;major / class&quot;.\nThe core of your demo is d3.rollup&#39;s chained calls — one function completes multi-dimensional grouping.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Embedded theory</span></h3>\n<p><strong>Theory patch: the four operations of data transformation (Card 1999, D layer)</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n<th>D3 implementation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Clean / filter</td>\n<td>Remove missing/outliers; keep rows matching a condition</td>\n<td><code>.filter()</code>, <code>d3.csv(row)</code> callback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Aggregate</td>\n<td>Group by key, reduce each group to one value</td>\n<td><code>d3.rollup()</code>, <code>d3.group()</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Join</td>\n<td>Combine two tables by key</td>\n<td><code>d3.map</code> + manual indexing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Derive</td>\n<td>Compute a new column from existing ones (e.g., &quot;class&quot; → &quot;major&quot;)</td>\n<td>compute a new field in the row callback</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>The rollup aggregation demonstrated here belongs to the &quot;aggregate&quot; row.</strong> Reading this table, you realize data transformation is the &quot;first kilometer&quot; of the whole pipeline.</p>\n<p><strong>d3.rollup is a functional composition of &quot;bucket by key, then reduce once&quot;</strong>:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const result = d3.rollup(\n  data,                    // 输入数组\n  v =&gt; v.length,           // reducer\n  d =&gt; d.major,            // key1（外层）\n  d =&gt; d.class             // key2（内层）\n);</code></pre>\n</div><p>It returns a <strong><code>Map</code></strong> (not an array, not an object):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Iterate with <code>for ([k, v] of m)</code> or <code>m.entries()</code></li>\n<li>Nested rollup produces a nested Map</li>\n<li>Difference from <code>d3.group</code>: rollup reduces the in-group data into <strong>a single value</strong>, while group preserves the <strong>original array</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>OLAP slice / dice / drill (Codd 1993)</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>OLAP operation</th>\n<th>Actual equivalent</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Slice (切片)</td>\n<td><code>.filter()</code> then rollup</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dice (切块)</td>\n<td>multi-key rollup</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Drill (钻取)</td>\n<td>nested rollup + recursive expand</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>Teaching point</strong>: The &quot;drill-down interaction&quot; in visualization systems is usually backed by a combination of rollup + hierarchy.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-2-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ① Two-level rollup</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>Key point to mark</strong>: d3.rollup&#39;s keys parameter is a rest parameter (...keys).</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const nested = d3.rollup(\n  students,\n  v =&gt; v.length,           // 每组聚合为单一值（这里是 count）\n  d =&gt; d.major,            // 外层 key\n  d =&gt; d.class             // 内层 key（rest 参数，可继续加）\n);\n\nfor (const [major, inner] of nested) {\n  for (const [cls, count] of inner) {\n    console.log(major, cls, count);\n  }\n}</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-2-2-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ② Extract major with regex</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>Key point to mark</strong>: regex <code>/^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/</code> — <code>.+?</code> is a <strong>non-greedy</strong> match.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const data = await d3.csv(&quot;./data/newstudent.csv&quot;, d =&gt; {\n  const cls = d[&quot;班级&quot;].trim();\n  const m = cls.match(/^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/);  // 中间非贪婪 + 末尾&quot;数字+班&quot;\n  return {\n    id:    +d[&quot;序号&quot;],\n    name:  d[&quot;姓名&quot;].trim(),\n    class: cls,\n    major: m ? m[1] : cls,  // &quot;软件工程1班&quot; → &quot;软件工程&quot;\n  };\n});</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Key point explanation</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>.+?</code> is a <strong>non-greedy</strong> match — keeps the middle as short as possible, leaving the end for <code>\\d+班</code></li>\n<li>Without this non-greedy match: <code>.+</code> would consume the entire string, and <code>m[1]</code> would be undefined</li>\n<li><strong>Students often fall into this regex pitfall — it must be mastered</strong></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-2-2-h1","text":"Your original case","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-2-2-h2","text":"Embedded theory","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-2-2-h3","text":"Key code ① Two-level rollup","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-2-h4","text":"Key code ② Extract major with regex","kind":"code"}],"text":"Where this sits in the pipeline: Card 1999 data-flow model, first arrow \"raw data → data table\". This is Data Transformation. Your original case Use freshman data to perform rollup bucketing aggregation by \"major / class\". The core of your demo is d3.rollup&#39;s chained calls — one function completes multi-dimensional grouping. Embedded theory Theory patch: the four operations of data transformation (Card 1999, D layer) Operation What it does D3 implementation Clean / filter Remove missing/outliers; keep rows matching a condition .filter(), d3.csv(row) callback Aggregate Group by key, reduce each group to one value d3.rollup(), d3.group() Join Combine two tables by key d3.map + manual indexing Derive Compute a new column from existing ones (e.g., \"class\" → \"major\") compute a new field in the row callback The rollup aggregation demonstrated here belongs to the \"aggregate\" row. Reading this table, you realize data transformation is the \"first kilometer\" of the whole pipeline. d3.rollup is a functional composition of \"bucket by key, then reduce once\": JavaScriptCopy const result = d3.rollup( data, // 输入数组 v => v.length, // reducer d => d.major, // key1（外层） d => d.class // key2（内层） ); It returns a Map (not an array, not an object): Iterate with for ([k, v] of m) or m.entries() Nested rollup produces a nested Map Difference from d3.group: rollup reduces the in-group data into a single value, while group preserves the original array OLAP slice / dice / drill (Codd 1993) OLAP operation Actual equivalent Slice (切片) .filter() then rollup Dice (切块) multi-key rollup Drill (钻取) nested rollup + recursive expand Teaching point: The \"drill-down interaction\" in visualization systems is usually backed by a combination of rollup + hierarchy. CodeKey code ① Two-level rollup ⭐ Key point to mark: d3.rollup&#39;s keys parameter is a rest parameter (...keys). JavaScriptCopy const nested = d3.rollup( students, v => v.length, // 每组聚合为单一值（这里是 count） d => d.major, // 外层 key d => d.class // 内层 key（rest 参数，可继续加） ); for (const [major, inner] of nested) { for (const [cls, count] of inner) { console.log(major, cls, count); } } CodeKey code ② Extract major with regex ⭐ Key point to mark: regex /^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/ — .+? is a non-greedy match. JavaScriptCopy const data = await d3.csv(\"./data/newstudent.csv\", d => { const cls = d[\"班级\"].trim(); const m = cls.match(/^(.+?)(\\d+班)$/); // 中间非贪婪 + 末尾\"数字+班\" return { id: +d[\"序号\"], name: d[\"姓名\"].trim(), class: cls, major: m ? m[1] : cls, // \"软件工程1班\" → \"软件工程\" }; }); Key point explanation: .+? is a non-greedy match — keeps the middle as short as possible, leaving the end for \\d+班 Without this non-greedy match: .+ would consume the entire string, and m[1] would be undefined Students often fall into this regex pitfall — it must be mastered","chars":2341}},"2.3":{"id":"2.3","num":"2.3","chapter":"ch2","demo":"tree","minutes":11,"related":["2.1","2.2","1.3"],"zh":{"title":"视觉映射：数据表 → 视觉结构","rawTitle":"视觉映射：数据表 → 视觉结构（Reingold-Tilford + 通道理论）","short":"视觉映射","subtitle":"数据表 → 视觉结构：Reingold-Tilford 树布局，以及 Mackinlay 通道排名。","bigIdea":"树布局本质上是用「位置」通道编码层级：父在上、子在下，兄弟不重叠。","points":["Reingold-Tilford 三遍遍历：算子树宽度、分配绝对坐标、修复线程。","d3.tree 的 x 是深度方向、y 是水平方向，横向树要 swap。","separation 控制兄弟与非兄弟的间距，是树「呼吸感」的来源。"],"quiz":{"q":"横向树里，d3.tree 的 x / y 分别对应屏幕的哪个方向？","options":["x 水平、y 垂直，和普通坐标一样","x 是深度方向（垂直），y 是水平方向","x 是半径、y 是角度"],"answer":1,"why":"d3.tree 把 x 当作同层展开方向、y 当作深度方向；画横向树时用 linkHorizontal 并交换坐标，即 x=d.y、y=d.x。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>在流程中的位置</strong>：接上节 2.2，我们有了&quot;数据表&quot;。这是第二段箭头「数据表 → 视觉结构」，即 <strong>视觉映射（Visual Mapping）</strong>。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-2-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">你的原案例</span></h3>\n<p>你的 4.2 节提到&quot;树形结构可视化&quot;。本节展开<strong>树布局算法</strong>原理 —— 拿到层级数据后，怎么把节点摆到屏幕上不打架？本质上是用「位置通道」做视觉映射。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__text\">嵌入的理论</span></h3>\n<p><strong>理论核心：什么是视觉通道？Mackinlay 的排名（图 1）</strong></p>\n<p>视觉通道是&quot;把数据编码到视觉元素上&quot;的载体：位置、长度、面积、角度、颜色、形状、纹理。<strong>Mackinlay 1986</strong> 给出经典排名：对<em>不同数据类型</em>，各通道的量化精确度不同。</p>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>对 Quantitative / Ordinal / Nominal 三类数据，各通道量化精确度排序。位置（Position）永远最准。</p>\n</blockquote><ul>\n<li><strong>位置（Position）</strong>：三种数据类型都是第一</li>\n<li><strong>定量数据</strong>：长度 → 角度 → 斜率 → 面积（长条图比面积图准）</li>\n<li><strong>名义数据</strong>：位置 → 色调（hue）→ 纹理 → 连接 → 形状</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>理论核心：图元（marks）与视觉通道（图 2、图 3）</strong></p>\n<p>视觉结构由 <strong>图元（mark）</strong> 打底：点（Point）、线（Line）、面（Area）。再通过 <strong>通道</strong> 做记号：位置、颜色、形状、倾斜、大小。</p>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"></blockquote><p><strong>理论核心：两类通道 —— 幅度 vs 标识（图 4、图 5）</strong></p>\n<p>按&quot;能不能表达量的多少&quot;，通道分两类：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>幅度通道（Magnitude）</strong>：表达<em>有序/定量</em>属性（共用尺度位置最准，长度/倾斜/面积次之，亮度/饱和度/体积最弱）</li>\n<li><strong>标识通道（Identity）</strong>：表达<em>类别</em>属性（空间区域、色调、运动、形状 —— 能区分&quot;不同类&quot;但分不出&quot;谁多谁少&quot;）</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"></blockquote><p><strong>本节案例的落点</strong>：树布局（Reingold-Tilford）本质上就是一种<strong>视觉映射</strong> —— 用<em>位置通道</em>把层级关系编码成&quot;父在上、子在下的树&quot;。</p>\n<p><strong>Reingold-Tilford 算法（1981，至今仍是 d3.tree() 的核心）</strong></p>\n<p>核心思路（3 遍遍历）：</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>第一遍（自底向上）：</strong> 对每个父节点，计算其左右子树&quot;占用多少横向空间&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>第二遍（自顶向下）：</strong> 给每个节点分配<strong>绝对 x 坐标</strong>（保证兄弟节点紧贴父节点中线且不重叠）</li>\n<li><strong>第三遍：</strong> 处理&quot;线程&quot;（threads）—— 修复子节点跨父中线时的对齐</li>\n</ol>\n<p>复杂度：<strong>O(n)</strong> 时间。</p>\n<p><strong>d3-hierarchy 模块全家桶：</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>API</th>\n<th>用途</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><code>hierarchy(data)</code></td>\n<td>嵌套 data → 计算 parent/children/depth</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>tree().size([h, w])</code></td>\n<td>Reingold-Tilford 算法，左右布局</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cluster().size([h, w])</code></td>\n<td>所有叶子对齐到同一深度</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>treemap().tile(...)</code></td>\n<td>面积布局（slice-and-dice / squarified）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>pack().radius(...)</code></td>\n<td>circle packing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>partition().size([h, w])</code></td>\n<td>icicle / sunburst</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-2-3-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① hierarchy + tree 三步走</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>标记要点</strong>：tree.x 是深度方向、tree.y 是水平方向 —— 横向树 swap 坐标轴。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 1. hierarchy：嵌套 JSON → parent/children/depth\nconst root = d3.hierarchy(rootData);\n\n// 2. tree layout：x/y 坐标\nconst treeLayout = d3.tree().size([360, 720]);\nconst treeData = treeLayout(root);\n\n// 3. links：path 走 linkHorizontal\ng.selectAll(&quot;.link&quot;).data(treeData.links()).join(&quot;path&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;d&quot;, d3.linkHorizontal().x(d =&gt; d.y).y(d =&gt; d.x));  // ⭐ swap\n\n// 4. nodes\nconst ng = g.selectAll(&quot;.node&quot;).data(treeData.descendants()).join(&quot;g&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;transform&quot;, d =&gt; `translate(${d.y}, ${d.x})`);  // ⭐ swap\n\nng.append(&quot;circle&quot;).attr(&quot;r&quot;, 5);\nng.append(&quot;text&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;text-anchor&quot;, d =&gt; d.children ? &quot;end&quot; : &quot;start&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;x&quot;, d =&gt; d.children ? -8 : 8)\n  .text(d =&gt; d.data.name);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>treeData.x</code> 是<strong>深度方向</strong>（垂直），<code>treeData.y</code> 是<strong>水平方向</strong></li>\n<li>所以 <code>linkHorizontal</code> 用 <code>x=d.y, y=d.x</code> —— 横向 swap</li>\n<li><strong>这种&quot;x 轴走 y、y 轴走 x&quot;的 swap 是横向树特有的</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-3-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② separation</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>标记要点</strong>：separation 接收函数，返回 <code>[node, parent]</code> 之间的间隔倍数。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const treeLayout = d3.tree()\n  .size([360, 720])\n  .separation((a, b) =&gt; (a.parent === b.parent ? 1 : 2));\n                              //   ↑ 兄弟节点紧贴        ↑ 非兄弟至少隔 2 倍</code></pre>\n</div><p><code>0.5</code> → 全部挤一起；<code>2.0</code> → 树变宽。Demo 里有 slider 实时调。</p>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-2-3-h1","text":"你的原案例","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-2-3-h2","text":"嵌入的理论","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-2-3-h3","text":"① hierarchy + tree 三步走","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-3-h4","text":"② separation","kind":"code"}],"text":"在流程中的位置：接上节 2.2，我们有了\"数据表\"。这是第二段箭头「数据表 → 视觉结构」，即 视觉映射（Visual Mapping）。 你的原案例 你的 4.2 节提到\"树形结构可视化\"。本节展开树布局算法原理 —— 拿到层级数据后，怎么把节点摆到屏幕上不打架？本质上是用「位置通道」做视觉映射。 嵌入的理论 理论核心：什么是视觉通道？Mackinlay 的排名（图 1） 视觉通道是\"把数据编码到视觉元素上\"的载体：位置、长度、面积、角度、颜色、形状、纹理。Mackinlay 1986 给出经典排名：对不同数据类型，各通道的量化精确度不同。 对 Quantitative / Ordinal / Nominal 三类数据，各通道量化精确度排序。位置（Position）永远最准。 位置（Position）：三种数据类型都是第一 定量数据：长度 → 角度 → 斜率 → 面积（长条图比面积图准） 名义数据：位置 → 色调（hue）→ 纹理 → 连接 → 形状 理论核心：图元（marks）与视觉通道（图 2、图 3） 视觉结构由 图元（mark） 打底：点（Point）、线（Line）、面（Area）。再通过 通道 做记号：位置、颜色、形状、倾斜、大小。 理论核心：两类通道 —— 幅度 vs 标识（图 4、图 5） 按\"能不能表达量的多少\"，通道分两类： 幅度通道（Magnitude）：表达有序/定量属性（共用尺度位置最准，长度/倾斜/面积次之，亮度/饱和度/体积最弱） 标识通道（Identity）：表达类别属性（空间区域、色调、运动、形状 —— 能区分\"不同类\"但分不出\"谁多谁少\"） 本节案例的落点：树布局（Reingold-Tilford）本质上就是一种视觉映射 —— 用位置通道把层级关系编码成\"父在上、子在下的树\"。 Reingold-Tilford 算法（1981，至今仍是 d3.tree() 的核心） 核心思路（3 遍遍历）： 第一遍（自底向上）： 对每个父节点，计算其左右子树\"占用多少横向空间\" 第二遍（自顶向下）： 给每个节点分配绝对 x 坐标（保证兄弟节点紧贴父节点中线且不重叠） 第三遍： 处理\"线程\"（threads）—— 修复子节点跨父中线时的对齐 复杂度：O(n) 时间。 d3-hierarchy 模块全家桶： API 用途 hierarchy(data) 嵌套 data → 计算 parent/children/depth tree().size([h, w]) Reingold-Tilford 算法，左右布局 cluster().size([h, w]) 所有叶子对齐到同一深度 treemap().tile(...) 面积布局（slice-and-dice / squarified） pack().radius(...) circle packing partition().size([h, w]) icicle / sunburst 代码① hierarchy + tree 三步走 ⭐ 标记要点：tree.x 是深度方向、tree.y 是水平方向 —— 横向树 swap 坐标轴。 JavaScript复制 // 1. hierarchy：嵌套 JSON → parent/children/depth const root = d3.hierarchy(rootData); // 2. tree layout：x/y 坐标 const treeLayout = d3.tree().size([360, 720]); const treeData = treeLayout(root); // 3. links：path 走 linkHorizontal g.selectAll(\".link\").data(treeData.links()).join(\"path\") .attr(\"d\", d3.linkHorizontal().x(d => d.y).y(d => d.x)); // ⭐ swap // 4. nodes const ng = g.selectAll(\".node\").data(treeData.descendants()).join(\"g\") .attr(\"transform\", d => `translate(${d.y}, ${d.x})`); // ⭐ swap ng.append(\"circle\").attr(\"r\", 5); ng.append(\"text\") .attr(\"text-anchor\", d => d.children ? \"end\" : \"start\") .attr(\"x\", d => d.children ? -8 : 8) .text(d => d.data.name); 关键点解释： treeData.x 是深度方向（垂直），treeData.y 是水平方向 所以 linkHorizontal 用 x=d.y, y=d.x —— 横向 swap 这种\"x 轴走 y、y 轴走 x\"的 swap 是横向树特有的 代码② separation ⭐ 标记要点：separation 接收函数，返回 [node, parent] 之间的间隔倍数。 JavaScript复制 const treeLayout = d3.tree() .size([360, 720]) .separation((a, b) => (a.parent === b.parent ? 1 : 2)); // ↑ 兄弟节点紧贴 ↑ 非兄弟至少隔 2 倍 0.5 → 全部挤一起；2.0 → 树变宽。Demo 里有 slider 实时调。","chars":2113},"en":{"title":"Visual Mapping: Data → Visual Structure","rawTitle":"Visual Mapping: Data → Visual Structure (Reingold-Tilford + channel theory)","short":"Visual Mapping","subtitle":"Data table → visual structure: Reingold-Tilford tree layout and Mackinlay's channel ranking.","bigIdea":"Tree layout is position encoding hierarchy: parents above, children below, siblings apart.","points":["Reingold-Tilford: subtree widths, absolute coordinates, thread repair.","In d3.tree, x is the breadth direction and y is depth; horizontal trees swap them.","separation controls sibling vs non-sibling spacing and gives the tree room to breathe."],"quiz":{"q":"In a horizontal tree, what do d3.tree's x / y map to on screen?","options":["x horizontal, y vertical, like normal coordinates","x is depth (vertical), y is horizontal","x is radius, y is angle"],"answer":1,"why":"d3.tree treats x as the breadth direction and y as depth. Horizontal trees use linkHorizontal and swap coordinates: x=d.y, y=d.x."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Where this sits in the pipeline</strong>: following 2.2, we now have a &quot;data table&quot;. This is the second arrow, &quot;data table → visual structure&quot;, i.e. <strong>Visual Mapping</strong>.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-2-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Your original case</span></h3>\n<p>Section 4.2 mentioned &quot;tree-structure visualization&quot;. This section expands on the <strong>tree layout algorithm</strong> — once you have hierarchical data, how do you place nodes on screen without collisions? Essentially it uses the &quot;position channel&quot; to do visual mapping.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Embedded theory</span></h3>\n<p><strong>Theory core: what is a visual channel? Mackinlay&#39;s ranking (Figure 1)</strong></p>\n<p>A visual channel is the carrier that &quot;encodes data onto a visual element&quot;: position, length, area, angle, color, shape, texture. <strong>Mackinlay (1986)</strong> gave the classic ranking: for <em>different data types</em>, the quantitative accuracy of each channel differs.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>For Quantitative / Ordinal / Nominal data, the quantitative-accuracy ordering of each channel. Position is always the most accurate.</p>\n</blockquote><ul>\n<li><strong>Position</strong>: ranks #1 for all three data types</li>\n<li><strong>Quantitative data</strong>: length → angle → slope → area (bar charts beat area charts)</li>\n<li><strong>Nominal data</strong>: position → hue → texture → connection → shape</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Theory core: marks and visual channels (Figures 2 &amp; 3)</strong></p>\n<p>The visual structure is built on <strong>marks</strong>: Point, Line, Area. These marks are &quot;marked up&quot; through <strong>channels</strong>: position, color, shape, tilt, size.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"></blockquote><p><strong>Theory core: two channel classes — Magnitude vs Identity (Figures 4 &amp; 5)</strong></p>\n<p>By &quot;whether it can express magnitude,&quot; channels split into two classes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Magnitude channels</strong>: express <em>ordered / quantitative</em> attributes (position on a common scale is best; length / tilt / area next; luminance / saturation / volume weakest)</li>\n<li><strong>Identity channels</strong>: express <em>categorical</em> attributes (spatial region, hue, motion, shape — distinguish &quot;different classes&quot; but cannot rank &quot;more vs less&quot;)</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"></blockquote><p><strong>Where this lesson lands</strong>: tree layout (Reingold-Tilford) is essentially a <strong>visual mapping</strong> — it uses the <em>position channel</em> to encode hierarchy as &quot;parent above, children below&quot;.</p>\n<p><strong>Reingold-Tilford algorithm (1981, still the core of d3.tree() today)</strong></p>\n<p>Core idea (3 passes):</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>First pass (bottom-up):</strong> for each parent node, compute how much horizontal space its left and right subtrees &quot;occupy&quot;</li>\n<li><strong>Second pass (top-down):</strong> assign an <strong>absolute x coordinate</strong> to each node (ensuring sibling nodes stay tight to the parent&#39;s midline and do not overlap)</li>\n<li><strong>Third pass:</strong> handle &quot;threads&quot; — fix alignment when child nodes cross the parent&#39;s midline</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Complexity: <strong>O(n)</strong> time.</p>\n<p><strong>d3-hierarchy module full toolkit:</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>API</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><code>hierarchy(data)</code></td>\n<td>nested data → compute parent/children/depth</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>tree().size([h, w])</code></td>\n<td>Reingold-Tilford algorithm, left-right layout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cluster().size([h, w])</code></td>\n<td>align all leaves to the same depth</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>treemap().tile(...)</code></td>\n<td>area layout (slice-and-dice / squarified)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>pack().radius(...)</code></td>\n<td>circle packing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>partition().size([h, w])</code></td>\n<td>icicle / sunburst</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-2-3-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ① hierarchy + tree three steps</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>Key point to mark</strong>: tree.x is the depth direction, tree.y is the horizontal direction — the horizontal tree swaps the axes.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 1. hierarchy：嵌套 JSON → parent/children/depth\nconst root = d3.hierarchy(rootData);\n\n// 2. tree layout：x/y 坐标\nconst treeLayout = d3.tree().size([360, 720]);\nconst treeData = treeLayout(root);\n\n// 3. links：path 走 linkHorizontal\ng.selectAll(&quot;.link&quot;).data(treeData.links()).join(&quot;path&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;d&quot;, d3.linkHorizontal().x(d =&gt; d.y).y(d =&gt; d.x));  // ⭐ swap\n\n// 4. nodes\nconst ng = g.selectAll(&quot;.node&quot;).data(treeData.descendants()).join(&quot;g&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;transform&quot;, d =&gt; `translate(${d.y}, ${d.x})`);  // ⭐ swap\n\nng.append(&quot;circle&quot;).attr(&quot;r&quot;, 5);\nng.append(&quot;text&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;text-anchor&quot;, d =&gt; d.children ? &quot;end&quot; : &quot;start&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;x&quot;, d =&gt; d.children ? -8 : 8)\n  .text(d =&gt; d.data.name);</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Key point explanation</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>treeData.x</code> is the <strong>depth direction</strong> (vertical), <code>treeData.y</code> is the <strong>horizontal direction</strong></li>\n<li>So <code>linkHorizontal</code> uses <code>x=d.y, y=d.x</code> — the horizontal swap</li>\n<li><strong>This &quot;x-axis takes y, y-axis takes x&quot; swap is unique to horizontal trees</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-3-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ② separation</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>Key point to mark</strong>: separation takes a function that returns the spacing multiplier between <code>[node, parent]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const treeLayout = d3.tree()\n  .size([360, 720])\n  .separation((a, b) =&gt; (a.parent === b.parent ? 1 : 2));\n                              //   ↑ siblings stay tight        ↑ non-siblings at least 2x apart</code></pre>\n</div><p><code>0.5</code> → everything squeezed together; <code>2.0</code> → the tree widens. The demo has a slider for real-time adjustment.</p>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-2-3-h1","text":"Your original case","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-2-3-h2","text":"Embedded theory","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-2-3-h3","text":"Key code ① hierarchy + tree three steps","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-3-h4","text":"Key code ② separation","kind":"code"}],"text":"Where this sits in the pipeline: following 2.2, we now have a \"data table\". This is the second arrow, \"data table → visual structure\", i.e. Visual Mapping. Your original case Section 4.2 mentioned \"tree-structure visualization\". This section expands on the tree layout algorithm — once you have hierarchical data, how do you place nodes on screen without collisions? Essentially it uses the \"position channel\" to do visual mapping. Embedded theory Theory core: what is a visual channel? Mackinlay&#39;s ranking (Figure 1) A visual channel is the carrier that \"encodes data onto a visual element\": position, length, area, angle, color, shape, texture. Mackinlay (1986) gave the classic ranking: for different data types, the quantitative accuracy of each channel differs. For Quantitative / Ordinal / Nominal data, the quantitative-accuracy ordering of each channel. Position is always the most accurate. Position: ranks #1 for all three data types Quantitative data: length → angle → slope → area (bar charts beat area charts) Nominal data: position → hue → texture → connection → shape Theory core: marks and visual channels (Figures 2 & 3) The visual structure is built on marks: Point, Line, Area. These marks are \"marked up\" through channels: position, color, shape, tilt, size. Theory core: two channel classes — Magnitude vs Identity (Figures 4 & 5) By \"whether it can express magnitude,\" channels split into two classes: Magnitude channels: express ordered / quantitative attributes (position on a common scale is best; length / tilt / area next; luminance / saturation / volume weakest) Identity channels: express categorical attributes (spatial region, hue, motion, shape — distinguish \"different classes\" but cannot rank \"more vs less\") Where this lesson lands: tree layout (Reingold-Tilford) is essentially a visual mapping — it uses the position channel to encode hierarchy as \"parent above, children below\". Reingold-Tilford algorithm (1981, still the core of d3.tree() today) Core idea (3 passes): First pass (bottom-up): for each parent node, compute how much horizontal space its left and right subtrees \"occupy\" Second pass (top-down): assign an absolute x coordinate to each node (ensuring sibling nodes stay tight to the parent&#39;s midline and do not overlap) Third pass: handle \"threads\" — fix alignment when child nodes cross the parent&#39;s midline Complexity: O(n) time. d3-hierarchy module full toolkit: API Purpose hierarchy(data) nested data → compute parent/children/depth tree().size([h, w]) Reingold-Tilford algorithm, left-right layout cluster().size([h, w]) align all leaves to the same depth treemap().tile(...) area layout (slice-and-dice / squarified) pack().radius(...) circle packing partition().size([h, w]) icicle / sunburst CodeKey code ① hierarchy + tree three steps ⭐ Key point to mark: tree.x is the depth direction, tree.y is the horizontal direction — the horizontal tree swaps the axes. JavaScriptCopy // 1. hierarchy：嵌套 JSON → parent/children/depth const root = d3.hierarchy(rootData); // 2. tree layout：x/y 坐标 const treeLayout = d3.tree().size([360, 720]); const treeData = treeLayout(root); // 3. links：path 走 linkHorizontal g.selectAll(\".link\").data(treeData.links()).join(\"path\") .attr(\"d\", d3.linkHorizontal().x(d => d.y).y(d => d.x)); // ⭐ swap // 4. nodes const ng = g.selectAll(\".node\").data(treeData.descendants()).join(\"g\") .attr(\"transform\", d => `translate(${d.y}, ${d.x})`); // ⭐ swap ng.append(\"circle\").attr(\"r\", 5); ng.append(\"text\") .attr(\"text-anchor\", d => d.children ? \"end\" : \"start\") .attr(\"x\", d => d.children ? -8 : 8) .text(d => d.data.name); Key point explanation: treeData.x is the depth direction (vertical), treeData.y is the horizontal direction So linkHorizontal uses x=d.y, y=d.x — the horizontal swap This \"x-axis takes y, y-axis takes x\" swap is unique to horizontal trees CodeKey code ② separation ⭐ Key point to mark: separation takes a function that returns the spacing multiplier between [node, parent]. JavaScriptCopy const treeLayout = d3.tree() .size([360, 720]) .separation((a, b) => (a.parent === b.parent ? 1 : 2)); // ↑ siblings stay tight ↑ non-siblings at least 2x apart 0.5 → everything squeezed together; 2.0 → the tree widens. The demo has a slider for real-time adjustment.","chars":3653}},"2.4":{"id":"2.4","num":"2.4","chapter":"ch2","demo":"events","minutes":10,"related":["1.5","2.3"],"zh":{"title":"视图渲染与用户交互","rawTitle":"视图渲染与用户交互（classed + 事件委托 + 动画 transition）","short":"渲染与交互","subtitle":"classed、事件委托、stopPropagation 与 transition：视图如何随时间与用户变化。","bigIdea":"动画不是装饰，而是「变化」在时间维上的展开；事件委托是让交互可扩展的关键。","points":["DOM 事件先捕获、再目标、后冒泡；stopPropagation 截断冒泡。","事件委托：父元素绑 1 次，用 closest 找实际目标，新增元素自动生效。","transition().duration() 让属性平滑变化；0ms 看不出过程，>1500ms 会走神。"],"quiz":{"q":"点「折叠」按钮时，为什么常常要 event.stopPropagation()？","options":["为了阻止页面刷新","为了不让点击继续冒泡，触发父级 li 的「选中」处理","为了提高动画性能"],"answer":1,"why":"折叠按钮通常在可点击的列表项内部；不阻止冒泡会同时触发折叠和选中，两个动作叠在一起让用户困惑。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>在流程中的位置</strong>：接上节 2.3，我们有了&quot;视觉结构&quot;。本节是最后两段箭头「视觉结构 → 视图」（渲染）和「视图 ↔ 用户」（交互反馈）。Card 的 V 层 + van Wijk 的反馈环都落在这里。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-2-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">你的原案例</span></h3>\n<p>原文档用了 <code>classed</code> 控制节点样式、用 <code>stopPropagation</code> 阻止冒泡。重点是<strong>把 D3 树布局输出变成可交互的 HTML 列表</strong>。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__text\">嵌入的理论</span></h3>\n<p><strong>理论补丁：动画 —— 视图渲染的&quot;时间维&quot;</strong></p>\n<p>动画（transition）不是&quot;花哨&quot;，而是视图渲染在<em>时间维</em>上的展开。D3 用 <code>.transition().duration(ms)</code> 让属性从旧值平滑过渡到新值。教学价值在 <code>duration</code> 一个参数：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>duration=0</code>：瞬间跳变，看不出&quot;变化过程&quot;</li>\n<li><code>duration=500</code>：0.5 秒过渡，看到展开/收缩/位移的流畅过程</li>\n<li><code>duration&gt;1500</code>：太慢，学生开始走神</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>本节的交互 demo 特意加了 duration 滑块</strong>，现场改变这个参数，直观看到&quot;渲染如何随时间展开&quot;。</p>\n<p><strong>DOM 事件三阶段</strong>：</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>捕获 (capturing)</strong>：window → document → ... → 目标元素（从外到内）</li>\n<li><strong>目标 (target)</strong>：目标元素本身</li>\n<li><strong>冒泡 (bubbling)</strong>：目标元素 → ... → document → window（从内到外）</li>\n</ol>\n<p>默认监听的是冒泡阶段。<code>e.stopPropagation()</code> 截断冒泡，让上层不再触发。</p>\n<p><strong>事件委托（Event Delegation）</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>问题</th>\n<th>解法</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>列表 1000 个 li 各绑 click → 慢、内存大</td>\n<td>给父元素（ul）绑 1 次 click</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>新增元素要重新绑</td>\n<td>用 <code>e.target.closest(&#39;.label&#39;)</code> 找实际点击元素</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>优势</strong>：1 个监听器代替 N 个、未来新增元素自动支持。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-4-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">① 事件委托（toggle vs select）</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>标记要点</strong>：toggle 按钮上 stopPropagation 阻止冒泡到 li 的 select 监听器。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">function buildList(liSel, d) {\n  const label = liSel.append(&quot;span&quot;).attr(&quot;class&quot;, &quot;label&quot;);\n\n  label.on(&quot;click.toggle&quot;, (event) =&gt; {\n    // ⭐ 关键 ①：阻止冒泡 —— toggle 不该触发&quot;选中&quot;\n    event.stopPropagation();\n    d.data._collapsed = !d.data._collapsed;\n    render();\n  });\n\n  liSel.on(&quot;click.select&quot;, (event) =&gt; {\n    // ⭐ 关键 ②：toggle click 已被 stopPropagation 阻断，不会到这里\n    document.querySelectorAll(&quot;li&quot;).forEach(li =&gt; li.classList.remove(&quot;selected&quot;));\n    liSel.classed(&quot;selected&quot;, true);  // D3 class 切换\n  });\n}</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>不 stopPropagation → 点 toggle 时同时触发&quot;切换折叠&quot;和&quot;选中节点&quot;，用户看着会困惑</li>\n<li>这是 DOM 事件机制的核心教学点</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-4-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">② 嵌套递归 buildList</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>标记要点</strong>：<code>selection.each()</code> + <code>d3.select(this)</code> 是 D3 与原生 DOM 互操作的关键模式。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">function render() {\n  $tree.innerHTML = &quot;&quot;;  // 全量重画（树结构变化没法增量更新）\n  const ul = d3.create(&quot;ul&quot;);\n  ul.selectAll(&quot;li&quot;).data([root]).join(&quot;li&quot;)\n    .each(function(d) { buildList(d3.select(this), d); });\n  $tree.appendChild(ul.node());\n}</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>关键点解释</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>D3 没有&quot;智能更新&quot;树结构（层级变化）的 API —— 全量重画最简单</li>\n<li><code>selection.each()</code> 配合 <code>d3.select(this)</code> 把原生元素转回 selection</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-4-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">③ D3 过渡动画（transition + duration）</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>标记要点</strong>：<code>transition + duration</code> = 让属性随时间平滑变化。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 关键：transition + duration = 让属性随时间平滑变化\nsvg.selectAll(&quot;.node&quot;)\n  .transition()                    // 进入过渡状态\n  .duration(DURATION)              // 时长（ms），滑块控制\n  .attr(&quot;transform&quot;, d =&gt; `translate(${d.y}, ${d.x})`)\n  .attr(&quot;opacity&quot;, 1);\n\n// 新节点进入时：先设 opacity=0，再过渡到 1 → 淡入效果\nng.attr(&quot;opacity&quot;, 0)\n  .transition().duration(DURATION).attr(&quot;opacity&quot;, 1);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-2-4-h6\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">代码</span><span class=\"blk__text\">④ 动画时长滑块（HTML/CSS 控制）</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"html\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">HTML</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-html\">&lt;!-- HTML 滑块：监听 input 事件即可改 DURATION --&gt;\n&lt;input id=&quot;dur&quot; type=&quot;range&quot; min=&quot;0&quot; max=&quot;1500&quot; step=&quot;50&quot; value=&quot;500&quot;&gt;\n\n&lt;!-- JS：改变 DURATION 后重放动画 --&gt;\ndocument.getElementById(&quot;dur&quot;).addEventListener(&quot;input&quot;, e =&gt; {\n  DURATION = +e.target.value;\n  render();   // 用新时长重新做一次过渡\n});</code></pre>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"s-2-4-h1","text":"你的原案例","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-2-4-h2","text":"嵌入的理论","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-2-4-h3","text":"① 事件委托（toggle vs select）","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-4-h4","text":"② 嵌套递归 buildList","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-4-h5","text":"③ D3 过渡动画（transition + duration）","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-4-h6","text":"④ 动画时长滑块（HTML/CSS 控制）","kind":"code"}],"text":"在流程中的位置：接上节 2.3，我们有了\"视觉结构\"。本节是最后两段箭头「视觉结构 → 视图」（渲染）和「视图 ↔ 用户」（交互反馈）。Card 的 V 层 + van Wijk 的反馈环都落在这里。 你的原案例 原文档用了 classed 控制节点样式、用 stopPropagation 阻止冒泡。重点是把 D3 树布局输出变成可交互的 HTML 列表。 嵌入的理论 理论补丁：动画 —— 视图渲染的\"时间维\" 动画（transition）不是\"花哨\"，而是视图渲染在时间维上的展开。D3 用 .transition().duration(ms) 让属性从旧值平滑过渡到新值。教学价值在 duration 一个参数： duration=0：瞬间跳变，看不出\"变化过程\" duration=500：0.5 秒过渡，看到展开/收缩/位移的流畅过程 duration>1500：太慢，学生开始走神 本节的交互 demo 特意加了 duration 滑块，现场改变这个参数，直观看到\"渲染如何随时间展开\"。 DOM 事件三阶段： 捕获 (capturing)：window → document → ... → 目标元素（从外到内） 目标 (target)：目标元素本身 冒泡 (bubbling)：目标元素 → ... → document → window（从内到外） 默认监听的是冒泡阶段。e.stopPropagation() 截断冒泡，让上层不再触发。 事件委托（Event Delegation）： 问题 解法 列表 1000 个 li 各绑 click → 慢、内存大 给父元素（ul）绑 1 次 click 新增元素要重新绑 用 e.target.closest(&#39;.label&#39;) 找实际点击元素 优势：1 个监听器代替 N 个、未来新增元素自动支持。 代码① 事件委托（toggle vs select） ⭐ 标记要点：toggle 按钮上 stopPropagation 阻止冒泡到 li 的 select 监听器。 JavaScript复制 function buildList(liSel, d) { const label = liSel.append(\"span\").attr(\"class\", \"label\"); label.on(\"click.toggle\", (event) => { // ⭐ 关键 ①：阻止冒泡 —— toggle 不该触发\"选中\" event.stopPropagation(); d.data._collapsed = !d.data._collapsed; render(); }); liSel.on(\"click.select\", (event) => { // ⭐ 关键 ②：toggle click 已被 stopPropagation 阻断，不会到这里 document.querySelectorAll(\"li\").forEach(li => li.classList.remove(\"selected\")); liSel.classed(\"selected\", true); // D3 class 切换 }); } 关键点解释： 不 stopPropagation → 点 toggle 时同时触发\"切换折叠\"和\"选中节点\"，用户看着会困惑 这是 DOM 事件机制的核心教学点 代码② 嵌套递归 buildList ⭐ 标记要点：selection.each() + d3.select(this) 是 D3 与原生 DOM 互操作的关键模式。 JavaScript复制 function render() { $tree.innerHTML = \"\"; // 全量重画（树结构变化没法增量更新） const ul = d3.create(\"ul\"); ul.selectAll(\"li\").data([root]).join(\"li\") .each(function(d) { buildList(d3.select(this), d); }); $tree.appendChild(ul.node()); } 关键点解释： D3 没有\"智能更新\"树结构（层级变化）的 API —— 全量重画最简单 selection.each() 配合 d3.select(this) 把原生元素转回 selection 代码③ D3 过渡动画（transition + duration） ⭐ 标记要点：transition + duration = 让属性随时间平滑变化。 JavaScript复制 // 关键：transition + duration = 让属性随时间平滑变化 svg.selectAll(\".node\") .transition() // 进入过渡状态 .duration(DURATION) // 时长（ms），滑块控制 .attr(\"transform\", d => `translate(${d.y}, ${d.x})`) .attr(\"opacity\", 1); // 新节点进入时：先设 opacity=0，再过渡到 1 → 淡入效果 ng.attr(\"opacity\", 0) .transition().duration(DURATION).attr(\"opacity\", 1); 代码④ 动画时长滑块（HTML/CSS 控制） HTML复制 <!-- HTML 滑块：监听 input 事件即可改 DURATION --> <input id=\"dur\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"1500\" step=\"50\" value=\"500\"> <!-- JS：改变 DURATION 后重放动画 --> document.getElementById(\"dur\").addEventListener(\"input\", e => { DURATION = +e.target.value; render(); // 用新时长重新做一次过渡 });","chars":2263},"en":{"title":"View Rendering & User Interaction","rawTitle":"View Rendering & User Interaction (classed + event delegation + transition)","short":"Render & Interact","subtitle":"classed, event delegation, stopPropagation, and transitions: how views change over time and with users.","bigIdea":"Animation is change unfolded in time, not decoration; delegation is what makes interaction scale.","points":["DOM events capture, target, then bubble; stopPropagation cuts the bubble.","Delegation binds once on a parent, uses closest to find the target, and covers new elements automatically.","transition().duration() animates attribute changes; 0ms hides the process, >1500ms loses attention."],"quiz":{"q":"Why is event.stopPropagation() often needed on a collapse button?","options":["To prevent a page reload","To stop the click from bubbling to the parent li's select handler","To speed up animation"],"answer":1,"why":"The collapse button usually sits inside a clickable list item. Without stopping propagation, collapse and select both fire, and the combined behavior confuses users."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Where this sits in the pipeline</strong>: following 2.3, we now have a &quot;visual structure&quot;. This section covers the last two arrows: &quot;visual structure → view&quot; (rendering) and &quot;view ↔ user&quot; (interaction feedback). Card&#39;s V layer + van Wijk&#39;s feedback loop both land here.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-2-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Your original case</span></h3>\n<p>The original document used <code>classed</code> to control node styling and <code>stopPropagation</code> to block bubbling. The key point is <strong>turning D3 tree layout output into an interactive HTML list</strong>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--theory\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Embedded theory</span></h3>\n<p><strong>Theory patch: animation — the &quot;time dimension&quot; of view rendering</strong></p>\n<p>Animation (transition) isn&#39;t &quot;fancy&quot; — it&#39;s the <em>time dimension</em> of view rendering. D3 uses <code>.transition().duration(ms)</code> to smoothly interpolate an attribute from its old value to a new one. The pedagogical value lies in a single <code>duration</code> parameter:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>duration=0</code>: instant jump — you can&#39;t &quot;see the change happen&quot;</li>\n<li><code>duration=500</code>: a 0.5s transition — you see expand / collapse / move smoothly</li>\n<li><code>duration&gt;1500</code>: too slow — students start to drift</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>This lesson&#39;s interactive demo adds a duration slider</strong> so you can change this parameter live and see &quot;how rendering unfolds over time.&quot;</p>\n<p><strong>DOM event three phases</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Capturing</strong>: window → document → ... → target element (outside to inside)</li>\n<li><strong>Target</strong>: the target element itself</li>\n<li><strong>Bubbling</strong>: target element → ... → document → window (inside to outside)</li>\n</ol>\n<p>By default, listeners attach to the bubbling phase. <code>e.stopPropagation()</code> truncates bubbling so the upper layers no longer fire.</p>\n<p><strong>Event Delegation</strong>:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Problem</th>\n<th>Solution</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Binding click to each of 1000 <code>li</code> in a list → slow, memory-heavy</td>\n<td>Bind click once on the parent element (<code>ul</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New elements need re-binding</td>\n<td>Use <code>e.target.closest(&#39;.label&#39;)</code> to find the actually clicked element</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p><strong>Advantage</strong>: one listener replaces N, and future-added elements are automatically supported.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-4-h3\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ① Event delegation (toggle vs select)</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>Key point to mark</strong>: the toggle button uses stopPropagation to prevent bubbling to the <code>li</code>&#39;s select listener.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">function buildList(liSel, d) {\n  const label = liSel.append(&quot;span&quot;).attr(&quot;class&quot;, &quot;label&quot;);\n\n  label.on(&quot;click.toggle&quot;, (event) =&gt; {\n    // ⭐ 关键 ①：阻止冒泡 —— toggle 不该触发&quot;选中&quot;\n    event.stopPropagation();\n    d.data._collapsed = !d.data._collapsed;\n    render();\n  });\n\n  liSel.on(&quot;click.select&quot;, (event) =&gt; {\n    // ⭐ 关键 ②：toggle click 已被 stopPropagation 阻断，不会到这里\n    document.querySelectorAll(&quot;li&quot;).forEach(li =&gt; li.classList.remove(&quot;selected&quot;));\n    liSel.classed(&quot;selected&quot;, true);  // D3 class 切换\n  });\n}</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Key point explanation</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Without stopPropagation → clicking toggle would trigger both &quot;toggle collapse&quot; and &quot;select node&quot; at once, which confuses the user</li>\n<li>This is a core teaching point of the DOM event mechanism</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-2-4-h4\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ③ D3 transition (transition + duration)</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>Key point to mark</strong>: <code>transition + duration</code> = letting attributes change smoothly over time.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Key: transition + duration = smooth change over time\nsvg.selectAll(&quot;.node&quot;)\n  .transition()                    // enter the transition state\n  .duration(DURATION)              // duration (ms), controlled by slider\n  .attr(&quot;transform&quot;, d =&gt; `translate(${d.y}, ${d.x})`)\n  .attr(&quot;opacity&quot;, 1);\n\n// New nodes entering: set opacity=0 first, then transition to 1 → fade-in\nng.attr(&quot;opacity&quot;, 0)\n  .transition().duration(DURATION).attr(&quot;opacity&quot;, 1);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-2-4-h5\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ④ Animation duration slider (HTML/CSS control)</span></h3>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"html\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">HTML</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-html\">&lt;!-- HTML slider: listen for input to change DURATION --&gt;\n&lt;input id=&quot;dur&quot; type=&quot;range&quot; min=&quot;0&quot; max=&quot;1500&quot; step=&quot;50&quot; value=&quot;500&quot;&gt;\n\n&lt;!-- JS: replay the animation after changing DURATION --&gt;\ndocument.getElementById(&quot;dur&quot;).addEventListener(&quot;input&quot;, e =&gt; {\n  DURATION = +e.target.value;\n  render();   // redo the transition with the new duration\n});</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-2-4-h6\" class=\"blk blk--code\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--code\">Code</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Key code ② Nested recursive buildList</span></h3>\n<p>⭐ <strong>Key point to mark</strong>: <code>selection.each()</code> + <code>d3.select(this)</code> is the key pattern for D3 ↔ native DOM interop.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">function render() {\n  $tree.innerHTML = &quot;&quot;;  // 全量重画（树结构变化没法增量更新）\n  const ul = d3.create(&quot;ul&quot;);\n  ul.selectAll(&quot;li&quot;).data([root]).join(&quot;li&quot;)\n    .each(function(d) { buildList(d3.select(this), d); });\n  $tree.appendChild(ul.node());\n}</code></pre>\n</div><p><strong>Key point explanation</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>D3 has no API for &quot;smart updating&quot; tree structures (hierarchy changes) — a full redraw is simplest</li>\n<li><code>selection.each()</code> together with <code>d3.select(this)</code> converts the native element back into a selection</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"s-2-4-h1","text":"Your original case","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-2-4-h2","text":"Embedded theory","kind":"theory"},{"id":"s-2-4-h3","text":"Key code ① Event delegation (toggle vs select)","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-4-h4","text":"Key code ③ D3 transition (transition + duration)","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-4-h5","text":"Key code ④ Animation duration slider (HTML/CSS control)","kind":"code"},{"id":"s-2-4-h6","text":"Key code ② Nested recursive buildList","kind":"code"}],"text":"Where this sits in the pipeline: following 2.3, we now have a \"visual structure\". This section covers the last two arrows: \"visual structure → view\" (rendering) and \"view ↔ user\" (interaction feedback). Card&#39;s V layer + van Wijk&#39;s feedback loop both land here. Your original case The original document used classed to control node styling and stopPropagation to block bubbling. The key point is turning D3 tree layout output into an interactive HTML list. Embedded theory Theory patch: animation — the \"time dimension\" of view rendering Animation (transition) isn&#39;t \"fancy\" — it&#39;s the time dimension of view rendering. D3 uses .transition().duration(ms) to smoothly interpolate an attribute from its old value to a new one. The pedagogical value lies in a single duration parameter: duration=0: instant jump — you can&#39;t \"see the change happen\" duration=500: a 0.5s transition — you see expand / collapse / move smoothly duration>1500: too slow — students start to drift This lesson&#39;s interactive demo adds a duration slider so you can change this parameter live and see \"how rendering unfolds over time.\" DOM event three phases: Capturing: window → document → ... → target element (outside to inside) Target: the target element itself Bubbling: target element → ... → document → window (inside to outside) By default, listeners attach to the bubbling phase. e.stopPropagation() truncates bubbling so the upper layers no longer fire. Event Delegation: Problem Solution Binding click to each of 1000 li in a list → slow, memory-heavy Bind click once on the parent element (ul) New elements need re-binding Use e.target.closest(&#39;.label&#39;) to find the actually clicked element Advantage: one listener replaces N, and future-added elements are automatically supported. CodeKey code ① Event delegation (toggle vs select) ⭐ Key point to mark: the toggle button uses stopPropagation to prevent bubbling to the li&#39;s select listener. JavaScriptCopy function buildList(liSel, d) { const label = liSel.append(\"span\").attr(\"class\", \"label\"); label.on(\"click.toggle\", (event) => { // ⭐ 关键 ①：阻止冒泡 —— toggle 不该触发\"选中\" event.stopPropagation(); d.data._collapsed = !d.data._collapsed; render(); }); liSel.on(\"click.select\", (event) => { // ⭐ 关键 ②：toggle click 已被 stopPropagation 阻断，不会到这里 document.querySelectorAll(\"li\").forEach(li => li.classList.remove(\"selected\")); liSel.classed(\"selected\", true); // D3 class 切换 }); } Key point explanation: Without stopPropagation → clicking toggle would trigger both \"toggle collapse\" and \"select node\" at once, which confuses the user This is a core teaching point of the DOM event mechanism CodeKey code ③ D3 transition (transition + duration) ⭐ Key point to mark: transition + duration = letting attributes change smoothly over time. JavaScriptCopy // Key: transition + duration = smooth change over time svg.selectAll(\".node\") .transition() // enter the transition state .duration(DURATION) // duration (ms), controlled by slider .attr(\"transform\", d => `translate(${d.y}, ${d.x})`) .attr(\"opacity\", 1); // New nodes entering: set opacity=0 first, then transition to 1 → fade-in ng.attr(\"opacity\", 0) .transition().duration(DURATION).attr(\"opacity\", 1); CodeKey code ④ Animation duration slider (HTML/CSS control) HTMLCopy <!-- HTML slider: listen for input to change DURATION --> <input id=\"dur\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"1500\" step=\"50\" value=\"500\"> <!-- JS: replay the animation after changing DURATION --> document.getElementById(\"dur\").addEventListener(\"input\", e => { DURATION = +e.target.value; render(); // redo the transition with the new duration }); CodeKey code ② Nested recursive buildList ⭐ Key point to mark: selection.each() + d3.select(this) is the key pattern for D3 ↔ native DOM interop. JavaScriptCopy function render() { $tree.innerHTML = \"\"; // 全量重画（树结构变化没法增量更新） const ul = d3.create(\"ul\"); ul.selectAll(\"li\").data([root]).join(\"li\") .each(function(d) { buildList(d3.select(this), d); }); $tree.appendChild(ul.node()); } Key point explanation: D3 has no API for \"smart updating\" tree structures (hierarchy changes) — a full redraw is simplest selection.each() together with d3.select(this) converts the native element back into a selection","chars":3636}},"3.1":{"id":"3.1","num":"3.1","chapter":"ch3","demo":"color:cvd","minutes":8,"related":["3.2","3.8"],"zh":{"title":"颜色模型基础","rawTitle":"颜色模型基础","short":"颜色模型","subtitle":"RGB / HSL / Lab / CMYK，以及色觉缺陷眼中的世界。","bigIdea":"RGB 不是感知空间，Lab 才是；红绿对比是最危险的编码。","points":["RGB 适合显示但不利于插值，HSL 适合调色，Lab 适合色差与渐变。","约 8% 男性有 CVD，绿色盲最常见。","颜色不能是唯一编码，叠加形状、标签与线型。"],"quiz":{"q":"为什么在 RGB 空间直接插值容易得到「发灰」的渐变？","options":["RGB 数值范围太小","RGB 不是感知均匀空间，中段亮度会塌陷","浏览器不支持 RGB 插值"],"answer":1,"why":"RGB 的距离不等于人眼感知的距离。在 Lab 等感知均匀空间插值，亮度与色相变化更均匀，中段不会脏。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>为什么需要四种颜色空间？因为它们各自回答不同的问题。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">四种颜色空间</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>空间</th>\n<th>坐标</th>\n<th>擅长</th>\n<th>不擅长</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>RGB</td>\n<td>红 / 绿 / 蓝，加色</td>\n<td>屏幕显示、设备输出</td>\n<td>不符合人眼感知，不能直接插值</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>HSL</td>\n<td>色相 / 饱和度 / 亮度</td>\n<td>艺术家调色、快速生成配色</td>\n<td>亮度不均匀，仍不是感知空间</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CIE Lab</td>\n<td>亮度 L + 对立色 a / b</td>\n<td>感知均匀，适合插值与色差计算</td>\n<td>需要色彩管理，不能直接写进 CSS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CMYK</td>\n<td>青 / 品红 / 黄 / 黑，减色</td>\n<td>印刷</td>\n<td>Web 基本用不到</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>RGB 不是感知均匀的：<code>rgb(255,0,0)</code> 与 <code>rgb(0,255,0)</code> 的数值距离一样，但人眼觉得绿色亮得多。直接在 RGB 里插值，渐变中段会发灰、发脏。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 同样从蓝到黄：RGB 插值中段偏灰，Lab 插值更干净\nconst rgbGrad = d3.interpolateRgb(&quot;steelblue&quot;, &quot;gold&quot;)(0.5);\nconst labGrad = d3.interpolateLab(&quot;steelblue&quot;, &quot;gold&quot;)(0.5);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-3-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">CVD（色觉缺陷）</span></h3>\n<p>约 <strong>8% 男性、0.5% 女性</strong> 存在某种色觉缺陷：</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>类型</th>\n<th>缺失的锥细胞</th>\n<th>表现</th>\n<th>在男性中的比例</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>红色盲 protanopia</td>\n<td>红</td>\n<td>红暗、红绿难分</td>\n<td>≈1%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>绿色盲 deuteranopia</td>\n<td>绿</td>\n<td>红绿几乎同色</td>\n<td>≈6%（最常见）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>蓝色盲 tritanopia</td>\n<td>蓝</td>\n<td>蓝黄难分</td>\n<td>极罕见</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>设计含义</strong>：红绿对比是最危险的配色。不要只用颜色区分类别，叠加形状、标签、线型或直接标注。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-1-h1","text":"四种颜色空间","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-1-h2","text":"CVD（色觉缺陷）","kind":"plain"}],"text":"为什么需要四种颜色空间？因为它们各自回答不同的问题。 四种颜色空间 空间 坐标 擅长 不擅长 RGB 红 / 绿 / 蓝，加色 屏幕显示、设备输出 不符合人眼感知，不能直接插值 HSL 色相 / 饱和度 / 亮度 艺术家调色、快速生成配色 亮度不均匀，仍不是感知空间 CIE Lab 亮度 L + 对立色 a / b 感知均匀，适合插值与色差计算 需要色彩管理，不能直接写进 CSS CMYK 青 / 品红 / 黄 / 黑，减色 印刷 Web 基本用不到 RGB 不是感知均匀的：rgb(255,0,0) 与 rgb(0,255,0) 的数值距离一样，但人眼觉得绿色亮得多。直接在 RGB 里插值，渐变中段会发灰、发脏。 JavaScript复制 // 同样从蓝到黄：RGB 插值中段偏灰，Lab 插值更干净 const rgbGrad = d3.interpolateRgb(\"steelblue\", \"gold\")(0.5); const labGrad = d3.interpolateLab(\"steelblue\", \"gold\")(0.5); CVD（色觉缺陷） 约 8% 男性、0.5% 女性 存在某种色觉缺陷： 类型 缺失的锥细胞 表现 在男性中的比例 红色盲 protanopia 红 红暗、红绿难分 ≈1% 绿色盲 deuteranopia 绿 红绿几乎同色 ≈6%（最常见） 蓝色盲 tritanopia 蓝 蓝黄难分 极罕见 设计含义：红绿对比是最危险的配色。不要只用颜色区分类别，叠加形状、标签、线型或直接标注。","chars":576},"en":{"title":"Color Model Fundamentals","rawTitle":"Color Model Fundamentals","short":"Color Models","subtitle":"RGB / HSL / Lab / CMYK, and the world as seen with color-vision deficiency.","bigIdea":"RGB is not perceptual; Lab is. Red-green contrast is the most dangerous encoding.","points":["RGB is for display, HSL for artistic control, Lab for color difference and gradients.","About 8% of men have CVD; deuteranopia is most common.","Never encode by color alone; add shape, labels, and line style."],"quiz":{"q":"Why does interpolating in RGB often produce a muddy gradient?","options":["RGB has too small a numeric range","RGB is not perceptually uniform; midpoints lose lightness","Browsers do not support RGB interpolation"],"answer":1,"why":"Distance in RGB is not perceptual distance. Interpolating in Lab keeps lightness and hue transitions even, so the middle stays clean."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Why four color spaces? Because each answers a different question.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Four color spaces</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Space</th>\n<th>Coordinates</th>\n<th>Good at</th>\n<th>Bad at</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>RGB</td>\n<td>red / green / blue, additive</td>\n<td>screens, device output</td>\n<td>not perceptual; do not interpolate directly</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>HSL</td>\n<td>hue / saturation / lightness</td>\n<td>artistic control, quick palettes</td>\n<td>uneven lightness; still not perceptual</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CIE Lab</td>\n<td>lightness L + opponent axes a / b</td>\n<td>perceptual uniformity, interpolation, color difference</td>\n<td>needs color management; not directly CSS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CMYK</td>\n<td>cyan / magenta / yellow / black, subtractive</td>\n<td>print</td>\n<td>rarely used on the web</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>RGB is not perceptually uniform: <code>rgb(255,0,0)</code> and <code>rgb(0,255,0)</code> have the same numeric distance, yet green looks much brighter. Interpolating in RGB makes gradients turn muddy or gray in the middle.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Blue to gold: RGB interpolation goes gray; Lab stays clean\nconst rgbGrad = d3.interpolateRgb(&quot;steelblue&quot;, &quot;gold&quot;)(0.5);\nconst labGrad = d3.interpolateLab(&quot;steelblue&quot;, &quot;gold&quot;)(0.5);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-3-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">CVD (color-vision deficiency)</span></h3>\n<p>About <strong>8% of men and 0.5% of women</strong> have some form of CVD:</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Missing cone</th>\n<th>Experience</th>\n<th>Prevalence in men</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Protanopia</td>\n<td>red</td>\n<td>red looks dark; red/green confuse</td>\n<td>≈1%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Deuteranopia</td>\n<td>green</td>\n<td>red and green look nearly identical</td>\n<td>≈6% (most common)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tritanopia</td>\n<td>blue</td>\n<td>blue/yellow confuse</td>\n<td>very rare</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>Design implication</strong>: red-green contrast is the most dangerous pairing. Never rely on color alone; add shape, labels, line style, or direct annotation.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-1-h1","text":"Four color spaces","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-1-h2","text":"CVD (color-vision deficiency)","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Why four color spaces? Because each answers a different question. Four color spaces Space Coordinates Good at Bad at RGB red / green / blue, additive screens, device output not perceptual; do not interpolate directly HSL hue / saturation / lightness artistic control, quick palettes uneven lightness; still not perceptual CIE Lab lightness L + opponent axes a / b perceptual uniformity, interpolation, color difference needs color management; not directly CSS CMYK cyan / magenta / yellow / black, subtractive print rarely used on the web RGB is not perceptually uniform: rgb(255,0,0) and rgb(0,255,0) have the same numeric distance, yet green looks much brighter. Interpolating in RGB makes gradients turn muddy or gray in the middle. JavaScriptCopy // Blue to gold: RGB interpolation goes gray; Lab stays clean const rgbGrad = d3.interpolateRgb(\"steelblue\", \"gold\")(0.5); const labGrad = d3.interpolateLab(\"steelblue\", \"gold\")(0.5); CVD (color-vision deficiency) About 8% of men and 0.5% of women have some form of CVD: Type Missing cone Experience Prevalence in men Protanopia red red looks dark; red/green confuse ≈1% Deuteranopia green red and green look nearly identical ≈6% (most common) Tritanopia blue blue/yellow confuse very rare Design implication: red-green contrast is the most dangerous pairing. Never rely on color alone; add shape, labels, line style, or direct annotation.","chars":1183}},"3.2":{"id":"3.2","num":"3.2","chapter":"ch3","demo":"color:colormap","minutes":9,"related":["1.3","3.5","3.6"],"zh":{"title":"colormap 三类选择","rawTitle":"colormap 三类选择","short":"colormap 三类","subtitle":"顺序型 / 发散型 / 定性型：选错类型就是在误导读者。","bigIdea":"colormap 的类型由数据的语义决定，而不是由好看程度决定。","points":["顺序型用于有自然顺序的数值，亮度单调变化。","发散型必须有一个有意义的中间值（0、均值、目标）。","定性型用于无序类别，类别数 ≤ 7。"],"quiz":{"q":"用发散型 RdBu 画「各州谋杀率」的主要问题是什么？","options":["颜色不够鲜艳","中段浅色被误读为有意义的中点","红色对色盲不友好，所以完全不能用"],"answer":1,"why":"发散型的浅色中段暗示「基准值」。谋杀率没有这样的中点，读者会把中段误解为「约 100」之类的语义。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>顺序型 / 发散型 / 定性型。选错类型 = 误导读者。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">三类 colormap</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>类型</th>\n<th>数据语义</th>\n<th>颜色变化</th>\n<th>典型例子</th>\n<th>反例</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>顺序型 Sequential</td>\n<td>有自然顺序：人口、温度、密度</td>\n<td>亮度单调变化 + 色相轻微偏移</td>\n<td>Viridis、Cividis、Blues</td>\n<td>彩虹 Jet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>发散型 Diverging</td>\n<td>有意义的&quot;中点&quot;：0、正负、距均值</td>\n<td>两端异色，中间浅/白</td>\n<td>RdBu、BrBG、PiYG</td>\n<td>用发散型画无中点的数据</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>定性型 Qualitative</td>\n<td>无序类别：产品、国家、性别</td>\n<td>色相区分，亮度接近</td>\n<td>Tableau10、Wong、Set2</td>\n<td>用定性色画连续数值</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-3-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">典型错误</span></h3>\n<p>用发散型 <code>RdBu</code> 画&quot;50 州谋杀率&quot;：中段接近白色，读者会以为&quot;谋杀率 100 附近&quot;是某种中点，但 100 没有任何语义。<strong>发散型的中间色必须对应一个有意义的基准值</strong>（0、平均值、政策目标）。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-2-h3\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">CVD 友好检查清单</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Viridis / Cividis：✅ 优（感知均匀 + CVD 友好 + 灰度友好）</li>\n<li>Wong / Okabe-Ito / Paul Tol：✅ 优（类别色）</li>\n<li>RdBu / BrBG：△ 中等（红绿对色盲不友好，但亮度差可辅助）</li>\n<li>Tableau10：△ 与色相相关，红绿相邻</li>\n<li>Jet / Rainbow：⚠ 禁用（非感知均匀、假边界、CVD 不友好）</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 顺序型：数值 → 颜色\nconst color = d3.scaleSequential(d3.interpolateViridis).domain([0, max]);\n\n// 发散型：以 0 为中心\nconst diverging = d3.scaleDiverging(d3.interpolateRdBu).domain([-max, 0, max]);\n\n// 定性型：类别 → 颜色\nconst ordinal = d3.scaleOrdinal(d3.schemeTableau10);</code></pre>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-2-h1","text":"三类 colormap","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-2-h2","text":"典型错误","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-2-h3","text":"CVD 友好检查清单","kind":"plain"}],"text":"顺序型 / 发散型 / 定性型。选错类型 = 误导读者。 三类 colormap 类型 数据语义 颜色变化 典型例子 反例 顺序型 Sequential 有自然顺序：人口、温度、密度 亮度单调变化 + 色相轻微偏移 Viridis、Cividis、Blues 彩虹 Jet 发散型 Diverging 有意义的\"中点\"：0、正负、距均值 两端异色，中间浅/白 RdBu、BrBG、PiYG 用发散型画无中点的数据 定性型 Qualitative 无序类别：产品、国家、性别 色相区分，亮度接近 Tableau10、Wong、Set2 用定性色画连续数值 典型错误 用发散型 RdBu 画\"50 州谋杀率\"：中段接近白色，读者会以为\"谋杀率 100 附近\"是某种中点，但 100 没有任何语义。发散型的中间色必须对应一个有意义的基准值（0、平均值、政策目标）。 CVD 友好检查清单 Viridis / Cividis：✅ 优（感知均匀 + CVD 友好 + 灰度友好） Wong / Okabe-Ito / Paul Tol：✅ 优（类别色） RdBu / BrBG：△ 中等（红绿对色盲不友好，但亮度差可辅助） Tableau10：△ 与色相相关，红绿相邻 Jet / Rainbow：⚠ 禁用（非感知均匀、假边界、CVD 不友好） JavaScript复制 // 顺序型：数值 → 颜色 const color = d3.scaleSequential(d3.interpolateViridis).domain([0, max]); // 发散型：以 0 为中心 const diverging = d3.scaleDiverging(d3.interpolateRdBu).domain([-max, 0, max]); // 定性型：类别 → 颜色 const ordinal = d3.scaleOrdinal(d3.schemeTableau10);","chars":732},"en":{"title":"The Three Categories of Colormaps","rawTitle":"The Three Categories of Colormaps","short":"Colormaps","subtitle":"Sequential / diverging / qualitative: choosing the wrong type misleads readers.","bigIdea":"The colormap type follows the semantics of the data, not personal taste.","points":["Sequential is for ordered values with monotone lightness.","Diverging requires a meaningful midpoint (0, mean, target).","Qualitative is for unordered categories, at most about seven."],"quiz":{"q":"What is wrong with using diverging RdBu for 'murder rate by state'?","options":["The colors are not vivid enough","The pale middle is misread as a meaningful midpoint","Red is CVD-unfriendly, so it can never be used"],"answer":1,"why":"A diverging map's pale middle implies a baseline. Murder rate has no such midpoint, so readers may read the middle as 'about 100'."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Sequential / diverging / qualitative. Choosing the wrong type misleads readers.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Three colormap types</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Data semantics</th>\n<th>Color behavior</th>\n<th>Examples</th>\n<th>Counterexample</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Sequential</td>\n<td>ordered: population, temperature, density</td>\n<td>monotone lightness + slight hue shift</td>\n<td>Viridis, Cividis, Blues</td>\n<td>rainbow Jet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Diverging</td>\n<td>a meaningful midpoint: 0, ±, distance from mean</td>\n<td>two hues, light in the middle</td>\n<td>RdBu, BrBG, PiYG</td>\n<td>diverging on data without a midpoint</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Qualitative</td>\n<td>unordered categories: products, countries, gender</td>\n<td>hue separation, similar lightness</td>\n<td>Tableau10, Wong, Set2</td>\n<td>qualitative colors for continuous values</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-3-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">A classic mistake</span></h3>\n<p>Using diverging <code>RdBu</code> for &quot;murder rate by state&quot;: the pale middle suggests a meaningful midpoint near 100, but 100 means nothing. <strong>The middle color of a diverging map must correspond to a meaningful baseline</strong> (0, the mean, a policy target).</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-2-h3\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">CVD-friendly checklist</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Viridis / Cividis: ✅ excellent (uniform, CVD-safe, grayscale-safe)</li>\n<li>Wong / Okabe-Ito / Paul Tol: ✅ excellent category palettes</li>\n<li>RdBu / BrBG: △ moderate (red-green issues, but lightness helps)</li>\n<li>Tableau10: △ hue-dependent, red and green adjacent</li>\n<li>Jet / Rainbow: ⚠ avoid (non-uniform, false boundaries, CVD-hostile)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Sequential: value → color\nconst color = d3.scaleSequential(d3.interpolateViridis).domain([0, max]);\n\n// Diverging: centered at 0\nconst diverging = d3.scaleDiverging(d3.interpolateRdBu).domain([-max, 0, max]);\n\n// Qualitative: category → color\nconst ordinal = d3.scaleOrdinal(d3.schemeTableau10);</code></pre>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-2-h1","text":"Three colormap types","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-2-h2","text":"A classic mistake","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-2-h3","text":"CVD-friendly checklist","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Sequential / diverging / qualitative. Choosing the wrong type misleads readers. Three colormap types Type Data semantics Color behavior Examples Counterexample Sequential ordered: population, temperature, density monotone lightness + slight hue shift Viridis, Cividis, Blues rainbow Jet Diverging a meaningful midpoint: 0, ±, distance from mean two hues, light in the middle RdBu, BrBG, PiYG diverging on data without a midpoint Qualitative unordered categories: products, countries, gender hue separation, similar lightness Tableau10, Wong, Set2 qualitative colors for continuous values A classic mistake Using diverging RdBu for \"murder rate by state\": the pale middle suggests a meaningful midpoint near 100, but 100 means nothing. The middle color of a diverging map must correspond to a meaningful baseline (0, the mean, a policy target). CVD-friendly checklist Viridis / Cividis: ✅ excellent (uniform, CVD-safe, grayscale-safe) Wong / Okabe-Ito / Paul Tol: ✅ excellent category palettes RdBu / BrBG: △ moderate (red-green issues, but lightness helps) Tableau10: △ hue-dependent, red and green adjacent Jet / Rainbow: ⚠ avoid (non-uniform, false boundaries, CVD-hostile) JavaScriptCopy // Sequential: value → color const color = d3.scaleSequential(d3.interpolateViridis).domain([0, max]); // Diverging: centered at 0 const diverging = d3.scaleDiverging(d3.interpolateRdBu).domain([-max, 0, max]); // Qualitative: category → color const ordinal = d3.scaleOrdinal(d3.schemeTableau10);","chars":1289}},"3.3":{"id":"3.3","num":"3.3","chapter":"ch3","demo":"color:gamut","minutes":9,"related":["3.1","3.5"],"zh":{"title":"CIE Lab 色域图","rawTitle":"CIE Lab 色域图","short":"Lab 色域","subtitle":"感知均匀空间、ΔE 色差，以及 sRGB / Adobe RGB / Rec.2020 的嵌套色域。","bigIdea":"Lab 里距离 ≈ 感知差；超出 sRGB 的颜色在普通屏幕上会被裁掉。","points":["L* 亮度、a* 绿红、b* 蓝黄；ΔE 用于量化色差。","sRGB 覆盖最小，Adobe RGB 居中，Rec.2020 最大。","在 Lab 中插值再转回 sRGB，能避免渐变中段发灰。"],"quiz":{"q":"ΔE 用来衡量什么？","options":["色域覆盖范围","两种颜色之间的感知差异","屏幕亮度"],"answer":1,"why":"ΔE 是 Lab 空间中的色差指标；ΔE<2 几乎不可辨，ΔE>5 才适合作为两个类别的区分色。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>在感知均匀的空间里，颜色之间的距离 ≈ 人眼看到的差别。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Lab 的三个坐标</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>L*</code>：亮度，0（黑）→ 100（白）；</li>\n<li><code>a*</code>：绿（负）↔ 红（正）；</li>\n<li><code>b*</code>：蓝（负）↔ 黄（正）。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>色差常用 <code>ΔE</code> 衡量。<code>ΔE76</code> 是 Lab 空间里的欧氏距离；<code>ΔE2000</code> 针对人眼感知做了加权，更接近真实判断。经验阈值：<code>ΔE &lt; 2</code> 人眼几乎看不出差别，<code>ΔE &gt; 5</code> 才适合作为两个类别的区分色。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">三个色域</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>色域</th>\n<th>用途</th>\n<th>相对 CIE 1931 的覆盖（约）</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>sRGB</td>\n<td>Web、普通屏幕、PPT</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Adobe RGB</td>\n<td>摄影、印刷</td>\n<td>50%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rec.2020</td>\n<td>4K / HDR 电视</td>\n<td>75%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>超出 sRGB 的颜色在普通屏幕上显示不出来，会被 <strong>clamp</strong>（裁到边界）。设计 colormap 时在 Lab 空间插值，再转回 sRGB，能避免&quot;中段发灰&quot;。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Lab 插值：感知均匀，适合生成 colormap\nconst ramp = d3.range(0, 1.01, 0.05)\n  .map(t =&gt; d3.interpolateLab(&quot;#1f4e79&quot;, &quot;#f2c14e&quot;)(t));\n\n// Lab → sRGB，检查是否被裁切\nconst rgb = d3.lab(60, 40, -30).rgb();\nconst clipped = rgb.displayable();   // false 表示超出 sRGB 色域</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>实战提示</strong>：高饱和的纯色（如 <code>#00ff00</code>）在 Lab 里往往超出 sRGB 色域。你在设计器里看到的颜色，和用户屏幕上的颜色可能不是同一个。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-3-h1","text":"Lab 的三个坐标","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-3-h2","text":"三个色域","kind":"plain"}],"text":"在感知均匀的空间里，颜色之间的距离 ≈ 人眼看到的差别。 Lab 的三个坐标 L*：亮度，0（黑）→ 100（白）； a*：绿（负）↔ 红（正）； b*：蓝（负）↔ 黄（正）。 色差常用 ΔE 衡量。ΔE76 是 Lab 空间里的欧氏距离；ΔE2000 针对人眼感知做了加权，更接近真实判断。经验阈值：ΔE < 2 人眼几乎看不出差别，ΔE > 5 才适合作为两个类别的区分色。 三个色域 色域 用途 相对 CIE 1931 的覆盖（约） sRGB Web、普通屏幕、PPT 35% Adobe RGB 摄影、印刷 50% Rec.2020 4K / HDR 电视 75% 超出 sRGB 的颜色在普通屏幕上显示不出来，会被 clamp（裁到边界）。设计 colormap 时在 Lab 空间插值，再转回 sRGB，能避免\"中段发灰\"。 JavaScript复制 // Lab 插值：感知均匀，适合生成 colormap const ramp = d3.range(0, 1.01, 0.05) .map(t => d3.interpolateLab(\"#1f4e79\", \"#f2c14e\")(t)); // Lab → sRGB，检查是否被裁切 const rgb = d3.lab(60, 40, -30).rgb(); const clipped = rgb.displayable(); // false 表示超出 sRGB 色域 实战提示：高饱和的纯色（如 #00ff00）在 Lab 里往往超出 sRGB 色域。你在设计器里看到的颜色，和用户屏幕上的颜色可能不是同一个。","chars":600},"en":{"title":"CIE Lab Gamut Diagram","rawTitle":"CIE Lab Gamut Diagram","short":"Lab Gamut","subtitle":"Perceptual space, ΔE color difference, and the nested sRGB / Adobe RGB / Rec.2020 gamuts.","bigIdea":"In Lab, distance approximates perception; colors outside sRGB are clipped on ordinary screens.","points":["L* lightness, a* green-red, b* blue-yellow; ΔE quantifies color difference.","sRGB is smallest, Adobe RGB in the middle, Rec.2020 largest.","Interpolate in Lab then convert back to sRGB to avoid muddy midpoints."],"quiz":{"q":"What does ΔE measure?","options":["gamut coverage","perceived difference between two colors","screen brightness"],"answer":1,"why":"ΔE is a color-difference metric in Lab. ΔE<2 is nearly invisible; ΔE>5 is a safe distinction between categories."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>In a perceptually uniform space, distance between colors approximates what the eye sees.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">The three Lab coordinates</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>L*</code>: lightness, 0 (black) → 100 (white);</li>\n<li><code>a*</code>: green (negative) ↔ red (positive);</li>\n<li><code>b*</code>: blue (negative) ↔ yellow (positive).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Color difference is measured by <code>ΔE</code>. <code>ΔE76</code> is Euclidean distance in Lab; <code>ΔE2000</code> is weighted toward human perception. Rules of thumb: <code>ΔE &lt; 2</code> is nearly indistinguishable; <code>ΔE &gt; 5</code> is a safe distinction between categories.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Three gamuts</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Gamut</th>\n<th>Use</th>\n<th>Coverage of CIE 1931 (approx.)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>sRGB</td>\n<td>web, ordinary screens, slides</td>\n<td>35%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Adobe RGB</td>\n<td>photography, print</td>\n<td>50%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rec.2020</td>\n<td>4K / HDR television</td>\n<td>75%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>Colors outside sRGB cannot be shown on ordinary screens; they are <strong>clamped</strong> to the boundary. Generate colormaps by interpolating in Lab, then convert back to sRGB, to avoid muddy midpoints.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Lab interpolation: perceptually even, good for colormaps\nconst ramp = d3.range(0, 1.01, 0.05)\n  .map(t =&gt; d3.interpolateLab(&quot;#1f4e79&quot;, &quot;#f2c14e&quot;)(t));\n\n// Lab → sRGB, then check for clipping\nconst rgb = d3.lab(60, 40, -30).rgb();\nconst clipped = rgb.displayable();   // false means outside sRGB</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>Practical tip</strong>: highly saturated colors (e.g. <code>#00ff00</code>) often fall outside sRGB in Lab terms. The color you see in a design tool and the color on a user&#39;s screen may differ.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-3-h1","text":"The three Lab coordinates","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-3-h2","text":"Three gamuts","kind":"plain"}],"text":"In a perceptually uniform space, distance between colors approximates what the eye sees. The three Lab coordinates L*: lightness, 0 (black) → 100 (white); a*: green (negative) ↔ red (positive); b*: blue (negative) ↔ yellow (positive). Color difference is measured by ΔE. ΔE76 is Euclidean distance in Lab; ΔE2000 is weighted toward human perception. Rules of thumb: ΔE < 2 is nearly indistinguishable; ΔE > 5 is a safe distinction between categories. Three gamuts Gamut Use Coverage of CIE 1931 (approx.) sRGB web, ordinary screens, slides 35% Adobe RGB photography, print 50% Rec.2020 4K / HDR television 75% Colors outside sRGB cannot be shown on ordinary screens; they are clamped to the boundary. Generate colormaps by interpolating in Lab, then convert back to sRGB, to avoid muddy midpoints. JavaScriptCopy // Lab interpolation: perceptually even, good for colormaps const ramp = d3.range(0, 1.01, 0.05) .map(t => d3.interpolateLab(\"#1f4e79\", \"#f2c14e\")(t)); // Lab → sRGB, then check for clipping const rgb = d3.lab(60, 40, -30).rgb(); const clipped = rgb.displayable(); // false means outside sRGB Practical tip: highly saturated colors (e.g. #00ff00) often fall outside sRGB in Lab terms. The color you see in a design tool and the color on a user&#39;s screen may differ.","chars":1081}},"3.4":{"id":"3.4","num":"3.4","chapter":"ch3","demo":"color:harmony","minutes":8,"related":["3.5","3.7"],"zh":{"title":"色系搭配规则","rawTitle":"色系搭配规则（5 大类）","short":"色系搭配","subtitle":"单色、类比、互补、三等分、分裂互补：五种规则与选择原则。","bigIdea":"配色规则解决的是「类别之间要多不同」，而不是「哪种颜色好看」。","points":["单色最安全，互补最强调但也最刺眼。","类别数 ≤ 7；超过就归并或改用连续色。","背景与注释保持低饱和，把饱和度留给数据。"],"quiz":{"q":"要突出「实验组 vs 对照组」的差异，优先考虑哪种色系？","options":["单色","互补","类比"],"answer":1,"why":"互补色在色轮上正对，对比最强，适合两组对照；但只让一组承担强调，避免两边都刺眼。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>单色 / 类比 / 互补 / 三等分 / 分裂互补。什么时候用哪个？</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">五种规则</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>规则</th>\n<th>色相关系</th>\n<th>气质</th>\n<th>适合</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>单色 Monochromatic</td>\n<td>同一色相，不同 L / S</td>\n<td>克制、专业</td>\n<td>严肃科研、单指标分层</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>类比 Analogous</td>\n<td>色轮相邻 ±30°</td>\n<td>和谐、柔和</td>\n<td>同一主题下的分组</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>互补 Complementary</td>\n<td>色轮正对 180°</td>\n<td>强对比、易刺眼</td>\n<td>实验组 vs 对照组</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>三等分 Triadic</td>\n<td>色轮 120° 等分</td>\n<td>活泼、平衡</td>\n<td>3 个类别</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>分裂互补 Split</td>\n<td>150° / 210°</td>\n<td>温和的对比</td>\n<td>一般情况的首选</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-3-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">选择原则</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>类别数 ≤ 7；超过 7 个类别，改用连续 colormap 或&quot;其他&quot;归并；</li>\n<li>需要强调时用互补色，但只让<strong>一个</strong>颜色承担强调；</li>\n<li>背景、网格、注释用低饱和中性色，把饱和度留给数据；</li>\n<li>先在灰度下检查：如果去掉颜色就分不清，说明亮度层次不够。</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// HSL 生成一组类比色：色相 ±30°，饱和度与亮度分档\nconst base = { h: 18, s: 62, l: 46 };\nconst analogous = [-30, -15, 0, 15, 30].map((dh, i) =&gt;\n  d3.hsl((base.h + dh + 360) % 360, base.s - i * 4, base.l + i * 5).formatHex()\n);</code></pre>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-4-h1","text":"五种规则","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-4-h2","text":"选择原则","kind":"plain"}],"text":"单色 / 类比 / 互补 / 三等分 / 分裂互补。什么时候用哪个？ 五种规则 规则 色相关系 气质 适合 单色 Monochromatic 同一色相，不同 L / S 克制、专业 严肃科研、单指标分层 类比 Analogous 色轮相邻 ±30° 和谐、柔和 同一主题下的分组 互补 Complementary 色轮正对 180° 强对比、易刺眼 实验组 vs 对照组 三等分 Triadic 色轮 120° 等分 活泼、平衡 3 个类别 分裂互补 Split 150° / 210° 温和的对比 一般情况的首选 选择原则 类别数 ≤ 7；超过 7 个类别，改用连续 colormap 或\"其他\"归并； 需要强调时用互补色，但只让一个颜色承担强调； 背景、网格、注释用低饱和中性色，把饱和度留给数据； 先在灰度下检查：如果去掉颜色就分不清，说明亮度层次不够。 JavaScript复制 // HSL 生成一组类比色：色相 ±30°，饱和度与亮度分档 const base = { h: 18, s: 62, l: 46 }; const analogous = [-30, -15, 0, 15, 30].map((dh, i) => d3.hsl((base.h + dh + 360) % 360, base.s - i * 4, base.l + i * 5).formatHex() );","chars":494},"en":{"title":"Color Scheme Combination Rules","rawTitle":"Color Scheme Combination Rules (5 major types)","short":"Color Schemes","subtitle":"Monochromatic, analogous, complementary, triadic, split-complementary: five rules and how to choose.","bigIdea":"Palette rules answer how different categories should be, not which color is pretty.","points":["Monochromatic is safest; complementary is strongest and harshest.","Keep categories ≤ 7; merge or switch to a continuous scale beyond that.","Keep backgrounds and annotations muted; save saturation for data."],"quiz":{"q":"To emphasize 'treatment vs control', which scheme is the first choice?","options":["monochromatic","complementary","analogous"],"answer":1,"why":"Complementary hues sit opposite on the wheel and give the strongest contrast for two groups. Let only one side carry the emphasis so neither becomes harsh."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Monochromatic / analogous / complementary / triadic / split-complementary. When to use which?</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Five rules</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Rule</th>\n<th>Hue relationship</th>\n<th>Mood</th>\n<th>Good for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Monochromatic</td>\n<td>one hue, varying L / S</td>\n<td>restrained, professional</td>\n<td>serious research, layered single metrics</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Analogous</td>\n<td>neighbors within ±30°</td>\n<td>harmonious, soft</td>\n<td>groups under one theme</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Complementary</td>\n<td>opposite, 180°</td>\n<td>strong, easily harsh</td>\n<td>treatment vs control</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Triadic</td>\n<td>120° apart</td>\n<td>lively, balanced</td>\n<td>three categories</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Split-complementary</td>\n<td>150° / 210°</td>\n<td>gentle contrast</td>\n<td>a good default</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-3-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Selection principles</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Keep categories ≤ 7; with more, switch to a continuous colormap or merge into &quot;other&quot;;</li>\n<li>Use a complementary color for emphasis, but let <strong>one</strong> color carry the emphasis;</li>\n<li>Keep backgrounds, grids, and annotations low-saturation; save saturation for data;</li>\n<li>Check in grayscale: if categories collapse without hue, lightness is not doing enough work.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// HSL analogous palette: hue ±30°, stepped saturation and lightness\nconst base = { h: 18, s: 62, l: 46 };\nconst analogous = [-30, -15, 0, 15, 30].map((dh, i) =&gt;\n  d3.hsl((base.h + dh + 360) % 360, base.s - i * 4, base.l + i * 5).formatHex()\n);</code></pre>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-4-h1","text":"Five rules","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-4-h2","text":"Selection principles","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Monochromatic / analogous / complementary / triadic / split-complementary. When to use which? Five rules Rule Hue relationship Mood Good for Monochromatic one hue, varying L / S restrained, professional serious research, layered single metrics Analogous neighbors within ±30° harmonious, soft groups under one theme Complementary opposite, 180° strong, easily harsh treatment vs control Triadic 120° apart lively, balanced three categories Split-complementary 150° / 210° gentle contrast a good default Selection principles Keep categories ≤ 7; with more, switch to a continuous colormap or merge into \"other\"; Use a complementary color for emphasis, but let one color carry the emphasis; Keep backgrounds, grids, and annotations low-saturation; save saturation for data; Check in grayscale: if categories collapse without hue, lightness is not doing enough work. JavaScriptCopy // HSL analogous palette: hue ±30°, stepped saturation and lightness const base = { h: 18, s: 62, l: 46 }; const analogous = [-30, -15, 0, 15, 30].map((dh, i) => d3.hsl((base.h + dh + 360) % 360, base.s - i * 4, base.l + i * 5).formatHex() );","chars":948}},"3.5":{"id":"3.5","num":"3.5","chapter":"ch3","demo":"color:palettes","minutes":8,"related":["3.2","3.4","3.8"],"zh":{"title":"科研经典配色","rawTitle":"科研经典配色","short":"经典配色","subtitle":"Wong、Okabe-Ito、Paul Tol、Tableau、Viridis：顶刊与商业图表的常用色板。","bigIdea":"优先选同时通过 CVD 与灰度检查的色板，而不是看起来最鲜艳的。","points":["Wong / Okabe-Ito 是科研配色的黄金标准。","Tableau10 通用但红绿相邻，对色盲不友好。","Viridis 适合连续数值，Jet 应淘汰。"],"quiz":{"q":"下面哪套配色最适合 8 类且需要 CVD 友好的科研图？","options":["Jet 彩虹","Wong 8 色","HSL 随机 12 色"],"answer":1,"why":"Wong 8 色专为 CVD 与灰度打印设计，类别数正好 8；Jet 非感知均匀，随机 12 色超过可辨别的类别上限。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Wong / Paul Tol / Okabe-Ito / Tableau / Viridis——顶刊都在用什么？</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-5-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">三套黄金标准</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>配色</th>\n<th>色数</th>\n<th>特点</th>\n<th>来源</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Wong</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>CVD 友好、灰度打印友好</td>\n<td>Wong, Nature Methods 2011</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Okabe-Ito</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>与 Wong 基本同源，早期顶刊默认</td>\n<td>Okabe &amp; Ito 2002</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Paul Tol bright</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>白底清晰、色相间隔均匀</td>\n<td>SRON Technical Note</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>Wong 8 色：<code>#000000 #E69F00 #56B4E9 #009E73 #F0E442 #0072B2 #D55E00 #CC79A7</code>。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 把 Wong 8 色直接注册成一个有序比例尺\nconst wong8 = [&quot;#000000&quot;, &quot;#E69F00&quot;, &quot;#56B4E9&quot;, &quot;#009E73&quot;,\n               &quot;#F0E442&quot;, &quot;#0072B2&quot;, &quot;#D55E00&quot;, &quot;#CC79A7&quot;];\nconst color = d3.scaleOrdinal(wong8);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-3-5-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">商业与通用</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Tableau 10</strong>：商业图表最常用，10 色；红绿相邻，对色盲不友好。</li>\n<li><strong>Paired (12)</strong>：成对设计（处理前/后），12 色容易过载。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-5-h3\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">顺序型 / 发散型</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Viridis</strong>：matplotlib / d3 默认，感知均匀 + CVD 友好；</li>\n<li><strong>Cividis</strong>：Viridis 的 CVD 强化版，蓝黄分明；</li>\n<li><strong>RdBu</strong>：发散型红蓝，适合以 0 为中心的数据。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>实战原则</strong>：类别数 ≤ 7；必须做 CVD 模拟；优先选 CVD 友好 + 灰度友好的配色。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-5-h1","text":"三套黄金标准","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-5-h2","text":"商业与通用","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-5-h3","text":"顺序型 / 发散型","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Wong / Paul Tol / Okabe-Ito / Tableau / Viridis——顶刊都在用什么？ 三套黄金标准 配色 色数 特点 来源 Wong 8 CVD 友好、灰度打印友好 Wong, Nature Methods 2011 Okabe-Ito 8 与 Wong 基本同源，早期顶刊默认 Okabe & Ito 2002 Paul Tol bright 7 白底清晰、色相间隔均匀 SRON Technical Note Wong 8 色：#000000 #E69F00 #56B4E9 #009E73 #F0E442 #0072B2 #D55E00 #CC79A7。 JavaScript复制 // 把 Wong 8 色直接注册成一个有序比例尺 const wong8 = [\"#000000\", \"#E69F00\", \"#56B4E9\", \"#009E73\", \"#F0E442\", \"#0072B2\", \"#D55E00\", \"#CC79A7\"]; const color = d3.scaleOrdinal(wong8); 商业与通用 Tableau 10：商业图表最常用，10 色；红绿相邻，对色盲不友好。 Paired (12)：成对设计（处理前/后），12 色容易过载。 顺序型 / 发散型 Viridis：matplotlib / d3 默认，感知均匀 + CVD 友好； Cividis：Viridis 的 CVD 强化版，蓝黄分明； RdBu：发散型红蓝，适合以 0 为中心的数据。 实战原则：类别数 ≤ 7；必须做 CVD 模拟；优先选 CVD 友好 + 灰度友好的配色。","chars":605},"en":{"title":"Classic Scientific Palettes","rawTitle":"Classic Scientific Palettes","short":"Palettes","subtitle":"Wong, Okabe-Ito, Paul Tol, Tableau, Viridis: palettes used by journals and business charts.","bigIdea":"Prefer palettes that pass both CVD and grayscale checks, not the most vivid one.","points":["Wong / Okabe-Ito are the gold standard for scientific figures.","Tableau10 is versatile but red and green are adjacent.","Viridis suits continuous values; Jet should be retired."],"quiz":{"q":"Which palette best fits an 8-category, CVD-safe scientific figure?","options":["Jet rainbow","Wong 8","12 random HSL colors"],"answer":1,"why":"Wong 8 is designed for CVD and grayscale printing and has exactly eight categories. Jet is not perceptually uniform; 12 random colors exceed reliable discrimination."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Wong / Paul Tol / Okabe-Ito / Tableau / Viridis — what do top journals actually use?</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-5-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Three gold standards</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Palette</th>\n<th>Colors</th>\n<th>Features</th>\n<th>Source</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Wong</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>CVD-safe, grayscale-safe</td>\n<td>Wong, Nature Methods 2011</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Okabe-Ito</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>essentially the same family; early journal default</td>\n<td>Okabe &amp; Ito 2002</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Paul Tol bright</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>crisp on white, evenly spaced hues</td>\n<td>SRON Technical Note</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>Wong 8: <code>#000000 #E69F00 #56B4E9 #009E73 #F0E442 #0072B2 #D55E00 #CC79A7</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Register Wong 8 as an ordinal scale\nconst wong8 = [&quot;#000000&quot;, &quot;#E69F00&quot;, &quot;#56B4E9&quot;, &quot;#009E73&quot;,\n               &quot;#F0E442&quot;, &quot;#0072B2&quot;, &quot;#D55E00&quot;, &quot;#CC79A7&quot;];\nconst color = d3.scaleOrdinal(wong8);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-3-5-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Commercial and general</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Tableau 10</strong>: the workhorse of business charts, 10 colors; red and green are adjacent, so CVD-unsafe.</li>\n<li><strong>Paired (12)</strong>: designed in pairs (before/after); 12 colors is easy to overload.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-5-h3\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Sequential / diverging</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Viridis</strong>: the matplotlib / d3 default, perceptually uniform and CVD-safe;</li>\n<li><strong>Cividis</strong>: a CVD-hardened Viridis with clearer blue-yellow separation;</li>\n<li><strong>RdBu</strong>: diverging red-blue, best for data centered on zero.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>Rules of thumb</strong>: ≤ 7 categories; always run a CVD simulation; prefer palettes that are both CVD-safe and grayscale-safe.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-5-h1","text":"Three gold standards","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-5-h2","text":"Commercial and general","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-5-h3","text":"Sequential / diverging","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Wong / Paul Tol / Okabe-Ito / Tableau / Viridis — what do top journals actually use? Three gold standards Palette Colors Features Source Wong 8 CVD-safe, grayscale-safe Wong, Nature Methods 2011 Okabe-Ito 8 essentially the same family; early journal default Okabe & Ito 2002 Paul Tol bright 7 crisp on white, evenly spaced hues SRON Technical Note Wong 8: #000000 #E69F00 #56B4E9 #009E73 #F0E442 #0072B2 #D55E00 #CC79A7. JavaScriptCopy // Register Wong 8 as an ordinal scale const wong8 = [\"#000000\", \"#E69F00\", \"#56B4E9\", \"#009E73\", \"#F0E442\", \"#0072B2\", \"#D55E00\", \"#CC79A7\"]; const color = d3.scaleOrdinal(wong8); Commercial and general Tableau 10: the workhorse of business charts, 10 colors; red and green are adjacent, so CVD-unsafe. Paired (12): designed in pairs (before/after); 12 colors is easy to overload. Sequential / diverging Viridis: the matplotlib / d3 default, perceptually uniform and CVD-safe; Cividis: a CVD-hardened Viridis with clearer blue-yellow separation; RdBu: diverging red-blue, best for data centered on zero. Rules of thumb: ≤ 7 categories; always run a CVD simulation; prefer palettes that are both CVD-safe and grayscale-safe.","chars":989}},"3.6":{"id":"3.6","num":"3.6","chapter":"ch3","demo":"color:quiz","minutes":7,"related":["3.2","3.5","3.8"],"zh":{"title":"对错案例对比","rawTitle":"对错案例对比","short":"对错案例","subtitle":"四个典型错误：Jet、红绿、颜色过多、发散型误用。","bigIdea":"先判断图表在编码什么，再判断颜色选得对不对。","points":["彩虹谱制造假边界，且对色盲不友好。","红绿对比在绿色盲眼中几乎同色。","超过 7 类时，颜色不再是可靠的区分通道。"],"quiz":{"q":"一张图用了 12 种颜色区分 12 个国家，最稳妥的改法是？","options":["换成 12 种更鲜艳的颜色","按地区归并为 6–7 类，其余归入「其他」","改成红绿交替"],"answer":1,"why":"人眼无法稳定区分超过约 7 种色相。归并类别、突出关键组，或改用位置分面，比增加颜色更可靠。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>四张图，三错一对。先判断，再看理由。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-6-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">四个典型错误</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>错误</th>\n<th>问题</th>\n<th>正确做法</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>彩虹谱 Jet 画连续数值</td>\n<td>非感知均匀、假边界、CVD 不友好</td>\n<td>Viridis / Cividis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>红绿对比区分两类</td>\n<td>红绿色盲眼中几乎同色</td>\n<td>Wong 的橙 + 蓝，或加形状/标签</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>12 种颜色区分 12 类</td>\n<td>超过 7 类，人眼无法稳定区分</td>\n<td>归并为 7 类 + &quot;其他&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>发散型画无中点数据</td>\n<td>中间白被误读为&quot;中点&quot;</td>\n<td>顺序型</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>教学建议</strong>：先让学生投票选&quot;哪张对&quot;，再打开 CVD 模拟。亲手选错一次，比看十遍理论记得牢。</p>\n</blockquote><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 用灰度亮度做一次快速检查：两类颜色不能只靠色相区分\nconst gray = (hex) =&gt; {\n  const c = d3.rgb(hex);\n  return 0.2126 * c.r + 0.7152 * c.g + 0.0722 * c.b;\n};\nconst pairs = wong8.slice(0, 4).map((c, i) =&gt; [gray(c), c]);</code></pre>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-6-h1","text":"四个典型错误","kind":"plain"}],"text":"四张图，三错一对。先判断，再看理由。 四个典型错误 # 错误 问题 正确做法 1 彩虹谱 Jet 画连续数值 非感知均匀、假边界、CVD 不友好 Viridis / Cividis 2 红绿对比区分两类 红绿色盲眼中几乎同色 Wong 的橙 + 蓝，或加形状/标签 3 12 种颜色区分 12 类 超过 7 类，人眼无法稳定区分 归并为 7 类 + \"其他\" 4 发散型画无中点数据 中间白被误读为\"中点\" 顺序型 教学建议：先让学生投票选\"哪张对\"，再打开 CVD 模拟。亲手选错一次，比看十遍理论记得牢。 JavaScript复制 // 用灰度亮度做一次快速检查：两类颜色不能只靠色相区分 const gray = (hex) => { const c = d3.rgb(hex); return 0.2126 * c.r + 0.7152 * c.g + 0.0722 * c.b; }; const pairs = wong8.slice(0, 4).map((c, i) => [gray(c), c]);","chars":382},"en":{"title":"Right-vs-Wrong Case Comparison","rawTitle":"Right-vs-Wrong Case Comparison","short":"Right vs Wrong","subtitle":"Four typical mistakes: Jet, red-green, too many colors, and misused diverging maps.","bigIdea":"First ask what the chart encodes, then whether the colors encode it correctly.","points":["Rainbow maps invent boundaries and fail CVD.","Red-green pairs collapse for deuteranopes.","Beyond seven categories, color is no longer a reliable channel."],"quiz":{"q":"A chart uses 12 colors for 12 countries. What is the safest fix?","options":["Use 12 more vivid colors","Group into 6–7 regions and put the rest in 'other'","Alternate red and green"],"answer":1,"why":"People cannot reliably distinguish more than about seven hues. Grouping, highlighting key groups, or faceting by position is far more robust than adding colors."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Four charts, three wrong, one right. Decide first, then read why.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-6-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Four typical mistakes</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Mistake</th>\n<th>Problem</th>\n<th>Fix</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>rainbow Jet for continuous values</td>\n<td>non-uniform, false boundaries, CVD-hostile</td>\n<td>Viridis / Cividis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>red-green contrast for two classes</td>\n<td>nearly identical for red-green colorblind readers</td>\n<td>Wong orange + blue, or add shape/labels</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>12 colors for 12 categories</td>\n<td>beyond ~7, hue discrimination collapses</td>\n<td>merge to 7 + &quot;other&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>diverging map without a midpoint</td>\n<td>pale middle misread as a meaningful baseline</td>\n<td>use a sequential map</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Teaching tip</strong>: let students vote on &quot;which one is right&quot; before revealing the CVD simulation. Getting it wrong once sticks better than ten readings.</p>\n</blockquote><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Quick grayscale check: two classes must not rely on hue alone\nconst gray = (hex) =&gt; {\n  const c = d3.rgb(hex);\n  return 0.2126 * c.r + 0.7152 * c.g + 0.0722 * c.b;\n};\nconst pairs = wong8.slice(0, 4).map((c, i) =&gt; [gray(c), c]);</code></pre>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-6-h1","text":"Four typical mistakes","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Four charts, three wrong, one right. Decide first, then read why. Four typical mistakes # Mistake Problem Fix 1 rainbow Jet for continuous values non-uniform, false boundaries, CVD-hostile Viridis / Cividis 2 red-green contrast for two classes nearly identical for red-green colorblind readers Wong orange + blue, or add shape/labels 3 12 colors for 12 categories beyond ~7, hue discrimination collapses merge to 7 + \"other\" 4 diverging map without a midpoint pale middle misread as a meaningful baseline use a sequential map Teaching tip: let students vote on \"which one is right\" before revealing the CVD simulation. Getting it wrong once sticks better than ten readings. JavaScriptCopy // Quick grayscale check: two classes must not rely on hue alone const gray = (hex) => { const c = d3.rgb(hex); return 0.2126 * c.r + 0.7152 * c.g + 0.0722 * c.b; }; const pairs = wong8.slice(0, 4).map((c, i) => [gray(c), c]);","chars":764}},"3.7":{"id":"3.7","num":"3.7","chapter":"ch3","demo":"color:generator","minutes":8,"related":["3.4","3.5"],"zh":{"title":"鲜艳 + 低饱和 哲学生成器","rawTitle":"鲜艳 + 低饱和 哲学生成器","short":"配色生成器","subtitle":"≤7 色、主色鲜艳、辅色低饱和：一套可复用的生成公式。","bigIdea":"好配色不是「选出来的」，而是按数量、色相间距、饱和度三条约束「算出来的」。","points":["主色 S 70–80%，配套色 S 30–50%。","色相间隔 ≥30°，互补色只用来强调。","生成后仍要过 CVD 与灰度检查。"],"quiz":{"q":"生成 7 色配色时，为什么要给配套色降低饱和度？","options":["为了让所有颜色一样亮","避免每个颜色都「抢」，让主色承担强调","因为低饱和颜色更便宜"],"answer":1,"why":"所有颜色都高饱和会互相争夺注意力，读者不知道看哪里。低饱和辅色提供区分但不抢戏，主色才能承担强调。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>颜色数量 ≤ 7，鲜艳颜色 + 低饱和度 = 好看又耐看。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-7-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">三条规则</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>数量 ≤ 7</strong>：超过 7 种，眼睛无法稳定区分；</li>\n<li><strong>色相拉开 ≥ 30°</strong>：用 H 制造类间距离；</li>\n<li><strong>主色鲜艳、辅色低饱和</strong>：主色 S 70–80%，配套色 S 30–50%。</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-7-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">7 色生成公式</span></h3>\n<p>主色 + 2 个类比色（±30°）+ 1 个低饱和类比色 + 1 个互补色 + 1 个低饱和互补色 + 1 个高亮色 = 7 色。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const h = base.h;\nconst palette = [\n  hsl(h, 72, 48),          // 主色\n  hsl(h + 30, 64, 52),     // 类比 +\n  hsl(h - 30, 60, 44),     // 类比 -\n  hsl(h + 15, 38, 60),     // 低饱和类比\n  hsl(h + 180, 58, 46),    // 互补\n  hsl(h + 150, 34, 62),    // 低饱和互补\n  hsl(h, 88, 88),          // 高亮 / 背景\n];</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--warn\"><p><strong>注意</strong>：这 7 色是&quot;起点&quot;不是&quot;终点&quot;。生成后仍要做 CVD 模拟与灰度检查；如果两类在灰度下亮度相同，加形状或直接标注。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-7-h1","text":"三条规则","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-7-h2","text":"7 色生成公式","kind":"plain"}],"text":"颜色数量 ≤ 7，鲜艳颜色 + 低饱和度 = 好看又耐看。 三条规则 数量 ≤ 7：超过 7 种，眼睛无法稳定区分； 色相拉开 ≥ 30°：用 H 制造类间距离； 主色鲜艳、辅色低饱和：主色 S 70–80%，配套色 S 30–50%。 7 色生成公式 主色 + 2 个类比色（±30°）+ 1 个低饱和类比色 + 1 个互补色 + 1 个低饱和互补色 + 1 个高亮色 = 7 色。 JavaScript复制 const h = base.h; const palette = [ hsl(h, 72, 48), // 主色 hsl(h + 30, 64, 52), // 类比 + hsl(h - 30, 60, 44), // 类比 - hsl(h + 15, 38, 60), // 低饱和类比 hsl(h + 180, 58, 46), // 互补 hsl(h + 150, 34, 62), // 低饱和互补 hsl(h, 88, 88), // 高亮 / 背景 ]; 注意：这 7 色是\"起点\"不是\"终点\"。生成后仍要做 CVD 模拟与灰度检查；如果两类在灰度下亮度相同，加形状或直接标注。","chars":396},"en":{"title":"Vivid + Low-Saturation Philosophy Generator","rawTitle":"Vivid + Low-Saturation Philosophy Generator","short":"Palette Generator","subtitle":"≤7 colors, vivid primary, muted companions: a reusable generation formula.","bigIdea":"A good palette is computed from three constraints (count, hue spacing, saturation), not picked by taste.","points":["Primary S 70–80%; companions S 30–50%.","Hue spacing ≥30°; use complementary colors only for emphasis.","Always run CVD and grayscale checks afterward."],"quiz":{"q":"Why lower the saturation of companion colors in a 7-color palette?","options":["So every color has the same lightness","So they do not compete and the primary can carry emphasis","Because low-saturation colors are cheaper"],"answer":1,"why":"If every color is highly saturated, they compete for attention and readers do not know where to look. Muted companions differentiate without stealing the show."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>≤ 7 colors, vivid accents + low-saturation companions = attractive and durable.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-7-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Three rules</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Count ≤ 7</strong>: beyond seven, hue discrimination collapses;</li>\n<li><strong>Hue spacing ≥ 30°</strong>: use H to create between-category distance;</li>\n<li><strong>Vivid primary, muted companions</strong>: primary S 70–80%, companions S 30–50%.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-7-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">The 7-color formula</span></h3>\n<p>Primary + 2 analogous (±30°) + 1 muted analogous + 1 complementary + 1 muted complementary + 1 highlight = 7.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const h = base.h;\nconst palette = [\n  hsl(h, 72, 48),          // primary\n  hsl(h + 30, 64, 52),     // analogous +\n  hsl(h - 30, 60, 44),     // analogous -\n  hsl(h + 15, 38, 60),     // muted analogous\n  hsl(h + 180, 58, 46),    // complementary\n  hsl(h + 150, 34, 62),    // muted complementary\n  hsl(h, 88, 88),          // highlight / background\n];</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Note</strong>: these seven colors are a starting point, not a verdict. Run a CVD and grayscale check afterward; if two categories share lightness, add shape or direct labels.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-7-h1","text":"Three rules","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-7-h2","text":"The 7-color formula","kind":"plain"}],"text":"≤ 7 colors, vivid accents + low-saturation companions = attractive and durable. Three rules Count ≤ 7: beyond seven, hue discrimination collapses; Hue spacing ≥ 30°: use H to create between-category distance; Vivid primary, muted companions: primary S 70–80%, companions S 30–50%. The 7-color formula Primary + 2 analogous (±30°) + 1 muted analogous + 1 complementary + 1 muted complementary + 1 highlight = 7. JavaScriptCopy const h = base.h; const palette = [ hsl(h, 72, 48), // primary hsl(h + 30, 64, 52), // analogous + hsl(h - 30, 60, 44), // analogous - hsl(h + 15, 38, 60), // muted analogous hsl(h + 180, 58, 46), // complementary hsl(h + 150, 34, 62), // muted complementary hsl(h, 88, 88), // highlight / background ]; Note: these seven colors are a starting point, not a verdict. Run a CVD and grayscale check afterward; if two categories share lightness, add shape or direct labels.","chars":741}},"3.8":{"id":"3.8","num":"3.8","chapter":"ch3","demo":"color:cvdtest","minutes":9,"related":["3.1","3.2","3.5"],"zh":{"title":"CVD 论文图测","rawTitle":"CVD 论文图测","short":"CVD 图测","subtitle":"用三种色觉缺陷模拟，检查你的图在别人眼里是否还读得懂。","bigIdea":"CVD 检查不是可选项，而是图表发布前的最后一道门。","points":["模拟要作用在线性 sRGB 上，而不是直接改色相。","检查三件事：类别可辨、顺序可读、标注还在。","颜色之外，形状、位置、标签是保险。"],"quiz":{"q":"开启绿色盲模拟后，红绿两条线几乎一样，最有效的补救是？","options":["把红色调得更红","给两条线加不同线型并直接标注","把背景改成黑色"],"answer":1,"why":"在绿色盲眼中红绿可能坍缩为同一亮度/色相；加实线/虚线、点标记和直接标签，用非颜色通道恢复区分。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>你的图在色盲眼里还看得懂吗？拿真实论文图做测试。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-8-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">模拟方法</span></h3>\n<p>CVD 模拟不是简单&quot;把红色变灰&quot;，而是按锥细胞响应做颜色变换。常用三组矩阵（Brettel / Viénot 模型）分别模拟红色盲、绿色盲、蓝色盲。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 简化版：绿色盲（deuteranopia）模拟矩阵，作用在 sRGB 线性值上\nconst deuteranopia = [\n  [0.625, 0.375, 0.0],\n  [0.7,   0.3,   0.0],\n  [0.0,   0.3,   0.7],\n];</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-3-8-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">测试流程</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>把图导出为 PNG（不要只截局部）；</li>\n<li>用 Coblis / Color Oracle / 本站色彩实验室做三种模拟；</li>\n<li>问三个问题：还能区分类别吗？还能读出顺序吗？关键标注还在吗？</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-8-h3\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">实测结论</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Wong / Okabe-Ito / Paul Tol：在三种 CVD 下都能区分；</li>\n<li>红绿对比：在绿色盲眼中几乎同色，是最严重的问题；</li>\n<li>Viridis：在三种 CVD 下亮度顺序保持，适合连续数值；</li>\n<li>Nature / Science / Cell 已逐步要求作者使用 CVD 友好配色。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>一句话总结</strong>：颜色是辅助，不是唯一编码。形状、位置、标签、线型，才是让图&quot;对所有人都可读&quot;的保险。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-8-h1","text":"模拟方法","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-8-h2","text":"测试流程","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-8-h3","text":"实测结论","kind":"plain"}],"text":"你的图在色盲眼里还看得懂吗？拿真实论文图做测试。 模拟方法 CVD 模拟不是简单\"把红色变灰\"，而是按锥细胞响应做颜色变换。常用三组矩阵（Brettel / Viénot 模型）分别模拟红色盲、绿色盲、蓝色盲。 JavaScript复制 // 简化版：绿色盲（deuteranopia）模拟矩阵，作用在 sRGB 线性值上 const deuteranopia = [ [0.625, 0.375, 0.0], [0.7, 0.3, 0.0], [0.0, 0.3, 0.7], ]; 测试流程 把图导出为 PNG（不要只截局部）； 用 Coblis / Color Oracle / 本站色彩实验室做三种模拟； 问三个问题：还能区分类别吗？还能读出顺序吗？关键标注还在吗？ 实测结论 Wong / Okabe-Ito / Paul Tol：在三种 CVD 下都能区分； 红绿对比：在绿色盲眼中几乎同色，是最严重的问题； Viridis：在三种 CVD 下亮度顺序保持，适合连续数值； Nature / Science / Cell 已逐步要求作者使用 CVD 友好配色。 一句话总结：颜色是辅助，不是唯一编码。形状、位置、标签、线型，才是让图\"对所有人都可读\"的保险。","chars":477},"en":{"title":"CVD Academic-Figure Test","rawTitle":"CVD Academic-Figure Test","short":"CVD Test","subtitle":"Simulate three kinds of color-vision deficiency and check whether your figure still reads.","bigIdea":"A CVD check is not optional; it is the last gate before publishing a figure.","points":["Simulate in linear sRGB, not by shifting hue directly.","Check three things: categories, order, and annotations.","Beyond color, shape, position, and labels are the safety net."],"quiz":{"q":"Under deuteranopia simulation the red and green lines look identical. Best fix?","options":["Make the red redder","Give the lines different dash patterns and direct labels","Change the background to black"],"answer":1,"why":"Red and green can collapse to similar lightness/hue for deuteranopes. Dash patterns, point markers, and direct labels restore distinction through non-color channels."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Can your figure still be read by a colorblind reader? Test it on real journal figures.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-3-8-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">How simulation works</span></h3>\n<p>CVD simulation is not &quot;turn red into gray&quot;; it transforms colors according to cone response. The common Brettel / Viénot matrices model protanopia, deuteranopia, and tritanopia.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Simplified deuteranopia matrix, applied to linear sRGB\nconst deuteranopia = [\n  [0.625, 0.375, 0.0],\n  [0.7,   0.3,   0.0],\n  [0.0,   0.3,   0.7],\n];</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-3-8-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Test workflow</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Export the figure as PNG (not a cropped screenshot);</li>\n<li>Run all three simulations with Coblis / Color Oracle / the Color Lab in this site;</li>\n<li>Ask three questions: can categories still be distinguished? is order still readable? are key annotations still visible?</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"s-3-8-h3\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Findings</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Wong / Okabe-Ito / Paul Tol: distinguishable under all three CVD types;</li>\n<li>red-green contrast: nearly identical for deuteranopes — the most serious failure;</li>\n<li>Viridis: keeps lightness order under all three CVD types, suitable for continuous values;</li>\n<li>Nature / Science / Cell increasingly require CVD-safe palettes.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>One-line summary</strong>: color is a helper, not the only encoding. Shape, position, labels, and line style are the insurance that makes a chart readable for everyone.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-3-8-h1","text":"How simulation works","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-8-h2","text":"Test workflow","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-3-8-h3","text":"Findings","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Can your figure still be read by a colorblind reader? Test it on real journal figures. How simulation works CVD simulation is not \"turn red into gray\"; it transforms colors according to cone response. The common Brettel / Viénot matrices model protanopia, deuteranopia, and tritanopia. JavaScriptCopy // Simplified deuteranopia matrix, applied to linear sRGB const deuteranopia = [ [0.625, 0.375, 0.0], [0.7, 0.3, 0.0], [0.0, 0.3, 0.7], ]; Test workflow Export the figure as PNG (not a cropped screenshot); Run all three simulations with Coblis / Color Oracle / the Color Lab in this site; Ask three questions: can categories still be distinguished? is order still readable? are key annotations still visible? Findings Wong / Okabe-Ito / Paul Tol: distinguishable under all three CVD types; red-green contrast: nearly identical for deuteranopes — the most serious failure; Viridis: keeps lightness order under all three CVD types, suitable for continuous values; Nature / Science / Cell increasingly require CVD-safe palettes. One-line summary: color is a helper, not the only encoding. Shape, position, labels, and line style are the insurance that makes a chart readable for everyone.","chars":1003}},"4.1":{"id":"4.1","num":"4.1","chapter":"ch4","demo":"widelong","minutes":8,"related":["1.4","4.2"],"zh":{"title":"数据转换","rawTitle":"数据转换","short":"数据转换","subtitle":"宽格式与长格式：一行一个实体，还是一行一个观测。","bigIdea":"宽表方便人读，长表方便机器画；flatMap 是两者之间的桥。","points":["长格式每行一个观测，便于过滤、分组和 data-join。","flatMap 不修改原数组，保持纯函数。","d3.autoType 可以在读取时推断类型。"],"quiz":{"q":"50 行 × 4 个指标列的宽表，转成长表后有多少行？","options":["50","200","54"],"answer":1,"why":"每个实体的每个指标都变成一行：50 × 4 = 200 行。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>宽格式方便人读，长格式方便机器画。可视化之前，先把表&quot;摆平&quot;。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">你的原案例</span></h3>\n<p>1985 年美国 50 州犯罪数据（Crime）是一张典型的宽表：每行一个州，每列一个犯罪指标（谋杀、抢劫、入室盗窃……）。要把它画成散点图或热图，先要转成长表。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-4-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">两种表形，各有所长</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>形态</th>\n<th>结构</th>\n<th>优点</th>\n<th>适合</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>宽格式 wide</td>\n<td>一行一个实体，一列一个指标</td>\n<td>人眼读得懂、贴近 Excel</td>\n<td>录入、核对、展示原始表</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>长格式 long</td>\n<td>一行一个观测：<code>{state, metric, value}</code></td>\n<td>方便过滤、分组、绑定数据</td>\n<td>D3 data-join、分面、热图</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>转换只需要一次 <code>flatMap</code>：</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 宽 → 长：对每一行，遍历指标列，生成多条观测\nconst metrics = [&quot;murder&quot;, &quot;robbery&quot;, &quot;burglary&quot;, &quot;larceny_theft&quot;];\nconst long = data.flatMap(row =&gt;\n  metrics.map(metric =&gt; ({\n    state: row.state,\n    metric,\n    value: +row[metric],   // 字符串 → 数字\n  }))\n);\n// 50 行 × 4 列 → 200 行长表</code></pre>\n</div><p><code>d3.autoType</code> 可以在读取时自动推断列类型，省掉逐个 <code>+d.field</code>：</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const data = await d3.csv(&quot;data/crime.csv&quot;, d3.autoType);\n// population 自动变成 number，date 列自动变成 Date</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--warn\"><p><strong>易错点</strong>：<code>flatMap</code> 返回的是新数组，不会改动原始 <code>data</code>。如果先 <code>data.forEach(...push)</code> 再返回，就把&quot;纯函数&quot;变成了&quot;副作用&quot;，后续复用同一份数据时会出现重复行。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-1-h1","text":"你的原案例","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-4-1-h2","text":"两种表形，各有所长","kind":"plain"}],"text":"宽格式方便人读，长格式方便机器画。可视化之前，先把表\"摆平\"。 你的原案例 1985 年美国 50 州犯罪数据（Crime）是一张典型的宽表：每行一个州，每列一个犯罪指标（谋杀、抢劫、入室盗窃……）。要把它画成散点图或热图，先要转成长表。 两种表形，各有所长 形态 结构 优点 适合 宽格式 wide 一行一个实体，一列一个指标 人眼读得懂、贴近 Excel 录入、核对、展示原始表 长格式 long 一行一个观测：{state, metric, value} 方便过滤、分组、绑定数据 D3 data-join、分面、热图 转换只需要一次 flatMap： JavaScript复制 // 宽 → 长：对每一行，遍历指标列，生成多条观测 const metrics = [\"murder\", \"robbery\", \"burglary\", \"larceny_theft\"]; const long = data.flatMap(row => metrics.map(metric => ({ state: row.state, metric, value: +row[metric], // 字符串 → 数字 })) ); // 50 行 × 4 列 → 200 行长表 d3.autoType 可以在读取时自动推断列类型，省掉逐个 +d.field： JavaScript复制 const data = await d3.csv(\"data/crime.csv\", d3.autoType); // population 自动变成 number，date 列自动变成 Date 易错点：flatMap 返回的是新数组，不会改动原始 data。如果先 data.forEach(...push) 再返回，就把\"纯函数\"变成了\"副作用\"，后续复用同一份数据时会出现重复行。","chars":698},"en":{"title":"Data Transformation","rawTitle":"Data Transformation","short":"Reshaping","subtitle":"Wide vs long: one row per entity, or one row per observation.","bigIdea":"Wide tables are for humans; long tables are for machines. flatMap is the bridge.","points":["Long format has one row per observation, ideal for filtering, grouping, and joins.","flatMap returns a new array and keeps the transformation pure.","d3.autoType infers column types while reading."],"quiz":{"q":"A wide table with 50 rows × 4 metric columns becomes how many rows in long format?","options":["50","200","54"],"answer":1,"why":"Every metric of every entity becomes one row: 50 × 4 = 200."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Wide tables are easy for humans; long tables are easy for machines. Flatten the table before you visualize it.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Your original case</span></h3>\n<p>The 1985 US crime data (50 states) is a classic wide table: one row per state, one column per crime metric (murder, robbery, burglary...). To draw a scatterplot or a heatmap, reshape it into a long table first.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-4-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Two shapes, two strengths</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Shape</th>\n<th>Structure</th>\n<th>Strength</th>\n<th>Good for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Wide</td>\n<td>one row per entity, one column per metric</td>\n<td>human-readable, close to Excel</td>\n<td>data entry, checking, showing the raw table</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Long</td>\n<td>one row per observation: <code>{state, metric, value}</code></td>\n<td>easy to filter, group, bind</td>\n<td>D3 data-join, faceting, heatmaps</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>One <code>flatMap</code> does the conversion:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// wide → long: for each row, walk the metric columns\nconst metrics = [&quot;murder&quot;, &quot;robbery&quot;, &quot;burglary&quot;, &quot;larceny_theft&quot;];\nconst long = data.flatMap(row =&gt;\n  metrics.map(metric =&gt; ({\n    state: row.state,\n    metric,\n    value: +row[metric],   // string → number\n  }))\n);\n// 50 rows × 4 columns → 200 rows</code></pre>\n</div><p><code>d3.autoType</code> infers column types while reading, so you can skip the per-field <code>+d.field</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const data = await d3.csv(&quot;data/crime.csv&quot;, d3.autoType);\n// population becomes a number, date columns become Date</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--warn\"><p><strong>Pitfall</strong>: <code>flatMap</code> returns a new array and never mutates <code>data</code>. Pushing into the original array inside <code>forEach</code> turns a pure transformation into a side effect, and reusing the data later will duplicate rows.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-1-h1","text":"Your original case","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-4-1-h2","text":"Two shapes, two strengths","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Wide tables are easy for humans; long tables are easy for machines. Flatten the table before you visualize it. Your original case The 1985 US crime data (50 states) is a classic wide table: one row per state, one column per crime metric (murder, robbery, burglary...). To draw a scatterplot or a heatmap, reshape it into a long table first. Two shapes, two strengths Shape Structure Strength Good for Wide one row per entity, one column per metric human-readable, close to Excel data entry, checking, showing the raw table Long one row per observation: {state, metric, value} easy to filter, group, bind D3 data-join, faceting, heatmaps One flatMap does the conversion: JavaScriptCopy // wide → long: for each row, walk the metric columns const metrics = [\"murder\", \"robbery\", \"burglary\", \"larceny_theft\"]; const long = data.flatMap(row => metrics.map(metric => ({ state: row.state, metric, value: +row[metric], // string → number })) ); // 50 rows × 4 columns → 200 rows d3.autoType infers column types while reading, so you can skip the per-field +d.field: JavaScriptCopy const data = await d3.csv(\"data/crime.csv\", d3.autoType); // population becomes a number, date columns become Date Pitfall: flatMap returns a new array and never mutates data. Pushing into the original array inside forEach turns a pure transformation into a side effect, and reusing the data later will duplicate rows.","chars":1173}},"4.2":{"id":"4.2","num":"4.2","chapter":"ch4","demo":"spaces","minutes":9,"related":["4.1","4.3","1.3"],"zh":{"title":"坐标轴变换","rawTitle":"坐标轴变换","short":"坐标轴变换","subtitle":"数据空间 → 坐标系空间 → 屏幕空间，以及六种比例尺的选型。","bigIdea":"三层空间各司其职；比例尺选错，图形会「说谎」。","points":["domain 是数据，range 是像素；margin 只在屏幕空间加一次。","跨数量级用 log，面积编码用 sqrt，类别用 band。","不要把 margin 同时写进 range 和 translate。"],"quiz":{"q":"用圆的半径直接编码数值，会有什么问题？","options":["面积按半径平方增长，大值被严重夸大","圆画不出来","颜色会失真"],"answer":0,"why":"人眼读的是面积，而面积 ∝ r²。半径翻倍，面积变成 4 倍。应使用 scaleSqrt 让面积与数值成正比。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>数据空间 → 坐标系空间 → 屏幕空间。三层职责分明，混在一起就会乱套。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">三层空间</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>层</th>\n<th>输入</th>\n<th>输出</th>\n<th>由谁负责</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>数据空间</td>\n<td>原始数值，如人口 27,058,000、谋杀率 8</td>\n<td>定义域 domain</td>\n<td>业务与统计</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>坐标系空间</td>\n<td>归一化到 <code>0..innerWidth</code> 的坐标</td>\n<td>值域 range</td>\n<td><code>d3.scaleLinear()</code> 等比例尺</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>屏幕空间</td>\n<td>加上 margin 偏移后的像素坐标</td>\n<td><code>x + margin.left</code></td>\n<td>SVG 分组 <code>transform</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>分层的意义：坐标系空间里的图元可以复用，窗口变宽时只改 <code>range</code>，不用重算数据。<code>d3.axisBottom(x)</code> 会自动完成&quot;坐标系 → 屏幕&quot;的刻度与标签。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-4-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">比例尺选型</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>比例尺</th>\n<th>映射关系</th>\n<th>典型场景</th>\n<th>误用后果</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><code>scaleLinear</code></td>\n<td>线性</td>\n<td>温度、年龄、比率</td>\n<td>跨数量级时小值挤成一条线</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scaleLog</code></td>\n<td>对数</td>\n<td>人口 53 万 → 2700 万、收入</td>\n<td>含 0 或负值时无定义</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scaleSqrt</code></td>\n<td>平方根</td>\n<td>圆面积编码数值</td>\n<td>用半径直接编码面积会夸大 4 倍</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scaleBand</code></td>\n<td>离散分段</td>\n<td>柱状图的类别轴</td>\n<td>类别用线性轴会算出&quot;0.5 个班&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scalePoint</code></td>\n<td>离散点</td>\n<td>折线图的类别轴</td>\n<td>点会贴在轴起点，缺少留白</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scaleTime</code></td>\n<td>时间</td>\n<td>日期轴、时间序列</td>\n<td>用序号当 x 轴会抹平不等间隔</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 数据空间 → 坐标系空间 → 屏幕空间\nconst x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, d3.max(data, d =&gt; d.population)]).range([0, innerW]);\nconst y = d3.scaleLog().domain([1, d3.max(data, d =&gt; d.robbery)]).range([innerH, 0]);\n\nconst g = svg.append(&quot;g&quot;).attr(&quot;transform&quot;, `translate(${margin.left},${margin.top})`);\ng.append(&quot;g&quot;).attr(&quot;transform&quot;, `translate(0,${innerH})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x));</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>一个常见错误</strong>：把 margin 加进 <code>range</code>，又在 <code>&lt;g&gt;</code> 上 <code>translate</code> 一次，结果整体偏移了两遍。只在一处加偏移。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-2-h1","text":"三层空间","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-4-2-h2","text":"比例尺选型","kind":"plain"}],"text":"数据空间 → 坐标系空间 → 屏幕空间。三层职责分明，混在一起就会乱套。 三层空间 层 输入 输出 由谁负责 数据空间 原始数值，如人口 27,058,000、谋杀率 8 定义域 domain 业务与统计 坐标系空间 归一化到 0..innerWidth 的坐标 值域 range d3.scaleLinear() 等比例尺 屏幕空间 加上 margin 偏移后的像素坐标 x + margin.left SVG 分组 transform 分层的意义：坐标系空间里的图元可以复用，窗口变宽时只改 range，不用重算数据。d3.axisBottom(x) 会自动完成\"坐标系 → 屏幕\"的刻度与标签。 比例尺选型 比例尺 映射关系 典型场景 误用后果 scaleLinear 线性 温度、年龄、比率 跨数量级时小值挤成一条线 scaleLog 对数 人口 53 万 → 2700 万、收入 含 0 或负值时无定义 scaleSqrt 平方根 圆面积编码数值 用半径直接编码面积会夸大 4 倍 scaleBand 离散分段 柱状图的类别轴 类别用线性轴会算出\"0.5 个班\" scalePoint 离散点 折线图的类别轴 点会贴在轴起点，缺少留白 scaleTime 时间 日期轴、时间序列 用序号当 x 轴会抹平不等间隔 JavaScript复制 // 数据空间 → 坐标系空间 → 屏幕空间 const x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, d3.max(data, d => d.population)]).range([0, innerW]); const y = d3.scaleLog().domain([1, d3.max(data, d => d.robbery)]).range([innerH, 0]); const g = svg.append(\"g\").attr(\"transform\", `translate(${margin.left},${margin.top})`); g.append(\"g\").attr(\"transform\", `translate(0,${innerH})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x)); 一个常见错误：把 margin 加进 range，又在 <g> 上 translate 一次，结果整体偏移了两遍。只在一处加偏移。","chars":890},"en":{"title":"Axis Transformation","rawTitle":"Axis Transformation","short":"Axis Transform","subtitle":"Data space → coordinate space → screen space, and choosing among six scales.","bigIdea":"Each of the three spaces has one job; a wrong scale makes the chart lie.","points":["domain is data, range is pixels; add the margin once, in screen space.","Use log across orders of magnitude, sqrt for area, band for categories.","Never put the margin in both range and translate."],"quiz":{"q":"What is wrong with encoding values directly by circle radius?","options":["Area grows with the square of radius, exaggerating large values","Circles cannot be drawn","Colors become distorted"],"answer":0,"why":"People read area, and area ∝ r². Doubling the radius quadruples the area. Use scaleSqrt so area is proportional to value."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Data space → coordinate space → screen space. Keep the three layers separate or everything drifts.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">The three spaces</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>Input</th>\n<th>Output</th>\n<th>Owner</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Data space</td>\n<td>raw values, e.g. population 27,058,000, murder rate 8</td>\n<td>domain</td>\n<td>business / statistics</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Coordinate space</td>\n<td>normalized to <code>0..innerWidth</code></td>\n<td>range</td>\n<td><code>d3.scaleLinear()</code> and friends</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Screen space</td>\n<td>pixel position after the margin offset</td>\n<td><code>x + margin.left</code></td>\n<td>SVG group <code>transform</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><p>Separating them lets primitives be reused: when the window widens you only change <code>range</code>, not the data. <code>d3.axisBottom(x)</code> performs the coordinate → screen step for ticks and labels.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-4-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Choosing a scale</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Scale</th>\n<th>Mapping</th>\n<th>Typical use</th>\n<th>Failure mode</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><code>scaleLinear</code></td>\n<td>linear</td>\n<td>temperature, age, rates</td>\n<td>small values collapse when the range spans orders of magnitude</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scaleLog</code></td>\n<td>logarithmic</td>\n<td>population 530k → 27M, income</td>\n<td>undefined at 0 or negative values</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scaleSqrt</code></td>\n<td>square root</td>\n<td>circle area encoding</td>\n<td>encoding area by radius exaggerates 4×</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scaleBand</code></td>\n<td>discrete bands</td>\n<td>bar chart category axis</td>\n<td>a linear axis on categories yields &quot;0.5 of a class&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scalePoint</code></td>\n<td>discrete points</td>\n<td>line chart category axis</td>\n<td>points stick to the axis start without padding</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>scaleTime</code></td>\n<td>time</td>\n<td>date axes, time series</td>\n<td>using row index as x flattens uneven intervals</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// data space → coordinate space → screen space\nconst x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, d3.max(data, d =&gt; d.population)]).range([0, innerW]);\nconst y = d3.scaleLog().domain([1, d3.max(data, d =&gt; d.robbery)]).range([innerH, 0]);\n\nconst g = svg.append(&quot;g&quot;).attr(&quot;transform&quot;, `translate(${margin.left},${margin.top})`);\ng.append(&quot;g&quot;).attr(&quot;transform&quot;, `translate(0,${innerH})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x));</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--warn\"><p><strong>A common bug</strong>: adding the margin inside <code>range</code> and also translating the <code>&lt;g&gt;</code> shifts everything twice. Add the offset in exactly one place.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-2-h1","text":"The three spaces","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-4-2-h2","text":"Choosing a scale","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Data space → coordinate space → screen space. Keep the three layers separate or everything drifts. The three spaces Layer Input Output Owner Data space raw values, e.g. population 27,058,000, murder rate 8 domain business / statistics Coordinate space normalized to 0..innerWidth range d3.scaleLinear() and friends Screen space pixel position after the margin offset x + margin.left SVG group transform Separating them lets primitives be reused: when the window widens you only change range, not the data. d3.axisBottom(x) performs the coordinate → screen step for ticks and labels. Choosing a scale Scale Mapping Typical use Failure mode scaleLinear linear temperature, age, rates small values collapse when the range spans orders of magnitude scaleLog logarithmic population 530k → 27M, income undefined at 0 or negative values scaleSqrt square root circle area encoding encoding area by radius exaggerates 4× scaleBand discrete bands bar chart category axis a linear axis on categories yields \"0.5 of a class\" scalePoint discrete points line chart category axis points stick to the axis start without padding scaleTime time date axes, time series using row index as x flattens uneven intervals JavaScriptCopy // data space → coordinate space → screen space const x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, d3.max(data, d => d.population)]).range([0, innerW]); const y = d3.scaleLog().domain([1, d3.max(data, d => d.robbery)]).range([innerH, 0]); const g = svg.append(\"g\").attr(\"transform\", `translate(${margin.left},${margin.top})`); g.append(\"g\").attr(\"transform\", `translate(0,${innerH})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x)); A common bug: adding the margin inside range and also translating the <g> shifts everything twice. Add the offset in exactly one place.","chars":1503}},"4.3":{"id":"4.3","num":"4.3","chapter":"ch4","demo":"curves","minutes":8,"related":["4.2","5.2"],"zh":{"title":"曲线拟合","rawTitle":"曲线拟合","short":"曲线拟合","subtitle":"插值 vs 拟合，以及 D3 十种 curve 的选择原则。","bigIdea":"曲线是在讲「观测之间的故事」；先决定要经过点，还是只表达趋势。","points":["插值经过所有点，拟合只反映趋势。","时间序列优先 monotoneX，避免伪震荡。","Catmull-Rom 适合叙事，不适合精确读数。"],"quiz":{"q":"时间序列最稳妥的 curve 选择是？","options":["curveBasis","curveMonotoneX","curveCatmullRom"],"answer":1,"why":"monotoneX 经过所有点且保持单调，不会在相邻点之间产生虚假的上下震荡，适合时间序列。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>同一组点，换一种 <code>curve</code> 就是另一种&quot;叙事&quot;。选曲线之前，先问：这条线是在<strong>连接观测</strong>，还是在<strong>表达趋势</strong>？</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">插值 vs 拟合</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>插值 interpolation</th>\n<th>拟合 fitting</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>是否经过数据点</td>\n<td>全部经过</td>\n<td>可以不经过</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>代表方法</td>\n<td>Catmull-Rom、natural、monotoneX</td>\n<td>线性回归、LOESS、多项式最小二乘</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>适合</td>\n<td>数据点可信、需要连续读数</td>\n<td>数据有噪声、只想看趋势</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>风险</td>\n<td>在点之间&quot;编造&quot;出不存在的波动</td>\n<td>掩盖局部异常</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-4-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">D3 常用 curve</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>curve</th>\n<th>经过所有点</th>\n<th>保单调</th>\n<th>适合</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><code>curveLinear</code></td>\n<td>✅</td>\n<td>✅</td>\n<td>点少、强调真实读数</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveMonotoneX</code></td>\n<td>✅</td>\n<td>✅</td>\n<td>时间序列，避免伪震荡</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveCatmullRom</code></td>\n<td>✅</td>\n<td>❌</td>\n<td>叙事型折线、Storyline</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveNatural</code></td>\n<td>✅</td>\n<td>❌</td>\n<td>平滑的自然曲线</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveBasis</code></td>\n<td>❌</td>\n<td>❌</td>\n<td>强平滑、只看大趋势</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveStep</code> / <code>curveStepAfter</code></td>\n<td>✅（阶跃）</td>\n<td>✅</td>\n<td>状态切换、离散信号</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const line = d3.line()\n  .x(d =&gt; x(d.year))\n  .y(d =&gt; y(d.value))\n  .curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);   // 时间序列默认选它\n\npath.attr(&quot;d&quot;, line(series));</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>判断题</strong>：一条&quot;平滑得很漂亮&quot;的曲线，如果它经过了每个点、又在点之间上下摆动，那多半是 Catmull-Rom 在&quot;编故事&quot;。时间序列优先 <code>monotoneX</code>。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-3-h1","text":"插值 vs 拟合","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-4-3-h2","text":"D3 常用 curve","kind":"plain"}],"text":"同一组点，换一种 curve 就是另一种\"叙事\"。选曲线之前，先问：这条线是在连接观测，还是在表达趋势？ 插值 vs 拟合 插值 interpolation 拟合 fitting 是否经过数据点 全部经过 可以不经过 代表方法 Catmull-Rom、natural、monotoneX 线性回归、LOESS、多项式最小二乘 适合 数据点可信、需要连续读数 数据有噪声、只想看趋势 风险 在点之间\"编造\"出不存在的波动 掩盖局部异常 D3 常用 curve curve 经过所有点 保单调 适合 curveLinear ✅ ✅ 点少、强调真实读数 curveMonotoneX ✅ ✅ 时间序列，避免伪震荡 curveCatmullRom ✅ ❌ 叙事型折线、Storyline curveNatural ✅ ❌ 平滑的自然曲线 curveBasis ❌ ❌ 强平滑、只看大趋势 curveStep / curveStepAfter ✅（阶跃） ✅ 状态切换、离散信号 JavaScript复制 const line = d3.line() .x(d => x(d.year)) .y(d => y(d.value)) .curve(d3.curveMonotoneX); // 时间序列默认选它 path.attr(\"d\", line(series)); 判断题：一条\"平滑得很漂亮\"的曲线，如果它经过了每个点、又在点之间上下摆动，那多半是 Catmull-Rom 在\"编故事\"。时间序列优先 monotoneX。","chars":584},"en":{"title":"Curve Fitting","rawTitle":"Curve Fitting","short":"Curves","subtitle":"Interpolation vs fitting, and how to choose among D3's curve types.","bigIdea":"A curve tells a story between observations; first decide whether it must pass through them.","points":["Interpolation passes all points; fitting only expresses trend.","For time series, prefer monotoneX to avoid phantom oscillation.","Catmull-Rom suits narrative, not precise readings."],"quiz":{"q":"The safest curve for a time series is:","options":["curveBasis","curveMonotoneX","curveCatmullRom"],"answer":1,"why":"monotoneX passes every point and preserves monotonicity, so it never invents up-and-down wiggles between adjacent points."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>The same points, a different <code>curve</code>, tell a different story. Before choosing one, ask: is this line <strong>connecting observations</strong> or <strong>expressing a trend</strong>?</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Interpolation vs fitting</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Interpolation</th>\n<th>Fitting</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Passes through every point</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>not necessarily</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Representatives</td>\n<td>Catmull-Rom, natural, monotoneX</td>\n<td>linear regression, LOESS, polynomial least squares</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Good for</td>\n<td>trustworthy points, continuous readings</td>\n<td>noisy data, trend only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Risk</td>\n<td>invents wiggles between points</td>\n<td>hides local anomalies</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-4-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Common D3 curves</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>curve</th>\n<th>passes all points</th>\n<th>monotone</th>\n<th>good for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td><code>curveLinear</code></td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>few points, honest readings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveMonotoneX</code></td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>time series without phantom oscillation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveCatmullRom</code></td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>narrative lines, Storyline</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveNatural</code></td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>smooth natural curves</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveBasis</code></td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>no</td>\n<td>heavy smoothing, trend only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>curveStep</code> / <code>curveStepAfter</code></td>\n<td>yes (step)</td>\n<td>yes</td>\n<td>state changes, discrete signals</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const line = d3.line()\n  .x(d =&gt; x(d.year))\n  .y(d =&gt; y(d.value))\n  .curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);   // the default for time series\n\npath.attr(&quot;d&quot;, line(series));</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Quick check</strong>: a beautiful smooth curve that passes every point and still swings up and down between them is probably Catmull-Rom telling a story. For time series, prefer <code>monotoneX</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-3-h1","text":"Interpolation vs fitting","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-4-3-h2","text":"Common D3 curves","kind":"plain"}],"text":"The same points, a different curve, tell a different story. Before choosing one, ask: is this line connecting observations or expressing a trend? Interpolation vs fitting Interpolation Fitting Passes through every point yes not necessarily Representatives Catmull-Rom, natural, monotoneX linear regression, LOESS, polynomial least squares Good for trustworthy points, continuous readings noisy data, trend only Risk invents wiggles between points hides local anomalies Common D3 curves curve passes all points monotone good for curveLinear yes yes few points, honest readings curveMonotoneX yes yes time series without phantom oscillation curveCatmullRom yes no narrative lines, Storyline curveNatural yes no smooth natural curves curveBasis no no heavy smoothing, trend only curveStep / curveStepAfter yes (step) yes state changes, discrete signals JavaScriptCopy const line = d3.line() .x(d => x(d.year)) .y(d => y(d.value)) .curve(d3.curveMonotoneX); // the default for time series path.attr(\"d\", line(series)); Quick check: a beautiful smooth curve that passes every point and still swings up and down between them is probably Catmull-Rom telling a story. For time series, prefer monotoneX.","chars":1029}},"4.4":{"id":"4.4","num":"4.4","chapter":"ch4","demo":"slope","minutes":8,"related":["4.2","4.3"],"zh":{"title":"倾角感知","rawTitle":"倾角感知（45° 黄金角）","short":"45° 倾角","subtitle":"Cleveland 的斜率感知实验：为什么 45° 最准，以及如何用纵横比修正。","bigIdea":"读者判断的是「倾角」，不是「斜率」；纵横比会改变倾角。","points":["0° 与 90° 附近误差最大，45° 附近最准。","关键趋势线尽量落在 30°–60°。","跨数量级用 log 轴，把陡度压回 45°。"],"quiz":{"q":"同一组数据，把画布拉高一倍，读者会觉得增长：","options":["变慢","变快","不变"],"answer":1,"why":"拉高画布会增大纵向像素/单位，倾角变陡，读者感知到的增长速度变快。这正是「视觉谎言」的常见手法。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>同一组数据，拉宽或压扁画布，读者对&quot;增长有多快&quot;的判断会完全不同。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Cleveland 的发现</span></h3>\n<p>Cleveland（1984）让被试估计直线的斜率，结果呈 U 型：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>斜率接近 0°（几乎水平）或 90°（几乎垂直）时，估计误差最大；</li>\n<li>斜率约 <strong>45°</strong> 时，估计最准；</li>\n<li>人眼会把&quot;陡度&quot;适度夸张，感知幂律指数约 1.0–1.3。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-4-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">设计原则</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>关键趋势线的倾角尽量落在 <strong>30°–60°</strong>；</li>\n<li>对比两条增长曲线时，先把它们放进同一坐标系、同一尺度；</li>\n<li>跨数量级的数据用 <strong>log 轴</strong>，把陡度&quot;压&quot;回 45° 附近；</li>\n<li>不要用拉伸画布的方式制造&quot;增长更快&quot;的错觉——这叫<strong>视觉谎言</strong>。</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 让趋势线的中位倾角接近 45°：先算斜率，再反推纵横比\nconst slope = (yScale(yMax) - yScale(yMin)) / (xScale(xMax) - xScale(xMin));\nconst idealH = innerW * Math.abs(slope);</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>银行家四原则</strong>（banking to 45°）：在给定数据下，调整纵横比，使平均绝对倾角接近 45°。这不是&quot;好看&quot;，而是让读者的斜率判断误差最小。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-4-h1","text":"Cleveland 的发现","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-4-4-h2","text":"设计原则","kind":"plain"}],"text":"同一组数据，拉宽或压扁画布，读者对\"增长有多快\"的判断会完全不同。 Cleveland 的发现 Cleveland（1984）让被试估计直线的斜率，结果呈 U 型： 斜率接近 0°（几乎水平）或 90°（几乎垂直）时，估计误差最大； 斜率约 45° 时，估计最准； 人眼会把\"陡度\"适度夸张，感知幂律指数约 1.0–1.3。 设计原则 关键趋势线的倾角尽量落在 30°–60°； 对比两条增长曲线时，先把它们放进同一坐标系、同一尺度； 跨数量级的数据用 log 轴，把陡度\"压\"回 45° 附近； 不要用拉伸画布的方式制造\"增长更快\"的错觉——这叫视觉谎言。 JavaScript复制 // 让趋势线的中位倾角接近 45°：先算斜率，再反推纵横比 const slope = (yScale(yMax) - yScale(yMin)) / (xScale(xMax) - xScale(xMin)); const idealH = innerW * Math.abs(slope); 银行家四原则（banking to 45°）：在给定数据下，调整纵横比，使平均绝对倾角接近 45°。这不是\"好看\"，而是让读者的斜率判断误差最小。","chars":468},"en":{"title":"Slope Perception","rawTitle":"Slope Perception (45° Golden Angle)","short":"45° Angle","subtitle":"Cleveland's slope-perception experiments: why 45° is most accurate, and how aspect ratio changes it.","bigIdea":"Readers judge angle, not slope; aspect ratio changes the angle.","points":["Error is largest near 0° and 90°, smallest near 45°.","Keep key trends between 30° and 60°.","Use a log axis to bring steepness back near 45°."],"quiz":{"q":"Stretch the canvas vertically without changing the data. Readers perceive growth as:","options":["slower","faster","unchanged"],"answer":1,"why":"A taller canvas increases vertical pixels per unit, steepening the angle. Readers then perceive faster growth — a classic visual lie."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>The same data, stretched or squashed, changes how fast readers think it grew.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Cleveland&#39;s finding</span></h3>\n<p>Cleveland (1984) asked subjects to estimate line slopes. The error curve is U-shaped:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>error is largest near 0° (almost flat) and 90° (almost vertical);</li>\n<li>error is smallest around <strong>45°</strong>;</li>\n<li>people slightly exaggerate steepness; the perceptual power exponent is about 1.0–1.3.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"s-4-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Design rules</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Keep the key trend line between <strong>30° and 60°</strong>;</li>\n<li>When comparing two growth curves, put them in the same coordinate system and scale;</li>\n<li>For data spanning orders of magnitude use a <strong>log axis</strong> to bring steepness back near 45°;</li>\n<li>Never stretch the canvas to fake a steeper trend — that is a <strong>visual lie</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Aim the median slope at 45°: compute the slope, then solve for the aspect ratio\nconst slope = (yScale(yMax) - yScale(yMin)) / (xScale(xMax) - xScale(xMin));\nconst idealH = innerW * Math.abs(slope);</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Banking to 45°</strong>: adjust the aspect ratio so the average absolute slope is near 45°. This is not decoration; it minimizes the reader&#39;s slope-estimation error.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-4-h1","text":"Cleveland&#39;s finding","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-4-4-h2","text":"Design rules","kind":"plain"}],"text":"The same data, stretched or squashed, changes how fast readers think it grew. Cleveland&#39;s finding Cleveland (1984) asked subjects to estimate line slopes. The error curve is U-shaped: error is largest near 0° (almost flat) and 90° (almost vertical); error is smallest around 45°; people slightly exaggerate steepness; the perceptual power exponent is about 1.0–1.3. Design rules Keep the key trend line between 30° and 60°; When comparing two growth curves, put them in the same coordinate system and scale; For data spanning orders of magnitude use a log axis to bring steepness back near 45°; Never stretch the canvas to fake a steeper trend — that is a visual lie. JavaScriptCopy // Aim the median slope at 45°: compute the slope, then solve for the aspect ratio const slope = (yScale(yMax) - yScale(yMin)) / (xScale(xMax) - xScale(xMin)); const idealH = innerW * Math.abs(slope); Banking to 45°: adjust the aspect ratio so the average absolute slope is near 45°. This is not decoration; it minimizes the reader&#39;s slope-estimation error.","chars":880}},"4.5":{"id":"4.5","num":"4.5","chapter":"ch4","demo":"marching","minutes":10,"related":["4.2","5.3"],"zh":{"title":"等值线","rawTitle":"等值线（Marching Squares）","short":"等值线","subtitle":"Marching Squares：16 种 case、鞍点处理，以及从 2D 到 3D 的扩展。","bigIdea":"等值线是把连续标量场离散化后，沿「高于阈值/低于阈值」的边界走出来的。","points":["四角编码成 0–15，共 16 种 case。","case 5 与 10 是鞍点，需要用中心值决定连法。","扩展到三维就是 Marching Cubes，256 种 case。"],"quiz":{"q":"Marching Squares 的一个格子有 4 个角，最多可能产生几条线段？","options":["1","2","4"],"answer":1,"why":"每个格子最多被边界穿过两次，对应 2 条线段（鞍点情况）。0/1/2 是全部可能。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>标量场是一张&quot;高度表&quot;，等值线是把&quot;同一高度&quot;的点连起来的曲线。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-5-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">算法原理</span></h3>\n<p>把平面离散成网格，每个格子看 4 个角：高于阈值记 1，低于记 0，得到 4 位二进制编号 <code>0–15</code>（共 16 种 case）。每种 case 对应 0、1 或 2 条线段，把&quot;高区&quot;与&quot;低区&quot;分开。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>角编码</th>\n<th>位</th>\n<th>说明</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>左下 BL</td>\n<td>bit0</td>\n<td>起点</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>右下 BR</td>\n<td>bit1</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>右上 TR</td>\n<td>bit2</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>左上 TL</td>\n<td>bit3</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 四个角的布尔值 → case 编号\nconst c = (bl &gt; t ? 1 : 0) | (br &gt; t ? 2 : 0) | (tr &gt; t ? 4 : 0) | (tl &gt; t ? 8 : 0);\n// c = 0 或 15：整格同侧，无线段\n// c = 5 或 10：鞍点，需要按中心值决定连法</code></pre>\n</div><p>扩展到三维就是 <strong>Marching Cubes</strong>（Lorensen &amp; Cline, 1987）：2⁸ = 256 种 case，用于 MRI / CT 的等值面提取。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-4-5-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">应用场景</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>地形等高线、气压/气温等值线；</li>\n<li>核密度估计（KDE）的密度轮廓；</li>\n<li>医学影像的三维重建；</li>\n<li>把散点&quot;密度&quot;变成可读的区域边界。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>实现提示</strong>：网格越密，等值线越平滑，但计算量按 <code>n²</code> 增长。交互式阈值滑块建议先用 60×60 网格，够用且流畅。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-5-h1","text":"算法原理","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-4-5-h2","text":"应用场景","kind":"plain"}],"text":"标量场是一张\"高度表\"，等值线是把\"同一高度\"的点连起来的曲线。 算法原理 把平面离散成网格，每个格子看 4 个角：高于阈值记 1，低于记 0，得到 4 位二进制编号 0–15（共 16 种 case）。每种 case 对应 0、1 或 2 条线段，把\"高区\"与\"低区\"分开。 角编码 位 说明 左下 BL bit0 起点 右下 BR bit1 右上 TR bit2 左上 TL bit3 JavaScript复制 // 四个角的布尔值 → case 编号 const c = (bl > t ? 1 : 0) | (br > t ? 2 : 0) | (tr > t ? 4 : 0) | (tl > t ? 8 : 0); // c = 0 或 15：整格同侧，无线段 // c = 5 或 10：鞍点，需要按中心值决定连法 扩展到三维就是 Marching Cubes（Lorensen & Cline, 1987）：2⁸ = 256 种 case，用于 MRI / CT 的等值面提取。 应用场景 地形等高线、气压/气温等值线； 核密度估计（KDE）的密度轮廓； 医学影像的三维重建； 把散点\"密度\"变成可读的区域边界。 实现提示：网格越密，等值线越平滑，但计算量按 n² 增长。交互式阈值滑块建议先用 60×60 网格，够用且流畅。","chars":461},"en":{"title":"Contours","rawTitle":"Contours (Marching Squares)","short":"Contours","subtitle":"Marching Squares: 16 cases, saddle points, and the extension from 2D to 3D.","bigIdea":"A contour traces the boundary between above-threshold and below-threshold regions of a discretized scalar field.","points":["Four corner bits encode cases 0–15.","Cases 5 and 10 are saddles; use the center value to choose the connection.","In 3D this becomes Marching Cubes with 256 cases."],"quiz":{"q":"How many line segments can one Marching Squares cell produce at most?","options":["1","2","4"],"answer":1,"why":"A cell boundary can cross at most twice, producing 2 segments in the saddle cases. The possibilities are 0, 1, or 2."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>A scalar field is a height map; a contour line connects points at the same height.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-4-5-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">How the algorithm works</span></h3>\n<p>Discretize the plane into a grid. For each cell, compare its four corners with the threshold: above = 1, below = 0. The four bits form a case number <code>0–15</code> (16 cases). Each case contributes zero, one, or two line segments separating the high region from the low region.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Corner</th>\n<th>Bit</th>\n<th>Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>bottom-left BL</td>\n<td>bit0</td>\n<td>start</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>bottom-right BR</td>\n<td>bit1</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>top-right TR</td>\n<td>bit2</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>top-left TL</td>\n<td>bit3</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// four corner booleans → case number\nconst c = (bl &gt; t ? 1 : 0) | (br &gt; t ? 2 : 0) | (tr &gt; t ? 4 : 0) | (tl &gt; t ? 8 : 0);\n// c = 0 or 15: the whole cell is on one side, no segment\n// c = 5 or 10: saddle point, use the center value to choose the connection</code></pre>\n</div><p>In 3D this becomes <strong>Marching Cubes</strong> (Lorensen &amp; Cline, 1987): 2⁸ = 256 cases, used to extract isosurfaces from MRI / CT volumes.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-4-5-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Applications</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>terrain contours, isobars and isotherms;</li>\n<li>density contours from kernel density estimation (KDE);</li>\n<li>3D reconstruction from medical scans;</li>\n<li>turning scatter density into readable region boundaries.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Implementation tip</strong>: a denser grid gives smoother contours, but cost grows as <code>n²</code>. For an interactive threshold slider, a 60×60 grid is smooth enough and stays fast.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-4-5-h1","text":"How the algorithm works","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-4-5-h2","text":"Applications","kind":"plain"}],"text":"A scalar field is a height map; a contour line connects points at the same height. How the algorithm works Discretize the plane into a grid. For each cell, compare its four corners with the threshold: above = 1, below = 0. The four bits form a case number 0–15 (16 cases). Each case contributes zero, one, or two line segments separating the high region from the low region. Corner Bit Note bottom-left BL bit0 start bottom-right BR bit1 top-right TR bit2 top-left TL bit3 JavaScriptCopy // four corner booleans → case number const c = (bl > t ? 1 : 0) | (br > t ? 2 : 0) | (tr > t ? 4 : 0) | (tl > t ? 8 : 0); // c = 0 or 15: the whole cell is on one side, no segment // c = 5 or 10: saddle point, use the center value to choose the connection In 3D this becomes Marching Cubes (Lorensen & Cline, 1987): 2⁸ = 256 cases, used to extract isosurfaces from MRI / CT volumes. Applications terrain contours, isobars and isotherms; density contours from kernel density estimation (KDE); 3D reconstruction from medical scans; turning scatter density into readable region boundaries. Implementation tip: a denser grid gives smoother contours, but cost grows as n². For an interactive threshold slider, a 60×60 grid is smooth enough and stays fast.","chars":1007}},"5.1":{"id":"5.1","num":"5.1","chapter":"ch5","demo":"timeattrs","minutes":7,"related":["5.2","5.3"],"zh":{"title":"时间属性","rawTitle":"时间属性","short":"时间属性","subtitle":"有序、连续、周期、独立于空间、有结构：五个属性如何决定图表选择。","bigIdea":"先问「我想让读者看到趋势、周期还是叙事」，再决定时间域。","points":["有序性要求 x 轴按时间排序。","周期性适合日历、螺旋等循环时间域。","结构性意味着闰年、月末、时区都要显式处理。"],"quiz":{"q":"要展示「每年同一季节」的规律，哪种时间域最合适？","options":["线性时间轴","循环时间域（日历/螺旋）","无序类别轴"],"answer":1,"why":"循环时间域把相同相位排在同一位置，季节规律不会被线性轴拉开；线性轴更适合看长期趋势。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>画时序图之前，先把&quot;时间&quot;这件事拆开看。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">五个核心属性</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>属性</th>\n<th>含义</th>\n<th>对设计的约束</th>\n<th>忽略后的后果</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>有序性</td>\n<td>两个事件有先后，且与因果相连</td>\n<td>x 轴必须按时间排序</td>\n<td>散点错位成噪声，趋势读不出来</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>连续性</td>\n<td>两个时间点之间总存在另一个时间点</td>\n<td>连续数据才能连线；离散事件用阶梯/点</td>\n<td>离散状态被连成&quot;连续变化&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>周期性</td>\n<td>季节、昼夜、周循环</td>\n<td>可用循环时间域（日历、螺旋）</td>\n<td>季节趋势被线性轴&quot;抹平&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>独立于空间</td>\n<td>时间与空间相关，但通常分开处理</td>\n<td>时间只占一个轴，不混用空间坐标</td>\n<td>双轴混读，因果关系被误导</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>结构性</td>\n<td>年/月/日/时/分/秒，自然分割 + 人为定义</td>\n<td>闰年、月末、工作日/周末要特殊处理</td>\n<td>跨月、跨年、闰日出现错位</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-5-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">属性 → 图表选择</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>你想让读者看到</th>\n<th>优先选择</th>\n<th>原因</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>长期趋势</td>\n<td>折线图 / 面积图</td>\n<td>线性时间域最直观</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>周内规律、节假日异常</td>\n<td>日历热图</td>\n<td>星期对齐，异常一眼可见</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>年度周期、循环节律</td>\n<td>螺旋图 / 极坐标</td>\n<td>每个回路 = 一个周期</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>多角色/多事件的叙事</td>\n<td>Storyline</td>\n<td>线的聚散表达关系变化</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>精确的单点读数</td>\n<td>折线 + 点 + 提示框</td>\n<td>位置通道最准</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 时间解析：不要依赖 new Date(&quot;2007/8/15&quot;) 的浏览器差异\nconst parse = d3.timeParse(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;);\nconst date = parse(&quot;2024-03-01&quot;);        // 明确、可移植\nconst fmt = d3.timeFormat(&quot;%Y 年第 %j 天&quot;);</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--warn\"><p><strong>易错点</strong>：<code>new Date(&quot;2024-03-01&quot;)</code> 按 UTC 解析，而 <code>new Date(&quot;2024/03/01&quot;)</code> 按本地时区解析。跨时区展示时，同一天可能变成前一天。统一用 <code>d3.timeParse</code> 或 ISO 字符串 + <code>timeParse</code>。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-1-h1","text":"五个核心属性","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-5-1-h2","text":"属性 → 图表选择","kind":"plain"}],"text":"画时序图之前，先把\"时间\"这件事拆开看。 五个核心属性 属性 含义 对设计的约束 忽略后的后果 有序性 两个事件有先后，且与因果相连 x 轴必须按时间排序 散点错位成噪声，趋势读不出来 连续性 两个时间点之间总存在另一个时间点 连续数据才能连线；离散事件用阶梯/点 离散状态被连成\"连续变化\" 周期性 季节、昼夜、周循环 可用循环时间域（日历、螺旋） 季节趋势被线性轴\"抹平\" 独立于空间 时间与空间相关，但通常分开处理 时间只占一个轴，不混用空间坐标 双轴混读，因果关系被误导 结构性 年/月/日/时/分/秒，自然分割 + 人为定义 闰年、月末、工作日/周末要特殊处理 跨月、跨年、闰日出现错位 属性 → 图表选择 你想让读者看到 优先选择 原因 长期趋势 折线图 / 面积图 线性时间域最直观 周内规律、节假日异常 日历热图 星期对齐，异常一眼可见 年度周期、循环节律 螺旋图 / 极坐标 每个回路 = 一个周期 多角色/多事件的叙事 Storyline 线的聚散表达关系变化 精确的单点读数 折线 + 点 + 提示框 位置通道最准 JavaScript复制 // 时间解析：不要依赖 new Date(\"2007/8/15\") 的浏览器差异 const parse = d3.timeParse(\"%Y-%m-%d\"); const date = parse(\"2024-03-01\"); // 明确、可移植 const fmt = d3.timeFormat(\"%Y 年第 %j 天\"); 易错点：new Date(\"2024-03-01\") 按 UTC 解析，而 new Date(\"2024/03/01\") 按本地时区解析。跨时区展示时，同一天可能变成前一天。统一用 d3.timeParse 或 ISO 字符串 + timeParse。","chars":679},"en":{"title":"Temporal Attributes","rawTitle":"Temporal Attributes","short":"Temporal Attributes","subtitle":"Ordered, continuous, periodic, space-independent, structured: how five properties drive chart choice.","bigIdea":"Ask whether readers should see trend, cycle, or narrative; that decides the time domain.","points":["Order requires a time-sorted x axis.","Periodicity suits cyclic domains such as calendars and spirals.","Structure means leap years, month ends, and time zones need explicit handling."],"quiz":{"q":"To show the pattern of 'the same season each year', which time domain fits best?","options":["a linear time axis","a cyclic domain (calendar/spiral)","an unordered category axis"],"answer":1,"why":"A cyclic domain puts the same phase in the same place, so seasonal patterns are not spread apart by a linear axis. A linear axis is better for long-term trend."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Before drawing a time-series chart, take &quot;time&quot; apart.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-1-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Five core properties</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Property</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th>Design constraint</th>\n<th>Cost of ignoring it</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Ordered</td>\n<td>events have an order, tied to causality</td>\n<td>the x axis must be time-sorted</td>\n<td>points misalign into noise; trends vanish</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Continuous</td>\n<td>another instant always exists between two</td>\n<td>connect continuous data; use steps/points for discrete events</td>\n<td>discrete states get drawn as continuous change</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Periodic</td>\n<td>seasons, day/night, weekly cycles</td>\n<td>cyclic time domains (calendar, spiral)</td>\n<td>seasonal patterns are flattened by a linear axis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Independent of space</td>\n<td>time correlates with space but is usually handled separately</td>\n<td>time gets one axis; do not mix spatial coordinates</td>\n<td>dual-axis confusion and false causality</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Structured</td>\n<td>year/month/day/hour/min/sec, natural + human-made</td>\n<td>handle leap years, month ends, weekdays/weekends</td>\n<td>misalignment across months, years, leap days</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><h3 id=\"s-5-1-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Property → chart choice</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>What readers should see</th>\n<th>Prefer</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>Long-term trend</td>\n<td>line / area chart</td>\n<td>a linear time domain is the most direct</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Weekly rhythm, holiday anomalies</td>\n<td>calendar heatmap</td>\n<td>weekdays align; anomalies pop out</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Annual cycle, rhythm</td>\n<td>spiral / polar</td>\n<td>one loop = one cycle</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi-actor narrative</td>\n<td>Storyline</td>\n<td>converging and diverging lines express relationships</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Precise single readings</td>\n<td>line + points + tooltip</td>\n<td>position is the most accurate channel</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div><div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// Parse time explicitly; do not rely on browser differences in new Date(&quot;2007/8/15&quot;)\nconst parse = d3.timeParse(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;);\nconst date = parse(&quot;2024-03-01&quot;);        // explicit and portable\nconst fmt = d3.timeFormat(&quot;%Y day %j&quot;);</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--warn\"><p><strong>Pitfall</strong>: <code>new Date(&quot;2024-03-01&quot;)</code> parses as UTC, while <code>new Date(&quot;2024/03/01&quot;)</code> parses as local time. Across time zones the same day can shift to the previous day. Use <code>d3.timeParse</code> or ISO strings consistently.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-1-h1","text":"Five core properties","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-5-1-h2","text":"Property → chart choice","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Before drawing a time-series chart, take \"time\" apart. Five core properties Property Meaning Design constraint Cost of ignoring it Ordered events have an order, tied to causality the x axis must be time-sorted points misalign into noise; trends vanish Continuous another instant always exists between two connect continuous data; use steps/points for discrete events discrete states get drawn as continuous change Periodic seasons, day/night, weekly cycles cyclic time domains (calendar, spiral) seasonal patterns are flattened by a linear axis Independent of space time correlates with space but is usually handled separately time gets one axis; do not mix spatial coordinates dual-axis confusion and false causality Structured year/month/day/hour/min/sec, natural + human-made handle leap years, month ends, weekdays/weekends misalignment across months, years, leap days Property → chart choice What readers should see Prefer Why Long-term trend line / area chart a linear time domain is the most direct Weekly rhythm, holiday anomalies calendar heatmap weekdays align; anomalies pop out Annual cycle, rhythm spiral / polar one loop = one cycle Multi-actor narrative Storyline converging and diverging lines express relationships Precise single readings line + points + tooltip position is the most accurate channel JavaScriptCopy // Parse time explicitly; do not rely on browser differences in new Date(\"2007/8/15\") const parse = d3.timeParse(\"%Y-%m-%d\"); const date = parse(\"2024-03-01\"); // explicit and portable const fmt = d3.timeFormat(\"%Y day %j\"); Pitfall: new Date(\"2024-03-01\") parses as UTC, while new Date(\"2024/03/01\") parses as local time. Across time zones the same day can shift to the previous day. Use d3.timeParse or ISO strings consistently.","chars":1510}},"5.2":{"id":"5.2","num":"5.2","chapter":"ch5","demo":"line","minutes":9,"related":["5.1","5.3","4.3"],"zh":{"title":"标准时间可视化","rawTitle":"标准时间可视化（折线图）","short":"折线图","subtitle":"标准时序图：真实时间间隔、点数决定平滑方式、交互服务于读数。","bigIdea":"折线图的第一原则是时间轴按真实间隔，而不是按行号。","points":["用 scaleTime，不要用序号当 x 轴。","≤50 点用 linear，50–500 用 monotoneX。","hover 给精确值，brush 选时间段，双击复位。"],"quiz":{"q":"把 1900–2020 的数据按「行号 1..N」画在 x 轴上，会有什么问题？","options":["颜色会变","不等间隔的年份被画成等距，趋势被扭曲","无法显示图例"],"answer":1,"why":"序号轴假设相邻行间隔相等。缺失年份或不等间隔时，时间被压缩/拉伸，趋势的斜率不再可信。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>x 轴 = 时间，y 轴 = 度量。它是最常见、也最容易被画错的时序图。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">你的原案例</span></h3>\n<p>法国人名 1900–2020 年的使用频率（Marie / Jean / Camille）。原始页面附带词云、鼠标高亮和时间段筛选。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-5-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">折线图的三条设计规则</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>时间轴按真实间隔</strong>：用 <code>scaleTime</code>，不要用序号。1900→1950 与 1950→2020 的宽度应该反映真实年数。</li>\n<li><strong>点数决定平滑方式</strong>：≤50 点用 <code>curveLinear</code>；50–500 点用 <code>curveMonotoneX</code>；&gt;500 点考虑面积或箱形聚合。</li>\n<li><strong>交互服务于读数</strong>：hover 显示精确值，brush 选择时间段，双击复位。</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const x = d3.scaleTime()\n  .domain(d3.extent(data, d =&gt; d.date))\n  .range([0, width]);\n\nconst y = d3.scaleLinear()\n  .domain([0, d3.max(data, d =&gt; d.value)]).nice()\n  .range([height, 0]);\n\nconst line = d3.line()\n  .x(d =&gt; x(d.date))\n  .y(d =&gt; y(d.value))\n  .curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);\n\nsvg.append(&quot;path&quot;).datum(data).attr(&quot;d&quot;, line)\n  .attr(&quot;fill&quot;, &quot;none&quot;).attr(&quot;stroke&quot;, &quot;var(--cinnabar)&quot;);</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>常见错误</strong>：把多年数据按&quot;月份序号 1–12&quot;堆叠，跨年时折线会从 12 月直接连回 1 月，形成一条不存在的&quot;断崖&quot;。跨年数据必须保留真实日期。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-2-h1","text":"你的原案例","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-5-2-h2","text":"折线图的三条设计规则","kind":"plain"}],"text":"x 轴 = 时间，y 轴 = 度量。它是最常见、也最容易被画错的时序图。 你的原案例 法国人名 1900–2020 年的使用频率（Marie / Jean / Camille）。原始页面附带词云、鼠标高亮和时间段筛选。 折线图的三条设计规则 时间轴按真实间隔：用 scaleTime，不要用序号。1900→1950 与 1950→2020 的宽度应该反映真实年数。 点数决定平滑方式：≤50 点用 curveLinear；50–500 点用 curveMonotoneX；>500 点考虑面积或箱形聚合。 交互服务于读数：hover 显示精确值，brush 选择时间段，双击复位。 JavaScript复制 const x = d3.scaleTime() .domain(d3.extent(data, d => d.date)) .range([0, width]); const y = d3.scaleLinear() .domain([0, d3.max(data, d => d.value)]).nice() .range([height, 0]); const line = d3.line() .x(d => x(d.date)) .y(d => y(d.value)) .curve(d3.curveMonotoneX); svg.append(\"path\").datum(data).attr(\"d\", line) .attr(\"fill\", \"none\").attr(\"stroke\", \"var(--cinnabar)\"); 常见错误：把多年数据按\"月份序号 1–12\"堆叠，跨年时折线会从 12 月直接连回 1 月，形成一条不存在的\"断崖\"。跨年数据必须保留真实日期。","chars":675},"en":{"title":"Standard Temporal Visualization","rawTitle":"Standard Temporal Visualization (Line Chart)","short":"Line Chart","subtitle":"The standard time chart: real intervals, point count drives smoothing, interaction serves reading.","bigIdea":"The first rule is a time axis with real intervals, not row indices.","points":["Use scaleTime, never row index, for the x axis.","≤50 points linear; 50–500 monotoneX.","Hover for exact values, brush to select periods, double-click to reset."],"quiz":{"q":"Plotting 1900–2020 against row index 1..N creates what problem?","options":["Colors change","Uneven year gaps become equal, distorting the trend","The legend disappears"],"answer":1,"why":"An index axis assumes equal spacing between rows. Missing years or uneven gaps get compressed or stretched, so slopes no longer reflect real rates."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>x axis = time, y axis = measure. It is the most common time-series chart and one of the easiest to get wrong.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-2-h1\" class=\"blk blk--case\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Your original case</span></h3>\n<p>The usage frequency of French given names from 1900 to 2020 (Marie / Jean / Camille). The original page added a word cloud, hover highlighting, and a time-range filter.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-5-2-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Three design rules</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Use real time intervals</strong>: <code>scaleTime</code>, not row indices. 1900→1950 and 1950→2020 should have widths proportional to their real durations.</li>\n<li><strong>Let point count choose the smoothing</strong>: ≤50 points <code>curveLinear</code>; 50–500 <code>curveMonotoneX</code>; &gt;500 consider area or binned aggregation.</li>\n<li><strong>Interaction serves reading</strong>: hover for exact values, brush to select a period, double-click to reset.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const x = d3.scaleTime()\n  .domain(d3.extent(data, d =&gt; d.date))\n  .range([0, width]);\n\nconst y = d3.scaleLinear()\n  .domain([0, d3.max(data, d =&gt; d.value)]).nice()\n  .range([height, 0]);\n\nconst line = d3.line()\n  .x(d =&gt; x(d.date))\n  .y(d =&gt; y(d.value))\n  .curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);\n\nsvg.append(&quot;path&quot;).datum(data).attr(&quot;d&quot;, line)\n  .attr(&quot;fill&quot;, &quot;none&quot;).attr(&quot;stroke&quot;, &quot;var(--cinnabar)&quot;);</code></pre>\n</div><blockquote class=\"callout callout--warn\"><p><strong>Common bug</strong>: stacking multi-year data by &quot;month index 1–12&quot; makes the line jump from December back to January, creating a cliff that does not exist. Keep real dates for multi-year data.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-2-h1","text":"Your original case","kind":"case"},{"id":"s-5-2-h2","text":"Three design rules","kind":"plain"}],"text":"x axis = time, y axis = measure. It is the most common time-series chart and one of the easiest to get wrong. Your original case The usage frequency of French given names from 1900 to 2020 (Marie / Jean / Camille). The original page added a word cloud, hover highlighting, and a time-range filter. Three design rules Use real time intervals: scaleTime, not row indices. 1900→1950 and 1950→2020 should have widths proportional to their real durations. Let point count choose the smoothing: ≤50 points curveLinear; 50–500 curveMonotoneX; >500 consider area or binned aggregation. Interaction serves reading: hover for exact values, brush to select a period, double-click to reset. JavaScriptCopy const x = d3.scaleTime() .domain(d3.extent(data, d => d.date)) .range([0, width]); const y = d3.scaleLinear() .domain([0, d3.max(data, d => d.value)]).nice() .range([height, 0]); const line = d3.line() .x(d => x(d.date)) .y(d => y(d.value)) .curve(d3.curveMonotoneX); svg.append(\"path\").datum(data).attr(\"d\", line) .attr(\"fill\", \"none\").attr(\"stroke\", \"var(--cinnabar)\"); Common bug: stacking multi-year data by \"month index 1–12\" makes the line jump from December back to January, creating a cliff that does not exist. Keep real dates for multi-year data.","chars":1073}},"5.3":{"id":"5.3","num":"5.3","chapter":"ch5","demo":"calendar","minutes":9,"related":["5.1","5.2","4.5"],"zh":{"title":"日历热图","rawTitle":"日历热图（van Wijk）","short":"日历热图","subtitle":"周 = 列、星期 = 行：把全年数据排成一张可扫视的日历。","bigIdea":"日历热图把「星期」这个周期维度对齐，让周内规律和节假日异常一眼可见。","points":["x = 周序号，y = 星期几，颜色 = 数值。","月份分隔线用「与前一日是否同月」判断。","顺序型 colormap，周一/周日起点要统一。"],"quiz":{"q":"日历热图中，月份分隔线最稳妥的判断方式是？","options":["每月 1 日画一条线","比较当前格与前一格是否同月","按 30 天等距画线"],"answer":1,"why":"数据可能从周中开始、月份长度不一；比较相邻两格是否同月，能把线落在月份真正切换的那一格。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>以&quot;周 = 列、星期 = 行&quot;排列全年数据，把周期性和异常同时显示出来。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">布局算法</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>每个日期计算它在年内的&quot;周序号&quot;和&quot;星期几&quot;；</li>\n<li>x = 周序号，y = 星期几，颜色 = 数值；</li>\n<li>月份之间画分隔线，比 7×53 的网格更容易定位；</li>\n<li>颜色用顺序型 colormap（如 Viridis），不要用彩虹。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// 周序号与星期几：以周一为一周起点\nconst week = d3.timeWeek.count(d3.timeYear(date), date);\nconst weekday = (date.getDay() + 6) % 7;   // 周一=0 … 周日=6\n\nconst x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, 53]).range([0, width]);\nconst y = d3.scaleBand().domain(d3.range(7)).range([0, height]);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-5-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">月份分隔线的巧妙判断</span></h3>\n<p>不要按&quot;每月 1 日&quot;画线，而是比较<strong>上一格与当前格是否同月</strong>：</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const isMonthDivider = (d, i) =&gt; i &gt; 0 &amp;&amp;\n  d.getMonth() !== data[i - 1].getMonth();</code></pre>\n</div><p>这样无论数据从周几开始、月份长度如何变化，分隔线都准确落在&quot;月份切换的那一格&quot;。</p>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>设计要点</strong>：每周从周一还是周日开始，会改变&quot;周末&quot;在视觉上的位置。中国习惯周一，美国习惯周日，团队内要统一并在图注里说明。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-3-h1","text":"布局算法","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-5-3-h2","text":"月份分隔线的巧妙判断","kind":"plain"}],"text":"以\"周 = 列、星期 = 行\"排列全年数据，把周期性和异常同时显示出来。 布局算法 每个日期计算它在年内的\"周序号\"和\"星期几\"； x = 周序号，y = 星期几，颜色 = 数值； 月份之间画分隔线，比 7×53 的网格更容易定位； 颜色用顺序型 colormap（如 Viridis），不要用彩虹。 JavaScript复制 // 周序号与星期几：以周一为一周起点 const week = d3.timeWeek.count(d3.timeYear(date), date); const weekday = (date.getDay() + 6) % 7; // 周一=0 … 周日=6 const x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, 53]).range([0, width]); const y = d3.scaleBand().domain(d3.range(7)).range([0, height]); 月份分隔线的巧妙判断 不要按\"每月 1 日\"画线，而是比较上一格与当前格是否同月： JavaScript复制 const isMonthDivider = (d, i) => i > 0 && d.getMonth() !== data[i - 1].getMonth(); 这样无论数据从周几开始、月份长度如何变化，分隔线都准确落在\"月份切换的那一格\"。 设计要点：每周从周一还是周日开始，会改变\"周末\"在视觉上的位置。中国习惯周一，美国习惯周日，团队内要统一并在图注里说明。","chars":591},"en":{"title":"Calendar Heatmap","rawTitle":"Calendar Heatmap (van Wijk)","short":"Calendar Heatmap","subtitle":"Week = column, weekday = row: arrange a whole year into a scannable calendar.","bigIdea":"A calendar heatmap aligns the weekly cycle so weekday patterns and holiday anomalies pop out.","points":["x = week index, y = weekday, color = value.","Month dividers compare the current cell with the previous day.","Use a sequential colormap and one weekday convention."],"quiz":{"q":"What is the most robust way to place month dividers in a calendar heatmap?","options":["Draw a line on the 1st of each month","Compare the current cell with the previous one for a month change","Draw lines every 30 days"],"answer":1,"why":"Data may start mid-week and months have different lengths. Comparing adjacent cells places the divider on the exact cell where the month changes."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Arrange a whole year as &quot;week = column, weekday = row&quot; to show cycles and anomalies at once.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-3-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Layout algorithm</span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>For each date, compute its week-of-year and weekday;</li>\n<li>x = week index, y = weekday, color = value;</li>\n<li>draw dividers between months; they make a 7×53 grid readable;</li>\n<li>use a sequential colormap (e.g. Viridis), never a rainbow.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">// week index and weekday, with Monday as the first day\nconst week = d3.timeWeek.count(d3.timeYear(date), date);\nconst weekday = (date.getDay() + 6) % 7;   // Monday=0 … Sunday=6\n\nconst x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, 53]).range([0, width]);\nconst y = d3.scaleBand().domain(d3.range(7)).range([0, height]);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-5-3-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">The clever month-divider test</span></h3>\n<p>Do not draw lines on &quot;the 1st of each month&quot;; compare the current cell with the previous one:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const isMonthDivider = (d, i) =&gt; i &gt; 0 &amp;&amp;\n  d.getMonth() !== data[i - 1].getMonth();</code></pre>\n</div><p>This places the divider on the exact cell where the month changes, regardless of the starting weekday or month length.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--design\"><p><strong>Design note</strong>: starting weeks on Monday or Sunday changes where &quot;the weekend&quot; appears. Pick one convention and state it in the caption.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-3-h1","text":"Layout algorithm","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-5-3-h2","text":"The clever month-divider test","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Arrange a whole year as \"week = column, weekday = row\" to show cycles and anomalies at once. Layout algorithm For each date, compute its week-of-year and weekday; x = week index, y = weekday, color = value; draw dividers between months; they make a 7×53 grid readable; use a sequential colormap (e.g. Viridis), never a rainbow. JavaScriptCopy // week index and weekday, with Monday as the first day const week = d3.timeWeek.count(d3.timeYear(date), date); const weekday = (date.getDay() + 6) % 7; // Monday=0 … Sunday=6 const x = d3.scaleLinear().domain([0, 53]).range([0, width]); const y = d3.scaleBand().domain(d3.range(7)).range([0, height]); The clever month-divider test Do not draw lines on \"the 1st of each month\"; compare the current cell with the previous one: JavaScriptCopy const isMonthDivider = (d, i) => i > 0 && d.getMonth() !== data[i - 1].getMonth(); This places the divider on the exact cell where the month changes, regardless of the starting weekday or month length. Design note: starting weeks on Monday or Sunday changes where \"the weekend\" appears. Pick one convention and state it in the caption.","chars":945}},"5.4":{"id":"5.4","num":"5.4","chapter":"ch5","demo":"spiral","minutes":8,"related":["5.1","5.3"],"zh":{"title":"周期时间可视化","rawTitle":"周期时间可视化（阿基米德螺旋）","short":"周期时间","subtitle":"阿基米德螺旋：r = a + bθ，每转一圈就是一个周期。","bigIdea":"折线看趋势，螺旋看周期；相同相位排在同一条射线上。","points":["螺旋 = 圆 + 持续展开，适合年/季节/周循环。","Δθ 动态调整角宽，让每格弧长近似相等。","不适合精确读数与稀疏事件。"],"quiz":{"q":"螺旋图最适合回答哪类问题？","options":["某个点的精确数值是多少","每年同一季节是否呈现相同节律","两个类别的占比谁更大"],"answer":1,"why":"螺旋把相同相位对齐，擅长呈现周期性节律；精确读数应回到折线/表格，占比应使用条形或饼图。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>把时间沿圆周排列：每转一圈 = 一个周期。螺旋 = 圆 + 持续展开。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--why\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--why\">追问</span><span class=\"blk__text\">为什么用螺旋</span></h3>\n<p>折线擅长&quot;趋势&quot;，不擅长&quot;周期&quot;——同一季节的两年数据在折线上隔得很远。螺旋把相同相位排在同一条射线上，季节规律立刻显形。</p>\n<p>阿基米德螺旋：<code>r = a + bθ</code>，每转一圈半径增加常量 <code>b</code>，等速展开。</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const theta = (dayOfYear / 365) * Math.PI * 2;\nconst turn = yearIndex;                    // 第几年\nconst r = r0 + turn * gap;                 // 每圈外扩 gap\nconst x = cx + r * Math.cos(theta);\nconst y = cy + r * Math.sin(theta);</code></pre>\n</div><p>原文档还有一个精妙处理：用 <code>Δθ = boxSize / √(b² + r²)</code> 动态调整每格的角宽，让每个日期扇环的<strong>弧长</strong>近似相等，避免外圈格子被拉长。</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-5-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">适用与取舍</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>适合</th>\n<th>不适合</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>年/季节/周的循环规律</td>\n<td>没有周期、或周期很长</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>多年同一相位的对比</td>\n<td>需要精确读取单点数值</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>呈现&quot;节律&quot;而非&quot;趋势&quot;</td>\n<td>事件稀疏、时间间隔不均</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-4-h1","text":"为什么用螺旋","kind":"why"},{"id":"s-5-4-h2","text":"适用与取舍","kind":"plain"}],"text":"把时间沿圆周排列：每转一圈 = 一个周期。螺旋 = 圆 + 持续展开。 追问为什么用螺旋 折线擅长\"趋势\"，不擅长\"周期\"——同一季节的两年数据在折线上隔得很远。螺旋把相同相位排在同一条射线上，季节规律立刻显形。 阿基米德螺旋：r = a + bθ，每转一圈半径增加常量 b，等速展开。 JavaScript复制 const theta = (dayOfYear / 365) * Math.PI * 2; const turn = yearIndex; // 第几年 const r = r0 + turn * gap; // 每圈外扩 gap const x = cx + r * Math.cos(theta); const y = cy + r * Math.sin(theta); 原文档还有一个精妙处理：用 Δθ = boxSize / √(b² + r²) 动态调整每格的角宽，让每个日期扇环的弧长近似相等，避免外圈格子被拉长。 适用与取舍 适合 不适合 年/季节/周的循环规律 没有周期、或周期很长 多年同一相位的对比 需要精确读取单点数值 呈现\"节律\"而非\"趋势\" 事件稀疏、时间间隔不均","chars":427},"en":{"title":"Cyclic Time Visualization","rawTitle":"Cyclic Time Visualization (Archimedean Spiral)","short":"Cyclic Time","subtitle":"The Archimedean spiral: r = a + bθ; one turn is one cycle.","bigIdea":"A line shows trend; a spiral shows cycle by putting the same phase on the same ray.","points":["A spiral is a circle that unfolds, good for annual/seasonal/weekly cycles.","Dynamic Δθ keeps each cell's arc length roughly equal.","Not for precise readings or sparse events."],"quiz":{"q":"What question is a spiral chart best at answering?","options":["What is the exact value at one point?","Does the same season show the same rhythm each year?","Which of two categories has a larger share?"],"answer":1,"why":"A spiral aligns the same phase and reveals cyclic rhythm. Precise readings belong to lines/tables; shares belong to bars or pies."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Arrange time around a circle: one loop = one cycle. A spiral is a circle that keeps unfolding.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-4-h1\" class=\"blk blk--why\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--why\">Why</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Why a spiral</span></h3>\n<p>A line chart shows trends but hides cycles: the same season in two years sits far apart. A spiral puts the same phase on the same ray, making seasonal rhythms visible.</p>\n<p>Archimedean spiral: <code>r = a + bθ</code>; each turn adds a constant <code>b</code> to the radius.</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const theta = (dayOfYear / 365) * Math.PI * 2;\nconst turn = yearIndex;                    // which year\nconst r = r0 + turn * gap;                 // expand by gap per turn\nconst x = cx + r * Math.cos(theta);\nconst y = cy + r * Math.sin(theta);</code></pre>\n</div><p>The original notes a neat detail: <code>Δθ = boxSize / √(b² + r²)</code> adjusts each cell&#39;s angular width so every date cell has roughly the same <strong>arc length</strong>, preventing outer cells from stretching.</p>\n<h3 id=\"s-5-4-h2\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">When to use it</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr>\n<th>Good for</th>\n<th>Not good for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead><tbody><tr>\n<td>annual / seasonal / weekly cycles</td>\n<td>no cycle, or a very long cycle</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>comparing the same phase across years</td>\n<td>precise single-value readings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>showing rhythm rather than trend</td>\n<td>sparse, irregular events</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-4-h1","text":"Why a spiral","kind":"why"},{"id":"s-5-4-h2","text":"When to use it","kind":"plain"}],"text":"Arrange time around a circle: one loop = one cycle. A spiral is a circle that keeps unfolding. WhyWhy a spiral A line chart shows trends but hides cycles: the same season in two years sits far apart. A spiral puts the same phase on the same ray, making seasonal rhythms visible. Archimedean spiral: r = a + bθ; each turn adds a constant b to the radius. JavaScriptCopy const theta = (dayOfYear / 365) * Math.PI * 2; const turn = yearIndex; // which year const r = r0 + turn * gap; // expand by gap per turn const x = cx + r * Math.cos(theta); const y = cy + r * Math.sin(theta); The original notes a neat detail: Δθ = boxSize / √(b² + r²) adjusts each cell&#39;s angular width so every date cell has roughly the same arc length, preventing outer cells from stretching. When to use it Good for Not good for annual / seasonal / weekly cycles no cycle, or a very long cycle comparing the same phase across years precise single-value readings showing rhythm rather than trend sparse, irregular events","chars":809}},"5.5":{"id":"5.5","num":"5.5","chapter":"ch5","demo":"storyline","minutes":9,"related":["5.2","4.3"],"zh":{"title":"Storyline 时间线","rawTitle":"Storyline 时间线（侏罗纪公园）","short":"Storyline","subtitle":"多角色叙事：生命线的聚散表达关系变化，事件层标注关键转折。","bigIdea":"Storyline 的重点不是精确读数，而是「关系如何随时间变化」。","points":["x 轴严格按时间比例映射。","Catmull-Rom α=0.5 让线自然流动而不过度弯曲。","事件层用半透明圆标注冲突与转折。"],"quiz":{"q":"Storyline 中两条生命线靠拢，通常表示？","options":["两个角色分离","两个角色相遇或发生冲突","时间轴压缩"],"answer":1,"why":"线的距离编码关系强度：靠拢表示相遇、合作或冲突，分开表示分离。"},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>多角色叙事：每条线 = 一个角色 / 组织 / 进程；线的聚散 = 关系的变化。</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-5-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">三大元素</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>时间尺度映射</strong>：电影时长 → SVG 宽度，x 轴严格按比例对齐；</li>\n<li><strong>生命线</strong>：<code>curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5)</code> 的样条，线的靠拢表示相遇/冲突，分开表示分离；</li>\n<li><strong>事件层</strong>：半透明圆 + 文字，标注关键转折点。</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>复制</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const line = d3.line()\n  .x(d =&gt; x(d.time))\n  .y(d =&gt; y(d.y))\n  .curve(d3.curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5));\n\ng.selectAll(&quot;.character&quot;).data(characters).join(&quot;path&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;d&quot;, d =&gt; line(d.points))\n  .attr(&quot;stroke&quot;, d =&gt; d.color)\n  .attr(&quot;fill&quot;, &quot;none&quot;);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-5-5-h2\" class=\"blk blk--why\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--why\">追问</span><span class=\"blk__text\">为什么用 Catmull-Rom 而不是 monotoneX</span></h3>\n<p><code>monotoneX</code> 保证不过度弯曲，但会让线&quot;太直&quot;，失去叙事的&quot;河流感&quot;。Catmull-Rom 的张力系数 <code>0.5</code> 是经验值：既能自然流动，又不会在控制点之间震荡。</p>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>应用场景</strong>：电影分析、案件多人时间线、体育比赛互动、项目任务交接。Storyline 的重点不是&quot;精确读数&quot;，而是&quot;关系如何随时间变化&quot;。</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-5-h1","text":"三大元素","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-5-5-h2","text":"为什么用 Catmull-Rom 而不是 monotoneX","kind":"why"}],"text":"多角色叙事：每条线 = 一个角色 / 组织 / 进程；线的聚散 = 关系的变化。 三大元素 时间尺度映射：电影时长 → SVG 宽度，x 轴严格按比例对齐； 生命线：curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5) 的样条，线的靠拢表示相遇/冲突，分开表示分离； 事件层：半透明圆 + 文字，标注关键转折点。 JavaScript复制 const line = d3.line() .x(d => x(d.time)) .y(d => y(d.y)) .curve(d3.curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5)); g.selectAll(\".character\").data(characters).join(\"path\") .attr(\"d\", d => line(d.points)) .attr(\"stroke\", d => d.color) .attr(\"fill\", \"none\"); 追问为什么用 Catmull-Rom 而不是 monotoneX monotoneX 保证不过度弯曲，但会让线\"太直\"，失去叙事的\"河流感\"。Catmull-Rom 的张力系数 0.5 是经验值：既能自然流动，又不会在控制点之间震荡。 应用场景：电影分析、案件多人时间线、体育比赛互动、项目任务交接。Storyline 的重点不是\"精确读数\"，而是\"关系如何随时间变化\"。","chars":541},"en":{"title":"Storyline Timeline","rawTitle":"Storyline Timeline (Jurassic Park)","short":"Storyline","subtitle":"Multi-actor narrative: lifelines converge and diverge to show relationships; events mark turning points.","bigIdea":"Storyline is about how relationships change over time, not about precise readings.","points":["The x axis is strictly proportional to time.","Catmull-Rom α=0.5 flows naturally without overshooting.","An event layer of translucent circles marks conflicts and turns."],"quiz":{"q":"In a Storyline, two lifelines moving closer usually means:","options":["the characters separate","they meet or conflict","the time axis is compressed"],"answer":1,"why":"Distance encodes relationship strength: convergence means meeting, cooperation, or conflict; divergence means separation."},"html":"<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p>Multi-actor narrative: each line = a character / organization / process; convergence and divergence express changing relationships.</p>\n</blockquote><h3 id=\"s-5-5-h1\" class=\"blk blk--plain\"><span class=\"blk__text\">Three elements</span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Time-scale mapping</strong>: film duration → SVG width, with the x axis strictly proportional;</li>\n<li><strong>Lifelines</strong>: <code>curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5)</code> splines; lines converge for encounters/conflicts and separate for distance;</li>\n<li><strong>Event layer</strong>: translucent circles plus labels for key turning points.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codeblock\" data-lang=\"js\">\n<div class=\"codeblock__bar\"><span class=\"codeblock__lang\">JavaScript</span><button class=\"codeblock__copy\" type=\"button\" data-copy>Copy</button></div>\n<pre class=\"codeblock__pre\"><code class=\"language-js\">const line = d3.line()\n  .x(d =&gt; d.time)\n  .y(d =&gt; d.y)\n  .curve(d3.curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5));\n\ng.selectAll(&quot;.character&quot;).data(characters).join(&quot;path&quot;)\n  .attr(&quot;d&quot;, d =&gt; line(d.points))\n  .attr(&quot;stroke&quot;, d =&gt; d.color)\n  .attr(&quot;fill&quot;, &quot;none&quot;);</code></pre>\n</div><h3 id=\"s-5-5-h2\" class=\"blk blk--why\"><span class=\"blk__badge blk__badge--why\">Why</span><span class=\"blk__text\">Why Catmull-Rom instead of monotoneX</span></h3>\n<p><code>monotoneX</code> avoids overshoot but makes the lines too straight, losing the &quot;river-like&quot; narrative flow. A Catmull-Rom tension of <code>0.5</code> is the empirical sweet spot: it flows naturally without oscillating between control points.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"callout callout--note\"><p><strong>Applications</strong>: film analysis, multi-person case timelines, sports interactions, project handoffs. Storyline is about how relationships change over time, not about exact readings.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"id":"s-5-5-h1","text":"Three elements","kind":"plain"},{"id":"s-5-5-h2","text":"Why Catmull-Rom instead of monotoneX","kind":"why"}],"text":"Multi-actor narrative: each line = a character / organization / process; convergence and divergence express changing relationships. Three elements Time-scale mapping: film duration → SVG width, with the x axis strictly proportional; Lifelines: curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5) splines; lines converge for encounters/conflicts and separate for distance; Event layer: translucent circles plus labels for key turning points. JavaScriptCopy const line = d3.line() .x(d => d.time) .y(d => d.y) .curve(d3.curveCatmullRom.alpha(0.5)); g.selectAll(\".character\").data(characters).join(\"path\") .attr(\"d\", d => line(d.points)) .attr(\"stroke\", d => d.color) .attr(\"fill\", \"none\"); WhyWhy Catmull-Rom instead of monotoneX monotoneX avoids overshoot but makes the lines too straight, losing the \"river-like\" narrative flow. A Catmull-Rom tension of 0.5 is the empirical sweet spot: it flows naturally without oscillating between control points. Applications: film analysis, multi-person case timelines, sports interactions, project handoffs. Storyline is about how relationships change over time, not about exact readings.","chars":968}}},"stats":{"chapters":5,"sections":27,"widgets":20,"codeBlocks":90,"tables":54,"charsZh":23189,"charsEn":41055,"minutes":236}};
